{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary","id":77869,"title":"Changeling 20th Anniversary","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-23T16:34:07-08:00","id":77869,"title":"Changeling 20th Anniversary","content":"Should the Changeling 20th Anniversary edition ever become a reality, do you think we would see the production of a Kithbook: Boggans, in much the same way we saw the finishing of the series of Mage's Technocratic Convention books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T17:27:14-08:00","id":77906,"title":"","content":"I can see it being offered as a stretch goal like Tribebook: White Howlers was for W20.<br /> But remember, there were two other vaporware Changeling Books. Plus there was a German Changeling book that's really hard to find. I hope that the company behind that book puts it up on DrivethruRPG some day or if there ever will be a translation of it or WOD: France (Which has a Changeling chapter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T06:35:49-08:00","id":78279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FWXoCXMo_IM\" data-code=\"FWXoCXMo_IM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/FWXoCXMo_IM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Yep, I <i>really</i> want a Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm torn on Kithbook: Boggans. On the one hand, it would be nice to have an official book. On the other other hand, back when it seemed like Changeling: The Dreaming would never in a million years have any chance of coming back, the fan community at the time pulled together and created a fantastic fan version of the book Thad's writing is just as good, or better than, most of the published Kithbooks. A lot of great artists, including Melissa Uran, pitched in art. I tried to do the layout so that it would look indistinguishable from the other Kithbooks. It would be nice if all that effort could be acknowledged in some way. If you're interested in it, there's a link to the book in my sig.<br /> <br /> As for Book of Glamour, I'd love to see it if it could be released now. Otherwise, we're getting very close to Dreaming's 20th Anniversary. It was intended to be a mostly rules book to update Changeling's magic system to revised standards without the expense of actually released a revised core book for the game. If there's going to be a C20 and Book of Glamour could only be released close to it, I'd kind of rather they just put the effort into updating the rules to revised standards and roll any extras into C20 itself.<br /> <br /> I'd rather see the stretch goals used for new things that might not have any chance of happening otherwise - a Book of Nod style book for Changeling, updating the cantrip card rules to C20, print on demand cantrip cards, something that really delves into the Changeling Way ritual and covers the difference between changelings and arcadian fae, and a book on how things transitioned from DA: Fae to C:tD and maybe show how some of the things that weren't mentioned in DA: Fae work in the Dark Ages: the noble houses, the Tuatha, the Fomorians, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T08:10:39-08:00","id":78313,"title":"","content":"I would love to see a C20 Edition!<br /> <br /> Occasionally Changeling is a greatly underestimated game. Some people just do not capture the essence of the game, it's about telling a story where dreams are dying in the midst of a world that has lost its creativity.<br /> <br /> However, the strongest point in Changeling, in my POV, was the metaplot. The game has always had solid NPCs and very exciting events. (I have always been and will always be a fan of using the metaplot, so sue me).<br /> <br /> Since V20, W20 (and most probably M20) will not use the metaplot tool, how C20 should deal with? High King David is dead? The Winter already come? Faerilyth, Morwen and Lenora still playing politics each others? What about the mastermind, King Meilge? The Armies of Dreaming were able to construct a faction and its own realm? Who the Red Branch Knights will support, or they will splat and divide? What about the Guardians of the Silver Dragon?<br /> <br /> Or maybe we receive a toolbox to build our own kingdoms and counties, not only in USA but throughout the world. I wouldn't like that, but it could be a good option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2299-kalindush","name":"Kalindush","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2299_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T09:24:22-08:00","id":78346,"title":"","content":"High King David: Not sure, but there was a hostile takeover by David Bowie.<br /> Winter is coming: In Westeros.<br /> Politics: Knowing how Vampire players play more than likely.<br /> Meilige: Reappeared as Captain Picard.<br /> Red Branch Knights: Split between The Authority and Dixieland.<br /> Guardians of the Silver Dragon: Going to sue the Guardians of the Galaxy.<br /> <br /> I am kinda curious considering most of what I heard is pretty much a playdate instead of dread and horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":1442,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","user":"PaladinDemo","date":".  Spelling correction. 02-24-2014, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T09:35:00-08:00","id":78364,"title":"","content":"Changeling: The Dreaming is not &quot;dread and horror&quot; like the other games in cWoD. It doesn't need to be about &quot;monster who feels depression because they now need to suck blood/save Gaia/run away from Arcadian Creepy True Fae&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's about a world who lost its sparks of magnamity e ingenuity, people who had sold their minds to Banality. A world when no one is capable of Dreaming or Creativity is much more dreadly than Ancient Monsters Who Walks Since Ancient Times And No One Can Stop It Because They Will Rape Us All.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2299-kalindush","name":"Kalindush","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2299_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T09:47:24-08:00","id":78387,"title":"","content":"How do the other supernaturals interact with Changelings per CtD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T10:16:38-08:00","id":78405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=78346#post78346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">most of what I heard is pretty much a playdate</div> </div> </div> </div>You heard wrong. This sort of thing gets old, fast.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T11:46:31-08:00","id":78474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=78405#post78405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You heard wrong. This sort of thing gets old, fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that it gets old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T13:03:34-08:00","id":78529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=78474#post78474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that it gets old.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect he meant your comment. :P<br /> <br /> It's much like the teethclench Masquerade fans have at people saying &quot;but it's vampire superheroes with katanas in trenchcoats&quot;. :P<br /> <br /> Changeling is a solid WoD game but it's one that's a little stranger to wrap your head around than the others (thinking Sandman helps a bit). It also never got the revisions the other settings did so it's a little rougher around the edges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=78387#post78387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the other supernaturals interact with Changelings per CtD?</div> </div> </div> </div>It varies. Kindred are nearly all awful for Changelings - most of them are unchanging and cold/calculating. They're basically the embodiment of Banality (which shreds Lings).<br /> <br /> Werewolves have a tribe (the Fianna) which heavily features them (as an Irishman, it's about the only good thing about the tribe of drunken Oirish stereotypes :P ) and have some totems that require them to render aid to the Fae when asked. They integrate quite well into Werewolf as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T14:09:06-08:00","id":78576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=78387#post78387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the other supernaturals interact with Changelings per CtD?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing how both you and me are both Werewolf fans at heart and I own Changeling books:<br /> Black Furies = Female Satyrs at most, I can only imagine what would happen to a male Satyr in their midst. And other female fae.<br /> Bone Gnawers = These guys probably run into Sluaghs and Boggans at most.<br /> Children of Gaia = Any, as long as they aren't Wyrm tainted.<br /> Fianna = Get along with pretty much any fae, unless said fae is Wyrm tainted. It's only House Daireann that really dislikes the Fianna. Whereas House Fionna has a Fianna working with their knights.<br /> Glass Walkers = Knockers and House Dougal.<br /> Get of Fenris = Trolls only. Have sworn a blood oath against the Sidhe and the oath still stands today.<br /> Red Talons = Probably only a Ragabash Red Talon might tolerate a Pooka, but as a whole, wouldn't mind a Redcap as long as said Redcap was directed towards where humans are.<br /> Shadow Lords = House Eiluned.<br /> Silent Striders = Eshu.<br /> Silver Fangs = Seelie Sidhe and maybe House Varich.<br /> Stargazers = Hsien.<br /> Uktena = Nunnehi, Menehune, other native fae for the areas they frequent.<br /> Wendigo = Nunnehi<br /> Black Spiral Dancers = Them and House Balor go together like peanut butter and jelly. As well as the Shadow Court.<br /> Changing Breeds = Depends on the area. African/Ahadi = Eshu, Hengeyokai = Hsien, South America = ?, Australia = ?, Europe = Changelings, North America = Nunnehi, Menehune (Hawaii), Changelings.<br /> <br /> Actually, talking about Changing Breeds and Fae relations, I would like to know about areas in the world that were never covered in Changeling and what the native fae are there are like.<br /> <br /> For Hunter, there's the book Urban Legends which talks about fae there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T15:34:05-08:00","id":78709,"title":"","content":"I hope they make it darker and more fitting to the rest of the World of Darkness. My biggest problem with Changeling was always that it was far too easy to run away from your problems. My group created a Revised Changeling update that fixed this problem rather handily by having the Dreaming be completely besieged and surrounded by the Nightmare realms so that every time you wanted to go into the Dreaming you had to cross the siege lines. This made Changelings really think twice before they wanted to run away to the land of make believe, and thus they actually had to deal with their problems. I hope they do something about that, even if it's nothing like my solution was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T21:03:18-08:00","id":79082,"title":"","content":"I was flipping through Get of Fenris Revised, and couldn't find anything about the anti-fae blood oath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T03:39:48-08:00","id":79235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obyrne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=78529#post78529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It varies. Kindred are nearly all awful for Changelings - most of them are unchanging and cold/calculating. They're basically the embodiment of Banality (which shreds Lings).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know anything about Changeling, being a vampire guy, but it's hard for me to square a supernatural existence with the concept of banality. I understand what you mean by vampires being unchanging, but the older a vampire gets the more powerful their disciplines, the more blood magic they learn, the more crazy occult shit they see...their world view and understanding of what's possible should be much more expansive than a mortal man's.<br /> <br /> I mean, the embrace all by itself should break down a lot of mental barriers. If vampires are real and I'm one of them, then anything is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 02-25-2014, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T06:48:13-08:00","id":79298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=79235#post79235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know anything about Changeling, being a vampire guy, but it's hard for me to square a supernatural existence with the concept of banality. I understand what you mean by vampires being unchanging, but the older a vampire gets the more powerful their disciplines, the more blood magic they learn, the more crazy occult shit they see...their world view and understanding of what's possible should be much more expansive than a mortal man's.<br /> <br /> I mean, the embrace all by itself should break down a lot of mental barriers. If vampires are real and I'm one of them, then anything is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. It's the WW take on it (or at least the version talked about in the Larp books). I think it's that they're not really imaginative creatures - blood magic/disciplines/occult knowledge are all hard reality things. Things that are objectively true. Even looking at Thaum compared to mortal magic, it's more rigid and less imaginative - they've boiled the creativeness out of Awakened magic, nailed what they know about into paths and made it powered by blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T06:55:19-08:00","id":79300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obyrne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=78529#post78529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's much like the teethclench Masquerade fans have at people saying &quot;but it's vampire superheroes with katanas in trenchcoats&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, for some reason Changeling in particular seems to bring out those sort of clueless, derisive comments. It feels like there's at least one just about every time Changeling comes up. I usually try to be patient, but having been into the game since the 90's, I'm beyond sick of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest problem with Changeling was always that it was far too easy to run away from your problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe point of Dreaming is that your character walks a razor's edge between the mundane and the fantastic. If you stray too close to the mundane, you fall to banality. If you spend too much time with the fantastic, you become overcome with bedlam. No one can keep up that balancing act forever. The fate of every Changeling is to either forget their whole existence - their hopes, dreams, and everything they hold dear or be consumed by absolute madness. Spending too much time in the Dreaming running away from their problems is well past the first steps on their way to bedlam.<br /> <br /> Changeling does have its issues. The levels of the various Arts could use some tweaking, and the Realms are a complete mess. I love the flexibility of Changeling's noun + verb magic though. I don't want to get rid of it, just fix it. Banality needs a clear and consistent definition. Currently, what constitutes Banality changes every time the author does. It also needs hard rules for gaining it. As it is now, it feels like an arbitrary punishment from the ST. I'd like to see it have the mechanical rigor of Vampire's Humanity, Mummy's Balance, or Demon's Torment. With the rules as written, the glamour economy is unsustainable for even a single game session. Changelings are lucky if they can manage to gain even a single point of glamour per month. Meanwhile, just about every non-mundane action they can take requires a glamour expenditure. The rates glamour is gained and lost needs to be brought closer to parity - either glamour needs to be easier to obtain or it needs to be spent less often. I'd like to see some combination of both. I'd also like to see the artwork be a bit more consistent with the tone of the text. The second edition core is either teddy bears and balloons or all ren faire all the time. The first edition did a much better job of conveying the juxtaposition of the fantastic with the mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T08:05:55-08:00","id":79326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=79300#post79300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, for some reason Changeling in particular seems to bring out those sort of clueless, derisive comments. It feels like there's at least one just about every time Changeling comes up. I usually try to be patient, but having been into the game since the 90's, I'm beyond sick of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf started its life being unfavorably compared to Captain Planet, and over twenty years later, it still happens. It also still gets associated with the ethnocultural blunders of first edition, so even if C20 does happen and fixes every issue that has cropped up, people will still act as though it doesn't exist and keep harping off of 1995-2004.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T08:42:46-08:00","id":79342,"title":"","content":"Saur Ops, I wish I could like your post more than once.<br /> <br /> Vampire and Werewolf certainly had (and have) people who deride them as supers with fangs and furry captain planet. They still managed to pull incredibly strong sales despite the haters. Changeling was always in a precarious position due to lower sales. The haters and trolls weren't just annoying. Everyone they swayed meant that Changeling was that much closer to being canceled, which eventually happened.<br /> <br /> Rich has said a few times that fan buzz is one of the determining factors for relaunching these old games. Now that there's a chance Changeling might find new life, I'd hate to see it get killed before it even begins because the clueless bad stereotypes out number the fans talking about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T12:42:01-08:00","id":79513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=79082#post79082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was flipping through Get of Fenris Revised, and couldn't find anything about the anti-fae blood oath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since nobody has answered your question yet, Saur: It wasn't in any of the Werewolf books. It was in Changeling books. Basically, Book of Lost Dreams and one or two more Changeling books that discuss crossovers always repeat that Get of Fenris blood oath when talking about different Garou tribes (When you see the reason fully explained, any Fenrir has a right to be beyond pissed off at that).<br /> <br /> <b>On bedlam</b>:<br /> As someone with autism, could there at least be a disclaimer note box next to it's rules or at least take autism out from the effects from bedlam? I like Changeling, but that was one thing I read in the corebooks that left me very, very angry and mad. I get it, Changeling was written when very little was known of autism and was portrayed very negatively in the media. But so much has changed, that needs to be updated.<br /> Two, if it is updated: People with autism shouldn't be portrayed as <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigo_children\" target=\"_blank\">Indigo children</a> either. Basically, if you have it: It doesn't make your chances of becoming a changeling or walking banality higher/lower or give you special unique powers. You should be on equal footing like any other normal human is in the WOD that either becomes one of the supernatural or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 02-25-2014, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T13:00:49-08:00","id":79537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>... [Big Brother] deleted lots of stuff about Banality and Glamour, most or all of which I agree with...</i></div> </div> </div> </div>My question is, do you have any suggestions? Everything I can think of, I immediately shoot down as just plain not being workable. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T13:54:33-08:00","id":79612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=79513#post79513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since nobody has answered your question yet, Saur: It wasn't in any of the Werewolf books. It was in Changeling books. Basically, Book of Lost Dreams and one or two more Changeling books that discuss crossovers always repeat that Get of Fenris blood oath when talking about different Garou tribes (When you see the reason fully explained, any Fenrir has a right to be beyond pissed off at that).</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes it even odder that the reaction of the narrator is &quot;Alfar? Don't know anything about them. Next, let's move on to some weird-ass humans with powers that just popped up with the Red Star...&quot; I suppose it could be The Mists, but one would imagine that something that important would stick with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T14:40:36-08:00","id":79653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=79612#post79612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes it even odder that the reaction of the narrator is &quot;Alfar? Don't know anything about them. Next, let's move on to some weird-ass humans with powers that just popped up with the Red Star...&quot; I suppose it could be The Mists, but one would imagine that something that important would stick with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling and Wraith stopped at Second Edition, while Vampire, Werewolf and Mage got Revised editions. I remember some Revised books being very anti-crossover in how they were written.<br /> <br /> Here we go, <b>Changeling Storytellers Guide</b>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Get of Fenris</b> (page 87)<br /> There are probably no other Prodigals who harbor such hatred for the Kithain, especially the sidhe... have a blood oath sworn to destroy any sidhe on sight... the Get find that it takes a lot of pooka pelts for a good cape... The reason behind the Get's hatred of the sidhe harkens from long before the Shattering. </div> </div> </div>A group of sidhe lost their horses and needed new mounts, they came across a troll talking with a Get about the craft of war, and they were amazed when the Get left and transformed into a wolf. So the group of sidhe decided these wolf men would make perfect mounts for snowy conditions if they were enscorcelled. They found out where this Get and his pack were and used a geasa on them to be faithful pets for one millennium. With the coming of the Shattering, the sidhe abandoned their pets, the descendants of other Get found them and the Get used as mounts told them of their thousand year bondage. Then the Get swore the blood oath, with only the Trolls and Nunnehi left out of the oath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 02-25-2014, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T15:42:43-08:00","id":79710,"title":"","content":"I'm not pointing out problems to convince anyone not to do this. I'm pointing out the problems in the hope that they get fixed if C20 does happen. Admittedly it is not my favorite sphere, and not the project I'm most anticipating, but it has some good aspects that I did really like. If the problems can be fixed, I'll embrace it wholeheartedly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T16:16:37-08:00","id":79727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=78709#post78709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they make it darker and more fitting to the rest of the World of Darkness. <b>My biggest problem with Changeling was always that it was far too easy to run away from your problems.</b> My group created a Revised Changeling update that fixed this problem rather handily by having the Dreaming be completely besieged and surrounded by the Nightmare realms so that every time you wanted to go into the Dreaming you had to cross the siege lines. This made Changelings really think twice before they wanted to run away to the land of make believe, and thus they actually had to deal with their problems. I hope they do something about that, even if it's nothing like my solution was.<br /> ----<br /> I'm not pointing out problems to convince anyone not to do this. I'm pointing out the problems in the hope that they get fixed if C20 does happen. Admittedly it is not my favorite sphere, and not the project I'm most anticipating, but it has some good aspects that I did really like. If the problems can be fixed, I'll embrace it wholeheartedly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting to note, the recent Nostalgia Critic video editorial delves into this a bit and what to do with it: <a href=\"http://thatguywiththeglasses.com/videolinks/thatguywiththeglasses/nostalgia-critic/42405-when-is-a-movie-just-a-movie\" target=\"_blank\">When is a Movie Just a Movie?</a><br /> Take the problems that the characters are running from in the real world and present it in some symbolic form in the Dreaming as well. Showing that they really can't run away from it in any shape or form and have to face it at some point. A Silent Hill 2, if you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T16:19:51-08:00","id":79731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point of Dreaming is that your character walks a razor's edge between the mundane and the fantastic. If you stray too close to the mundane, you fall to banality. If you spend too much time with the fantastic, you become overcome with bedlam. No one can keep up that balancing act forever. The fate of every Changeling is to either forget their whole existence - their hopes, dreams, and everything they hold dear or be consumed by absolute madness. Spending too much time in the Dreaming running away from their problems is well past the first steps on their way to bedlam. </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe main problem with this I think is that it isn't even. Bedlam is described as being bad, but every mechanic encourages it. You get more Galmour and less Banality and you just get better and more powerful. If they wanted to play the razor's edge, they should make you balance two sets of principles like is done with morals in Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom balancing your Orun (Connection to the ephemeral) and Aye (Connection to the material), or balance two different power sources like is done in Kindred of the East and other eastern supplements balancing out Yin and Yang chi. In order to make a razor's edge work you need two equally bad options or two equally good options. Right now it is like walking a razor where falling off one side leads to a horrible pit full of rusty razorblades and used hypodermic needles and the other side is a comfortable down mattress. I know which side I'm leaning towards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T18:11:07-08:00","id":79799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=79653#post79653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changeling and Wraith stopped at Second Edition, while Vampire, Werewolf and Mage got Revised editions. I remember some Revised books being very anti-crossover in how they were written.<br /> <br /> Here we go, <b>Changeling Storytellers Guide</b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> A group of sidhe lost their horses and needed new mounts, they came across a troll talking with a Get about the craft of war, and they were amazed when the Get left and transformed into a wolf. So the group of sidhe decided these wolf men would make perfect mounts for snowy conditions if they were enscorcelled. They found out where this Get and his pack were and used a geasa on them to be faithful pets for one millennium. With the coming of the Shattering, the sidhe abandoned their pets, the descendants of other Get found them and the Get used as mounts told them of their thousand year bondage. Then the Get swore the blood oath, with only the Trolls and Nunnehi left out of the oath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, right. That. I vaguely remember having heard it back in the day. Must have repressed it for obvious reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T20:54:46-08:00","id":79921,"title":"","content":"Killersquirrel59, if you consider a loss of self as one descends into complete madness to be eventually consumed wholly by the Dreaming a fall onto a comfortable down mattress, we're going to have to agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> Big Brother, I have some thoughts for how I would address those issues, but they'll have to wait until I have more time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":".  Formatting 02-25-2014, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T22:38:43-08:00","id":80003,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the razor's edge that is described. I just think it needs to be reflected better in mechanics. There needs to be mechanical encouragement to walk the middle ground and not just jump into the mattress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T08:12:37-08:00","id":80236,"title":"","content":"I really don't know where you're getting the idea that the game encourages players to jump headlong into bedlam. I reread the section on bedlam to make sure I wasn't forgetting anything. There are no bonuses for descending into bedlam. The book gives a detailed list of bedlam warning signs. The three stages of bedlam are increasingly horrific and debilitating, and in the end, the character vanishes from earth, consumed entirely by the Dreaming never to be seen again. Changeling does have issues, but bedlam isn't really one of them.<br /> <br /> (Bedlam does have the unfortunate inclusion of autism as Laughing Hyena pointed out. It's the same sort of early White Wolf-ism that also gave us early Fianna, World of Darkness: Gypsies, and other unintentional bad stereotypes. I'd hope that if there's a C20, it won't be called autism.)<br /> <br /> Now, for Big Brother's question about how I would fix banality and the glamour economy....<br /> <br /> A solid definition of banality is seriously difficulty. So many writers over the years have had very different views on what banality is, and so many gaming groups have interpreted it in their own way. At this point, clearly defining banality is almost certainly going to contradict someone's chronicle. That being said, it really needs to happen anyway. I'd start with a great post from reddit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida grande\">Banality isn't about the division between science and magic, which the resurgence of the Dreaming at the time of the moon landing should show.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida grande\">Banality is the slow soul-deadening creep of conformity and the death of hope, the bleak granite wind that finally blows out the candle flame of childlike wonder. It is not the rise of glass and steel and circuit that chokes off the Dreaming, not the spread of pavement over grass that brings the ruin of Arcadia, but the 'rat race' of blind consumerism and the constant struggle against poverty. Every dreamer, every artist, every would-be bright spot in the bland nightmare of modern life who finally puts on a tie and goes to work in a cube is another drop of Fae blood spilled.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida grande\">If you don't think technology can be magical then you've never been to Disneyland, you've never seen Doc Brown's time machine, never watched Explorers or heard a young child declare they are going to be an astronaut with the kind of wide-eyed certainty reserved for playing at being Superman.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida grande\">If you want to hear what the struggle sounds like over the years, listen to this: </span></span><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zxazWMlxQLM\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zxazWMlxQLM</a><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:lucida grande\"> (Fair warning, it makes me cry 9/10 times.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida grande, tahoma, verdana, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">...The game isn't set up to be straight horror as much as it is a sort of appreciation of the last few flowers on a rose bush that is being slowly buldozed under. Thematically, the game is set up to be about the last days of a once-great empire of dreams and the fear every morning that this will be the day you are too tired to fight the coming winter any longer. You aren't meant to fear for your life, but for your hope.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>From there, I would look at retooling banality gain to follow a hierarchy of sins in similar way Vampire, Mummy, and Demon do. Instead of charting a descent into becoming a monster, this path would be the slow, inevitable death of hope and wonder. This would require a major reworking of the way Autumn Person and Dauntain powers work, but they're in desperate need of an overhaul anyway.<br /> <br /> For the glamour economy, I think I would keep musing (reverie and rapture) the long, personal process that it is now. It should be difficult, and it should be intimate. I would make the pay off much greater though to reflect the amount of effort put into it. I'd look at it resulting in either a permanent glamour or a reduction in banality. I would keep ravaging and rhapsody pretty much as they are. They're both a quick fix of glamour and extremely thematic. If banality was changed to a hierarchy of sins, they would both definitely be sins on the chart.<br /> <br /> I would add a method to gain glamour that is something like spontaneous inspiration. It would be a bit more difficult than ravaging, but not punishing and doable within a scene of a game session. The changeling would do something to inspire a mortal (individually or an audience). It could be a performance, a motivational speech, showing them how to do something or how something works - anything that could fit a musing threshold. It would produce a little bit of spontaneous glamour - one or two points, more if the target is one of the changeling's dreamers. It wouldn't be a victory against banality like musing is, but it's enough to keep the cold winds of winter at bay temporarily.<br /> <br /> To reduce the constant expenditure of glamour, I would default all cantrips to chimerical. If they want a cantrip to have a wyrd effect, then they spend a glamour point while they're casting it. Alternately, they could call upon the wyrd for a slightly increased cost, but then everything for the rest of the scene is wyrd without having to pay the cost per action.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T09:31:06-08:00","id":80294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really don't know where you're getting the idea that the game encourages players to jump headlong into bedlam. I reread the section on bedlam to make sure I wasn't forgetting anything. There are no bonuses for descending into bedlam. The book gives a detailed list of bedlam warning signs. The three stages of bedlam are increasingly horrific and debilitating, and in the end, the character vanishes from earth, consumed entirely by the Dreaming never to be seen again. Changeling does have issues, but bedlam isn't really one of them </div> </div> </div>It's not that there are bonuses for bedlam. It's that there are serious drawbacks to banality, and no drawbacks on the road to bedlam. Banality affects you constantly as a detriment and cautionary tale of falling back asleep. Bedlam doesn't have warning signs that hit you mechanically at all. You get higher Glamour and get more powerful. It's all better. Bedlam is something with no mechanical support. The ST can threaten it, but the threat is always arbitrary because there is no mechanical way to &quot;fall&quot; to bedlam other than ST fiat. Therefore it isn't really a threat. Therefore the razor's edge doesn't work.<br /> <br /> What is really needed is to redo the Permanent Glamor score to actually mirror Permanent Banality, independent of their temporary values. There need to be different advantages and penalties for getting either too high above the other and force the player to play the middle ground or go careening off into madness or slumber. Hell make the power of doing either look really damn tempting, but seriously risky. But there needs to be a mechanical enforcement of this balance. If you want to encourage a balancing act, both sides of the tightrope have to look equally dangerous, both in theme and in mechanics. Bedlam is not a risk, because right now there is no hard and fast way to get there that a player can point to on his sheet and worry about how close he's getting.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd run it like KOE Yin and Yang virtues. Make them opposed virtues that can't exceed a certain number (I'll say 10 for now for the sake of argument, but the number is arbitrary). Then you have different actions that can increase one or the other (personally I'd take xp out of the equation entirely and move this closer to a morality scale with a hierarchy of sins and virtues). Then you establish that if you gain a dot of Glamour that would take you above the allowed max, you lose a dot of Banality and come that one more step closer to Bedlam and vice versa. Say when either reaches 10, you're screwed, falling to either Slumber or Bedlam. That way you really have to balance your actions. The other side to this is make Banality not entirely bad. Make it feel familiar and comfortable. Have a higher Banality score give bonuses to dealing with the mundane in some form. Make it easy to just slip back off to sleep, because it's easier than fighting. <br /> <br /> With a system like this, Changeling really becomes about walking that delicate tightrope between being a Fae and being human, between creativity and dolor, with either side looking just as nasty. <br /> <br /> THAT would be a World of Darkness game. I may just go write this system up and try it out. Funny, I've never really been inspired to actually run Changeling, but this is a hack I could see making it actually work.<br /> <br /> On second thought, don't use Glamour for the opposed stat to Banality. Glamour is a spent resource and has its own mechanics that need to stay constant. Leave Glamour out of it. It needs a new stat, let's call it Inspiration (at least for now). You set up Inspiration vs. Banality, each with their own hierarchy of sins and virtues. Make the sins and virtues for one exactly diametrically opposed so that a sin for one is always a virtue for the other. When you commit an over act that would put them into conflict, roll your Inspiration vs. your Banality at an arbitrary but equal difficulty. The number of net successes gained is the number of temporary points gained in the victor's side. 10 temporary points equal a permanent point. When you make your character divide 10 points among your Inspiration and Banality depending on the kind of character you want to play (Seeming can still set a minimum Banality rating). When a new Permanent point is gained in either one, the other loses one. This makes it a vicious slope that once you start falling one way you are more likely to pick up speed, continuing to fall down the cliff until it's too late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T09:53:59-08:00","id":80312,"title":"","content":"Changeling: The Dreaming, 2nd edition pages 208-209.<br /> <br /> <b>Bedlam</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>First Threshold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Color Change: Everything changes color, either randomly or in patterns</li> <li>Whispers: The changeling &quot;hears&quot; telepathic or audible whispers that impart secrets or prophecies, or that spew unintelligible gibberish</li> <li>Dread: A feeling of complete and utter dread engulfs the changeling; shadows distort into monstrous shapes</li> <li>Lights: Bright lights flash in and out of existance, surrounding people with nimbi or other illuminations</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Threshold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Don Quixote Syndrome: The character believes everything to be from an ancient time or fantasy realm</li> <li>Delusions of Grandeur: The character sees everyone as an underling, fit only to serve him. No matter what utter nonsense he spouts, he expects others to laud his ideas and cater to his insane visions.</li> <li>Social Darwninism: The character sees everyone as either predator or prey - and herself as a predator of great strength and skill. This is an insidious form of madness, as it can remain undetected for some time. Soon, however, the character will strike - and death will follow in her wake.</li> <li>The Walls Have Ears: The character believes that everything has a personality and is alive. Manifestations of this madness range from a changeling holding quite conversations with fence posts to uttering apologies every time he takes a step on the street.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Third Threshold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Berserker: The character attacks all around her with whatever weapons are nearby.</li> <li>Autism: The character withdraws into himself, not recognizing the outside world at all.</li> <li>Feral Cunning: The character reverts to an animalistic state; not a frenzied attacker like Berserker, but a cunning, predatory animal that doesn't communicate and seeks only to escape or kill.</li> <li>Perversity: The character descends into the depths of her psyche and performs inhuman acts barely conceivable by even the most depraved soul.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Note</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If left untreated, Bedlam completely overtakes a character. She loses all free will and passes into the world of dreams. One night, while the changeling dreams, she simply ceases to be, disappearing entirely from the face of the Earth. At this point (or perhaps sooner), the player may no longer run the character and must create a new one if she wishes to continue play in the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see lots of warning signs, drawbacks, and debilitation here.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> On second read through of your post, I see what you're getting at. I'd be concerned that would take away from Changeling focus on Earth. Right now, the Dreaming is *hard* to get to. Trods are rare and to magic yourself into the Dreaming requires a level 3 Art and a level 5 Realm at minimum. Bedlam isn't as immediate of a threat, but it is there waiting if a changeling purposefully goes too far that direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 02-26-2014, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T10:20:00-08:00","id":80331,"title":"","content":"While I agree that there\u2019s much about Changeling that needs to be fixed, the hypothetical C20 should approach such changes within the existing structure as much as possible. Don\u2019t go introducing whole new stats (e.g., Inspiration) or replacing the Kiths with a build-your-own-form system (as tempting as that is). As much as possible, start by identifying how many of the perceived problems are matters of misunderstandings, and address as many of those as possible through clarifications of existing rules. The sorts of changes I\u2019d favor would be things like rewriting the Seelie and Unseelie Legacies so that they feel less like Virtues and Vices and more like two competing visions of virtue: while the fluff says that the Seelie and Unseelie Courts are both potentially good guys, the Legacy write-ups make it hard to picture Unseelie protagonists. <i>That\u2019s</i> the sort of thing I\u2019d like to see: leaving as much of the overall structure intact as possible, and overhauling the details within that structure as necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T12:29:31-08:00","id":80429,"title":"","content":"I'd like to think over your comments, Pooka. They're good. Yours too, KS and Data.<br /> <br /> I've always sorta pictured DtF as having a fairl workable system (albeit, far from perfect) for changelings... but then again, I view them as largely two sides of the same coin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T13:10:27-08:00","id":80449,"title":"","content":"Demon: The Fallen always stuck me as sort of a spiritual successor to Changeling: The Dreaming. While the themes of the two games are very different, the way things work in them is remarkably similar - an immortal soul merged with a mortal, a demon's relationship with its thralls and a changeling's relationship with its dreamers, and gaining faith and glamour seem to parallel each other. Demon seems to part ways with Changeling in how it handles torment, but I think there are some good lessons there for Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T14:45:48-08:00","id":80522,"title":"","content":"I can see your point in not changing too much for the 20th anniversary, though I still say that Changeling should need to change more than Vampire, Werewolf, or Mage to try to address what caused it to fail in the first place. I'll pack up that system and pocket it for one of my own future projects I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T14:48:04-08:00","id":80525,"title":"","content":"@PookaKnight<br /> <br /> It's not that Bedlam isn't bad. I don't know how much clearer I can say that. It's that how you get there has no basis in mechanics. The only way to get to bedlam is that the ST suddenly says &quot;Guess what, you're in bedlam now.&quot; This makes it arbitrary. When something is arbitrary, it isn't a threat. For something to represent a consequence, the player has to see a logical cause to the effect, notably a cause they can prevent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T16:48:55-08:00","id":80614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For something to represent a consequence, the player has to see a logical cause to the effect, notably a cause they can prevent.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warning Signs Checklist, p. 209</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Your Glamour is higher than both your Willpower and your Banality</li> <li>You spend more nights in freeholds than in the real world. (If you spend all of your time in freeholds, Bedlam is almost assured.)</li> <li>You have more than one faerie treasure.</li> <li>You interact with more than three chimera on a regular basis.</li> <li>You are a constant Ravager.</li> <li>You have no mortal friends.</li> <li>You have no mortal job (or other attachment, such as school).</li> <li>You are almost exclusively nocturnal.</li> <li>You drink alcohol or use drugs or have sex to excess.</li> <li>You spend more than half of your waking time creating art of some kind.</li> <li>You have no mortal family.</li> <li>You have no mortal possessions.</li> <li>You are in a state of unrequited love.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, if banality were as clear and consistent as bedlam, I don't think it would generate nearly as much controversy as it does. Now, I'll certainly agree that some of the warning signs could use changing, but they're definitely clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T17:14:14-08:00","id":80635,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'm getting my point across very well. I apologize for appearing to rehash the same thing. Let me try phrasing it a bit differently.<br /> <br /> Those warning signs appear to be clear. But to what degree? There's no system for it. There is no progression of penalties that leads to it. You can't accidentally fall to it in a dangerous situation or from a bad roll. The only way a character will ever hit bedlam is for the ST to arbitrarily say &quot;I think you've done too much, you're in bedlam now, hand me your sheet&quot;. As such, it will never be a real threat. <br /> <br /> Is that clearer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T17:56:46-08:00","id":80662,"title":"","content":"I do see what you're saying, I just think it's a non-issue. There are enough rules there considering this is one of the original five classic World of Darkness games. There are more rules for falling to bedlam in Changeling than there are for being overcome by harano in Werewolf or entering into quiet in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T23:50:35-08:00","id":80844,"title":"","content":"Difference being that Quiet can be triggered by botches or paradox and Harano can be triggered by draining gnosis. There is a way to have it happen in game without ST fiat.<br /> <br /> To illustrate this, has anyone here ever actually seen a Changeling fall to bedlam in one of their games? And I don't mean as an epilogue at the end or as a willing choice when someone was done with the character. Has it ever happened to anyone in the middle of a game as an unfortunate and unexpected character end? Because unless that can happen, it will never be a threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T06:10:23-08:00","id":80990,"title":"","content":"Quiet isn\u2019t triggered by a Paradox or a botch; it\u2019s triggered by the Storyteller deciding that it makes sense for Quiet to be triggered. Paradox is merely a warning sign. More generally: one person\u2019s \u201cit\u2019s triggered by Storyteller fiat\u201d is another person\u2019s \u201cit\u2019s a story-driven event\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T08:54:51-08:00","id":81077,"title":"","content":"Clearly I'm either not making my point or it is not being agreed with, I can't really tell which, but I think I've derailed this thread with my personal gripes long enough. I look forward to seeing what they do with C20 and hope it succeeds where the previous edition flopped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T14:27:37-08:00","id":81772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=79326#post79326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf started its life being unfavorably compared to Captain Planet, and over twenty years later, it still happens. It also still gets associated with the ethnocultural blunders of first edition, so even if C20 does happen and fixes every issue that has cropped up, people will still act as though it doesn't exist and keep harping off of 1995-2004.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind those people who will rail FOR the first edition blunders because it's 'in the books' XD<br /> <br /> (offtopic post is offtopic)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T01:51:03-08:00","id":84474,"title":"","content":"I'm all for C20. Changeling was a breath of fresh air to pointless grimdark and betrayal of Vampire. Not that politics didn't happen in Changeling, but Changelings lacked the Beast that made Vampires so... evil, for lack of a better word.<br /> <br /> I would like C20 to reconcile &quot;Changeling: The Dreaming&quot; and &quot;Dark Ages: Fae&quot; as far as theme, powers, etc. Lots of good ideas between those two books, they just need to be consolidated and perhaps polished up a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T11:05:48-08:00","id":84722,"title":"","content":"I'll start by copping to the fact that I am NOT a fan of <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>, but in light of that, I'd support the heck out of a <b>C20</b> offering. Here's why (kinda for both):<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b> does have darkness in it, but the CORE rules don't make it very obvious. There are scads of supplemental material that brings up a much wider level of possible diversity among these creatures, their domains, their histories. If <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b> had received a Revised Edition, I would'a expected more of that to have shown up in such a book. A 500+ page <b>C20</b> could encompass a lot of that, offering looks at the Unseelie, the Shadow Court, the Thallain, and more. After seeing how much more of a nuanced view we got from the 20th anniversary edition of <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b> versus what we got from <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b>'s 20th, I'd hope for a full view of this game.<br /> <br /> ...However, I think that a LOT of how a <b>C20</b> will look shall depend on how the 20th Anniversary of <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> will look. Last I heard, the decision whether the game would get something closer to a 'Revised-Plus' treatment around 200 pages or a full, 500+ page version was still a point of conversation at Onyx Path. My information may be off on this, so don't send for a solicitor if I'm wrong, but there's still a bit of time until it's going to be an issue. Regardless, I'd look forward to seeing such a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T10:44:27-08:00","id":86115,"title":"","content":"@Killersquirrel59<br /> Even if one would choose to ignore Bedlam altogether and travel to the Dreaming would be made easier I would still have to disagree about people running to the Dreaming to escape their problems. In general who in their right mind would try to escape problems into a land comprised of Dreams and Nightmares? What real world problem would be so great as to risk Dragons, giant spider's, Zombie outbreaks and what ever else people have dreams and nightmares about?<br /> Also despite Dreaming being just as dangerous as the Umbra it is actually, as mentioned earlier, harder to get to yet I have never heard of Werewolf being scolded about letting the protagonists escape their problems into the Umbra.<br /> Final reason for why it is a bad idea to escape your problems into the Dreaming is that you can barely remember what happened in there after you come back into the Autumn World as the Mists affect even Changelings there.<br /> All in all I really have trouble understanding your position on the Dreaming. It may, admittedly, just be some kind of misunderstanding here or just me being unable to see the forest for the trees as I'm standing in it but still I find claims of Dreaming being an escape hatch away from your problems to be rather absurd idea. To me it is if anything a source of more problems and naturally story hooks. Just like Umbra in WtA.<br /> <br /> In general I do hope that C20 does happen and I do hope that they do not remove the Kiths, Thallain, Adhene and the rest in favor of the custom system, although I wouldn't mind some sort of custom system existing in an appendix or in a C20 ST Companion type of book as an option for those who want such a system. Mostly I think the things that deserve to be changed are connected to the Glamour, Banality and Magic systems. Like mentioned by the Pooka earlier Glamour generation, and the size of the pool being limited by your Permanent Glamour, are way too meager compared to how much an average Changeling needs to be throwing Glamour around. One could without further problems drop Glamour Costs from Birthrights that have them as you already need to use Glamour to either call upon the Wyrd or to Enchant anyone not of the dreaming and amongst each other they are balanced enough. Just why does changing form Cost Glamour for a Pooka and is free for Shapechangers in general considering how limited, and generally, non combative Pooka changing is for example.<br /> <br /> So like mentioned Glamour costs and where they are needed should be reconsidered as well as the ways of regaining it. PookaKnight gave nice options and ideas already, few more and we'd be there. Also I would like to rip Glamour itself apart a bit dividing it into Bright, Seelie, Glamour and Dark, Unseelie, Glamour this would tie into both the magic system and the Courts but that's a discussion for another time. But speaking of the Magic system I kinda like PookaKnights idea about somewhat costlier Calling Upon the Wyrd which would last a scene and make all Cantrips Wyrd without extra costs. Also while I do like the idea behind the magic system, verb and a noun basically, I do think the way it's been implemented to be kinda awkward and clunky in a way that it really does unfortunately loose the Fae quality of it. I would prefer a somewhat more chaotic and wild magic system, I like the magic system of DA:Fae (and non-DA Mage's as well) but it is likely a bit powerful for a modern day changeling chronicle, besides here is where I would like to see a difference between Dreaming Glamour and Nightmare Glamour in action so to speak. Seelie and Unseelie Magic just should feel different to me despite being basically the same.<br /> <br /> For myself CtD has never lacked Darkness, which has been a complain of some, though admittedly the art in the 2nd ed Core hides it a bit from a casual observer but still some of my darkest themed games have involved Changelings as beings of Nightmare made flesh nothing quite compares to them in the darkness scale. In addition to the Darkness of Nightmares CtD has the death of imagination, invention, innocence and joy, whether coming from horrible or pleasant deeds and experiences,as it's core theme which is pretty damn dark to begin with.<br /> <br /> Sorry about the slight rambling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T02:09:38-08:00","id":86603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=80331#post80331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that there\u2019s much about Changeling that needs to be fixed, the hypothetical C20 should approach such changes within the existing structure as much as possible. Don\u2019t go introducing whole new stats (e.g., Inspiration) or replacing the Kiths with a build-your-own-form system (as tempting as that is). As much as possible, start by identifying how many of the perceived problems are matters of misunderstandings, and address as many of those as possible through clarifications of existing rules. The sorts of changes I\u2019d favor would be things like rewriting the Seelie and Unseelie Legacies so that they feel less like Virtues and Vices and more like two competing visions of virtue: while the fluff says that the Seelie and Unseelie Courts are both potentially good guys, the Legacy write-ups make it hard to picture Unseelie protagonists. <i>That\u2019s</i> the sort of thing I\u2019d like to see: leaving as much of the overall structure intact as possible, and overhauling the details within that structure as necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree here. I think Changeling was a great game but it got bogged down with lots of sub systems and a lack of direction in the dark aspect. I really hope this happens and I am super excited for Wraith. Wraith is just freaking awesome and deserves its 500+ pages of glory. Which means it will include a lot of stuff from the players guide and I am hoping things from The Risen.<br /> <br /> Anyway, back on topic. Go Changeling!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T06:26:35-08:00","id":86711,"title":"","content":"Hello all! Name is Iris, I am an AVID fan, player and collector of all the Classic WoD systems, my favorite being Changeling: The Dreaming. I have come to the site becuase of all of the work on the 20th anniversary editions of white wolf and hope to offer my thoughts on other potential creations (I have purchased Vampire Werewolf and Mage already. Changeling is my all time fav, outside of roleplaying I even brought it into my life (my dj handle was DJ Nocker even, haha). If a kickstarter were ever done for a Changeling 20th, I would easily put in at least $500 for my kickstart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2467-iris","name":"Iris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T21:17:45-07:00","id":140217,"title":"","content":"I am not a Changeling player and don't know much about the game, so I'm not invested emotionally in C20. But I do hope CB20 happens.<br /> <br /> 1. I hope that if it happens it mentions something about Fae/Changelings in the whole world, not just Western countries. I thought it was quite bad that East Asia somehow got Hsien instead. As though there are no Fae or Changelings, and no Dreaming, corresponding to that part of the world. It also doesn't make sense to me if Eshu are the only Fae/Changelings connected to all the dreams of the entire varied African continent. Long descriptions, rules, and splatbooks for umpteen different types of Fae/Changelings are unlikely, but at least some information on other continents outside Europe, North America, and Hawai`i would be nice.<br /> <br /> I'm also a little lost on why banality would be overtaking the whole world, just because science and rationality are in vogue in the West and some other Developed countries. There are still huge swaths of the globe where religion and &quot;superstition&quot; and belief in magic are very alive and strong, so wouldn't those regions have Fae who have no need to become Changelings? Or just boast open trods back to Arcadia? How can the world be sliding into Winter if only part of humanity has embraced a purely mundane, anti-supernatural, pure-science worldview?<br /> <br /> <i>Even better if 2nd edition already had that and I just didn't know it.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> 2. I also hope that Changelings get some kind of historical treatment: either some guidelines for how DA:Fae became C:tD, or if that can't be done coherently due to large differences, offer an (optional) DA:Changeling that can be connected to the present day.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3. What effect does the internet have on Changelings and Glamour? If the Moon Landing caused the Resurgence (AFAIK) then the internet could be really interesting for Changelings. Can they access the Digital Web, or is there a Dream Realm equivalent?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=79300#post79300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe point of Dreaming is that your character walks a razor's edge between the mundane and the fantastic. If you stray too close to the mundane, you fall to banality. If you spend too much time with the fantastic, you become overcome with bedlam. No one can keep up that balancing act forever. The fate of every Changeling is to either forget their whole existence - their hopes, dreams, and everything they hold dear or be consumed by absolute madness. Spending too much time in the Dreaming running away from their problems is well past the first steps on their way to bedlam.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something confusing to me. The description of Bedlam sounds like they lose touch with mundane reality, which is bad from a human perspective. But I thought that Changelings were exiles from Arcadia, essentially trapped on Earth, who want to get back to their homeworld. Wouldn't their goal be to transcend their half-human nature and become full Fae in the Dreaming once again? Or is the Dreaming completely separate from Arcadia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-17-2014, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T01:36:58-07:00","id":140338,"title":"","content":"Arcadia is closed and whir you must pass through the Deep Dreaming to reach it the Trods are essentially Gone, the Gates are Sealed and the threat s immense to even get so far as to glimpse the walls. Bedlam isn't some form of Ascension for Changelings it's a fading into dream stuff and as suh it's simply another disconnect that removes some magic and wonder from the mortal world and without Dreaming Mortals the Dreaming dies, if the Dreaming dies Aracadia will fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T04:43:42-07:00","id":140421,"title":"","content":"Originally posted by <b>Third Threshold</b><ul><li>Berserker: The character attacks all around her with whatever weapons are nearby.</li> <li>Autism: The character withdraws into himself, not recognizing the outside world at all.</li> <li>Feral Cunning: The character reverts to an animalistic state; not a frenzied attacker like Berserker, but a cunning, predatory animal that doesn't communicate and seeks only to escape or kill.</li> <li>Perversity: The character descends into the depths of her psyche and performs inhuman acts barely conceivable by even the most depraved soul.</li> </ul><br /> Okay, from reading the &quot;autism&quot; entry, I suspect that it would be better termed &quot;Catatonia,&quot; as the description is more classically a symptom of a catatonic state.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2980-steampunkadventurer","name":"SteampunkAdventurer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T09:34:41-07:00","id":140615,"title":"","content":"Yes, definitely. It's a total, gross misreading of what autism is.<br /> Didn't Changeling also have the horrible, extremely offensive idea that autistic people are automatically banality fountains and that having autism is worse than death?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T12:34:30-07:00","id":140821,"title":"","content":"I think you may be confusing that with &quot;Autumn People&quot; there Erinys who were founts of Banality and walking devastation of the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T01:54:04-07:00","id":142175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=78474#post78474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that it gets old.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially since it's always cast as if all the other WoD games are actually horror.<br /> <br /> Okay. Wraith is a horror game. Hunter <i>can be</i> a horror game. But the rest? Despite the sales pitch, the WoD games are far, far less &quot;horror&quot; than they are &quot;modern fantasy.&quot;. Mage and Changeling are totally open about this. werewolf is action fantasy. Vampire is social fantasy, which becomes very clear the tenth time you're at a con seeing a neckbearded baconsniffer play a 38-24-28 Toreador with Resources 5. I don't even <i>know</i> what the hell Demon and Mummy are supposed to be. One is a RPG version of a Linkin Park album, the other is Mummy.<br /> <br /> Anyone coming after Changeling for &quot;not being horror&quot; or something doesn't deserve a rebuttal about how you can pin horror themes in Changeling. They deserve a smack to the head and a reminder that werewolves have a totem from <i>The Dukes of Hazzard</i> and that Bela Lugosi is a Malkavian who lives in the Universal Studios basement. OOOOOOO HORROR","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T11:00:33-07:00","id":142502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=140615#post140615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, definitely. It's a total, gross misreading of what autism is.<br /> Didn't Changeling also have the horrible, extremely offensive idea that autistic people are automatically banality fountains and that having autism is worse than death?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it was 1995, it wasn't as if autism was a deeply-studied condition even in medicine at the time. It was pretty much assumed that autism = Rain Man. I'm not going to lay fault on a 20 year pld game for getting it wrong about a condition that has only really gotten a lot of study in the last ten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T13:20:48-07:00","id":142635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=142502#post142502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, it was 1995, it wasn't as if autism was a deeply-studied condition even in medicine at the time. It was pretty much assumed that autism = Rain Man. I'm not going to lay fault on a 20 year pld game for getting it wrong about a condition that has only really gotten a lot of study in the last ten.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was born in the early 80's and was misdiagnosed with childhood schizophrenia at the time, so I know it wasn't fully studied at the time. However, by the early 90's that started to change (<i>And I was re-diagnosed as being on the autism spectrum with Asperger's</i>). Granted, by that time, it wasn't fully known in Media/Culture circles either and thank fricking Sky Coyote for that. As once it became fully known in those circles, the whole huge stigma towards it developed and I was very glad I was out of Middle School by then. I can't even imagine what would happen if my tormentors at the time knew what I had.<br /> <br /> When I was a child, it was pretty extreme as I wouldn't talk to anyone outside my family. So most people at the time assumed I was mute or in my own little world. But once I hit around my teenage years, I completely changed. As I can now have social interactions with people. But that doesn't mean all my issues went away either.<br /> <br /> <u>That said, if most of the 20th editions are changing to keep up with how much has changed over the years as a reflection:</u> That is something to be changed from the two corebooks and not just copy-pasted from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T20:43:10-07:00","id":144057,"title":"","content":"I would greatly prefer DA:Fae brought into the modern age (mechanically and lore-wise) versus CtD being given a similar treatment as V20. CtD was too splat heavy and the kiths were too restrictive for designing Fae folk. DA:F was absolutely fantastic. In my own games I brought them into modern times and they work prettywell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T14:39:23-07:00","id":144867,"title":"","content":"DA:F is a fantastic game, yes. But so is C:tD, and like the other original cWoD lines, it deserves it's own 20th Anniversary polishing and not just being swept under the rug or being treated like the red-headed stepchild.<br /> <br /> I think the biggest complaint coming from Lost and DA players - the &quot;limitedness&quot; of the Kith - could be solved with rules/suggestion for creating kith beyond the basic 9 (or 10, if you count piskies - which I do.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/h38q1qmfx/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/67hc6e1i5/i_backed_ex3_small.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2045-melonlord82","name":"melonlord82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2045_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T20:13:02-07:00","id":145194,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure the limited nature of Kiths is my biggest complaint with CtD. It is my biggest complaint that isn't a matter of (a) rules that don't do what they were supposed to or (b) things that don't have support in the system.<br /> <br /> Fixing them without going full flexible is actually pretty easy: Take the current Birthrights and Frailties and turn them into defining traits that can be either a Birthright or a Frailty. So if you want a Pooka that cuts out the lying, you can have a Frailty based more on the animal parts. So you define each Kith with four &quot;themes&quot; and each has an attached Birthright and Frailty. Pick two Birthrights and two Frailties from your options. The Kiths are still pretty tight thematically, but you get away from such strong stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T20:34:34-07:00","id":145206,"title":"","content":"@Heavy: It's not mine either, but it does seem the biggest gripe from Lost/DA fans. I honestly don't see how it's any less restrictive then having to choose from Kindred Clans or Garou Tribes.<br /> <br /> So, one thing I'd like to throw in here as a suggestion, should the people who pick up the C20 project. There seemed to be hints dropped throughout some of the books that the Changeling Way tied the various fae to mortal <b>bloodlines</b>. Hence, <b>kinain</b>... mortals with fae blood that give them a touch of magic. At times this implied that fae souls reincarnate down family-lines. I think this is a good place to really help tether changelings to mortal concerns and the importance of family ties. Not only are <b>kinain </b>potential allies, but one never knows when down the line another fae soul will be born, possibly in need of rescuing from banal parents. I'd like to see that idea solidified and polished up. The Garou know the importance of <b>kin</b>; more-so should changelings need to feel a bond with and protect the precious magic they gifted to <b>bloodlines </b>centuries ago, and which now protects them from a world they are trapped in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/h38q1qmfx/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/67hc6e1i5/i_backed_ex3_small.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2045-melonlord82","name":"melonlord82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2045_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T02:28:52-07:00","id":145454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>melonlord82</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=145206#post145206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Heavy: It's not mine either, but it does seem the biggest gripe from Lost/DA fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone that gripes plenty about CtD, and vastly prefers Lost (I have issues with DA Fae and Mage that are somewhat separate), I do bring this gripe up a lot when it comes up. Part of the problem is that it is such an immediate impact on play. When you crack open the book and read and get lots of ideas of what you might want to play, but then get to the character creation part and find out that your Kith options are incredibly limited... it kind of stops you in your tracks. You don't even get into all the other issues the game has because most of those are ones that come up in play as you go.<br /> <br /> That is, barring the age old tone/art issues that are another big gripe about CtD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I honestly don't see how it's any less restrictive then having to choose from Kindred Clans or Garou Tribes. </div> </div> </div>The biggest issue is the way they're handled. The Frailties in particular are a big culprit here. A Clan, mechanically, is a set of powers you get cheaper and a weakness. The Clans have a very big spread of options there, and you have to work pretty hard to come up with a concept that really falls flat with any of them.<br /> <br /> Garou Tribes are an example of how a few variables can vastly increase your options. Tribe only defines a fraction of your character's mechanics. Auspice and Breed also have a large impact. As long as it fits the fluff of WtA... it is a really big stretch to come up with a concept that you can't slot into a Tribe/Auspice/Breed combo of some sort.<br /> <br /> The problem with CtD is you run into really basic concepts that get cut out very quickly. You want to play a wise Owl changeling? Not going to happen. If you go Pooka you have to accept all the trickster and lying stuff that you don't care about (and is contrary to being the wise sage font of knowledge). If you go something like Boggan or Slaugh, the Owl part is lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T04:51:17-07:00","id":145525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=145454#post145454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with CtD is you run into really basic concepts that get cut out very quickly. You want to play a wise Owl changeling? Not going to happen. If you go Pooka you have to accept all the trickster and lying stuff that you don't care about (and is contrary to being the wise sage font of knowledge). If you go something like Boggan or Slaugh, the Owl part is lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not, you can just say your Sluagh looks like an owl, with big eyes and feathers. Take the wings and oracle merit too.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think what sucks with the Kith spreads, is that they go far too deep into what each kith looks. My advise is just to disregard how -exactly- each kith should look and just by what you like. I've had a sluagh with wolf eyes, ears and fangs and no one has bat an eye about him.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T06:49:28-07:00","id":145630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>melonlord82</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=144867#post144867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DA:F is a fantastic game, yes. But so is C:tD, and like the other original cWoD lines, it deserves it's own 20th Anniversary polishing and not just being swept under the rug or being treated like the red-headed stepchild.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I'd love to see DA:Fae get updated along with V20: Dark Ages, but I don't want it at the expense of C20. Dreaming is such a fantastic, underrated game. It deserves a chance to really shine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the biggest complaint coming from Lost and DA players - the &quot;limitedness&quot; of the Kith - could be solved with rules/suggestion for creating kith beyond the basic 9 (or 10, if you count piskies - which I do.) </div> </div> </div>I can see the flexibility argument from DA: Fae, but I've never understood it from Lost. You still have to pick a kith with the same sort of restrictions as in Dreaming. The only difference I see is that the core book has a whole lot more kiths. Dreaming only presents 9 options in the core book, but one of the big complaints folks used to have about Dreaming was splat overload. Once you go past the core book, Dreaming has crazy amounts of splat options. Beyond the core 9 kiths, there are Piskies, Gillhe Dhu, Clurichauns, Selkies, and Merfolk. You have kith variations such as River Hags and Oba. Nearly all the kiths have a Thallain equivalent. You have all the Nunnehi and Menehune tribes. You have the 6 Inanimae kiths. You have the Adhene kiths. If you count the Hsien as part of Changeling: The Dreaming, that's 10 more splats.<br /> <br /> The only thing enforced mechanically about the kiths are their birthrights and frailties. Ana Mizuki is spot on, merits let you customize their appearance however you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T08:05:04-07:00","id":145669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=145454#post145454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with CtD is you run into really basic concepts that get cut out very quickly. You want to play a wise Owl changeling? Not going to happen. If you go Pooka you have to accept all the trickster and lying stuff that you don't care about (and is contrary to being the wise sage font of knowledge). If you go something like Boggan or Slaugh, the Owl part is lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wise Owl Changeling? Through Pooka you can easily be the Oracle who speaks in riddles, remember that Pookaese is quite a bit more than lying. Or instead of actual riddles just point people towards clues that point to the truths you see and know, which ends up only amplifying your air of wisdom. This is with Pooka. On the other hand you could go towards the Owl thing through Merits as suggested and give your Sluagh, who by the way can twist his/her head around like an owl no problems, Owl wings. Of course these two are not the only easy natural options for your wise owl since there is the Fuaths. Yes they have a nasty wild violent side which tends to emerge in life or death situations and under similar duress but that is way more lenient a curse than that of an average Brujah for example, and should pose no problem for playing a wise sage of knowledge, after all the Brujah were known as scholars once.<br /> <br /> Add to this that like PookaKnight mentioned there is an abundance of splats in CtD which is why I have hard time understanding these accusations of Kiths being somehow limiting. Pooka can be played in many ways most of them do not involve concepts of liar or a trickster, there are two socialite examples in Kithbook Pooka for example that nicely showcase how a Pooka can be played in the Noble Socialite Concept right along side the Sidhe without anyone claiming them liars or tricksters. There is no lack of splats in CtD there is like said above a splat overload and in addition to that the splats actually can be played in as versatile manner as any Clan or Tribe the difference is that for some reason most people refuse to look beyond the obvious in CtD, which is ironic since it is the one game that tends to emphasize that the truth is often hidden under a layer of obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T08:32:02-07:00","id":145679,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying the the Wise Owl example is impossible to do, I'm saying that you get to the core book Kiths and you don't see it as viable anymore. Nothing in the presentation gives you an obvious option; especially if you don't want to be riddle-trickster about it. Having to take Merits just to accomplish a basic concept? That's not a good counter-argument. I don't need Merits to make a suave Gangrel, or a sneaky Get of Fenris.<br /> <br /> And the abundance of splats in CtD are largely supplemental. They're not presented as core options. You need... what? 6 or so books to actually have the full spread of Kiths PookaKnight brought up. A large number of which are not compatible in a single group.<br /> <br /> As for the comparison to Lost?<br /> <br /> Lost has a metric ton of Kiths, sure, but Kiths in Lost are just modifiers to Seemings. You pick a Lost Seeming (which is more comparable to a Dreaming Kith) and then the laundry list of possible Kiths within a Seeming (which is optional, Kithless Lost are supposed to be a thing even if there is no reason to do it mechanically). Lost Kiths are basically a free Merit you get to bend your very general Seeming into something more specific. That's the &quot;flexibility&quot; thing. The base splat (Seeming) is very broad and open to interpretation. And you get a free list of things you can pick from to support your interpretation. And the list isn't exhaustive. Making your own if none of the list fits is something you're encouraged to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T12:13:58-07:00","id":145901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=145679#post145679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying the the Wise Owl example is impossible to do, I'm saying that you get to the core book Kiths and you don't see it as viable anymore. Nothing in the presentation gives you an obvious option; especially if you don't want to be riddle-trickster about it. Having to take Merits just to accomplish a basic concept? That's not a good counter-argument. I don't need Merits to make a suave Gangrel, or a sneaky Get of Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's a different comparison don't you agree? You can make a wise Owl Changeling with the Core Kiths or a Socialite Butterfly etc and need no merits to do so. The merit comparison is equal to you wanting to play a Ventrue with Wolf-features, you will need merits or other supernatural things to make it happen. Same is true if playing Owl like Sluagh, apart from their ability to twist their heads like one, you need a Merit to do so but unlike in Vampire the Merits that allow you to customize your character like this are widely available from the Core. The rest of the options come with the supplemental books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=145679#post145679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the abundance of splats in CtD are largely supplemental. They're not presented as core options. You need... what? 6 or so books to actually have the full spread of Kiths PookaKnight brought up. A large number of which are not compatible in a single group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same is true of Vampire, Werewolf, Mage and the other core games from the 2nd edition times. So it's a bit unfair to compare that to NWoD book that gives a bit more options on the Core or the 20th anniversary editions of CWoD games where they have purposefully collected as many of the options between the two covers as possible. Still Changeling does have one of the widest splat selection of oWoD lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=145679#post145679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the comparison to Lost?<br /> <br /> Lost has a metric ton of Kiths, sure, but Kiths in Lost are just modifiers to Seemings. You pick a Lost Seeming (which is more comparable to a Dreaming Kith) and then the laundry list of possible Kiths within a Seeming (which is optional, Kithless Lost are supposed to be a thing even if there is no reason to do it mechanically). Lost Kiths are basically a free Merit you get to bend your very general Seeming into something more specific. That's the &quot;flexibility&quot; thing. The base splat (Seeming) is very broad and open to interpretation. And you get a free list of things you can pick from to support your interpretation. And the list isn't exhaustive. Making your own if none of the list fits is something you're encouraged to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for me as entertaining as the Seemings and the Kiths were they still felt a bit... stale I guess, compared to CtD Kiths. The various Kiths are my favourite part of the CtD setting and the reason I never seem to get quite that much out of CtL or even DA:Fae, though I like 'em both quite a lot for me they just loose something in loosing the Kiths. Also I had to give my players the Double-Kith (or whatever it's called) Merit for free just so that their characters had more of a CtD feel instead of being much more limited to a single theme.<br /> <br /> Still I have no objections for an optional system where you choose two Birthrights and a Frailty from set options determined by your Kith. Though I feel this might be better achieved by re-doing the DA:Fae system of Seemings and Frailties (or what ever they were called in Da:F).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T19:52:35-07:00","id":146274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=145454#post145454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest issue is the way they're handled. The Frailties in particular are a big culprit here. A Clan, mechanically, is a set of powers you get cheaper and a weakness. The Clans have a very big spread of options there, and you have to work pretty hard to come up with a concept that really falls flat with any of them.<br /> <br /> Garou Tribes are an example of how a few variables can vastly increase your options. Tribe only defines a fraction of your character's mechanics. Auspice and Breed also have a large impact. As long as it fits the fluff of WtA... it is a really big stretch to come up with a concept that you can't slot into a Tribe/Auspice/Breed combo of some sort.<br /> <br /> The problem with CtD is you run into really basic concepts that get cut out very quickly. You want to play a wise Owl changeling? Not going to happen. If you go Pooka you have to accept all the trickster and lying stuff that you don't care about (and is contrary to being the wise sage font of knowledge). If you go something like Boggan or Slaugh, the Owl part is lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was that whatever you play, you're just as restricted by a Clan Flaw as you are Kith Frailty. You can't play a Malkavian that isn't insane in some way; you can't play a pooka that tells a straight answer. Both gives plenty of leeway to interpret HOW it manifests, however. Your mileage has obviously been different than me, but I have never felt too restricted; in fact, each kith always seemed like a basic framework waiting to be built upon.<br /> <br /> What's really needed is more non-Eurocentric kith, or a guide to creating them. I'd love to see 'Keys to the Kingdom' - which promised to explore Africa - as a stretch goal. 'Book of Glamour' just needs to be worked into the main book, maybe with stretch goals for extra tidbits. I love tidbits. Mmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/h38q1qmfx/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/67hc6e1i5/i_backed_ex3_small.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2045-melonlord82","name":"melonlord82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2045_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T23:39:43-07:00","id":146462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=145630#post145630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see the flexibility argument from DA: Fae, but I've never understood it from Lost. You still have to pick a kith with the same sort of restrictions as in Dreaming.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>we're going to have to agree to disagree on this one. the Lost character creation process is in my opinion way more versatile than dreaming even with merits. Not just mechanicly but flavor wise. You place two Seelie Sidhe of House Fionna next too one another and they may be differnt people, but they are fundemetally the same thing. You place two Fairest Brightones of the Spring Court next to each other and not only are they different people, but they more than likely look entirley different, and approach their magic entirely different. One might get their light by having candles for eyes and wax dripping down their heads as hair and another might have a shining Arcadian star in place on their heart. Mechanically they are the same thing but story wise they couldn't be more different. you don't have to buy merits just to have the same ascetic look and abilities as their basic concept. <br /> <br /> though a good compromise could be to give changelings a certain number of Free Merit points at character creation too help customize their character with out getting rid of the kiths. I'm talking beyond basic freebies and in addition to any flaws. Or introduce new Merits and Flaws that allow the kiths too take a different frailty or birthright or just new Merits and Flaws that allow for more aesthetic choices rather. that way the aforementioned Wise owl Changeling can be possible with out having to sacrifice other abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T04:46:53-07:00","id":146575,"title":"","content":"Well, end of the day, C20 will be, at the hardest, a revision of Changeling: the Dreaming, not a total re-write (and thank goodness, the last thing the game needs is a <i>fourth</i> version - 1st and 2nd edition really are that different).<br /> <br /> Arguing that it needs to be like Dark Ages: Fae is like arguing that M20 needs to redo its magic system to that of DA: Mage. You might like it better, and i have no opinion either way on that... but the gamelines do have a story, and that story says that magic is harder now than it was then. paradox beats Mages across the face now, and banality restricts the Fae. Could even say it's the Dreaming's punishment against the changelings for having broken their oaths to not mingle blood with mortals, if you want the historical tie-in.<br /> <br /> That said, the kiths COULD use a little re-working. 2nd edition is very... <i>second-edition-y</i>, because of how it goes &quot;this kith is always like this.&quot; Right down to what members of the kith <i>wear</i>. That's very easily corrected, of course.<br /> <br /> Some level of customization wouldn't be amiss - not full-out modularity, but something to make the kith more archetype and less stereotype. For instance, Boggans are a &quot;household spirit&quot; archetype, the genius locii of fields, hearths, mills and such. Why would a Boggan hailing from the dreams of a welsh bwg be identical to the boggan derived from a Swedish tomte or a Russian bannik? Very similar, sure, enough that they would consider each other brothers... but not identical. whether it's fluff about different Kithain &quot;tribes&quot; (similar to how Corax do) or full-on crunch, works for me.<br /> <br /> Second... Can we get a few more Arts, or some variety on what's there? Maybe even a few kith-specific arts (yes, we have Chronos, Infusion, and... and... urk, hurp, Talecraft). It was always a little bewildering that the supposedly most magical of the WoD's inhabitants... actually get the least variety in their magic. Much of the variety that is there is behind locked doors (These arts are for Nobles only. These Arts are Shadow Court only. These arts are mer only, etc.)<br /> <br /> Also... bring balance back towards Seelie / Unseelie. First things first, present the Seelie and Unseelie takes on kiths as equal, rather than the trend of one or othe other being &quot;anomalous&quot; - there's no reason in the world for trolls - trolls, for crying out loud - to be so seelie it makes your teeth hurt, with the Unseelie among htem a mistrusted minority. Make the pslit between the two &quot;no big deal&quot; for the commoner kith - they've been living this way for centuries, after all. And while the books do <i>say</i> &quot;seelie is not good nor is unseelie evil,&quot; in practice it doesn't pan out; the seelie are depicted as good guys, the unseelie as bad guys. Part of this is the legacy system; Seelie legacies are all clearly positive or at least benign, while Unseelie legacies are... anything but. An idea I pitched to my changeling ST, was to make [i]each[/] Legacy have both a Seelie and Unseelie face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T05:12:03-07:00","id":146589,"title":"","content":"When I say I want DA:Fae updated to modern that includes some blending of CtD in with it. The powers should be weaker all around (no more turning the top of a mountain temporarily into the sun to kill all the Vamps.) but should still be organized into the Dawn/Day/Dusk/Night. Banality should definitely exist in some fashion, and players should generally be restricted to Changelings; but with rules on creating Fae/Inanimae for Storytellers.<br /> <br /> I would keep the seasonal courts too instead of the slightly too simple dichotomy of Seelie/Unseelie. I would also keep Echoes/Oaths. The Features absolutely trump kiths for character creation though. Would it be a drastic change for fans of CtD? Probably, but the CtD metaplot could be worked into it; and other than the metaplot what is it you really need from CtD to come forward to C20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T05:26:10-07:00","id":146604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=146589#post146589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">other than the metaplot what is it you really need from CtD to come forward to C20?</div> </div> </div> </div> The game to actually be Changeling: The Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I really enjoy DA: Fae. I'd like to see it get a big, impressive book to go along with V20: Dark Ages, but I want my C20 to be Changeling: The Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":".  Formatting 05-23-2014, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T08:27:10-07:00","id":146780,"title":"","content":"Picked up CtD 1st ed (along with Street Fighter) Wednesday. Still reading through it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T15:11:44-07:00","id":147192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=146604#post146604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The game to actually be Changeling: The Dreaming. Don't get me wrong, I really enjoy DA: Fae. I'd like to see it get a big, impressive book to go along with V20: Dark Ages, but I want my C20 to be Changeling: The Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well if having both is an option that'd be swell. I wouldn't expect that though and would prefer modern fae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T15:35:57-07:00","id":147229,"title":"","content":"Why not? It's in the top 1% selling books on DriveThruRPG. Dark Ages: Vampire is the only other fat splat from the Dark Ages line with that distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T20:33:08-07:00","id":149991,"title":"","content":"I would like what changeling promised to deliver, the magic of Disney, the politics and danger of Game of Thrones, the romance and adventure of The Princess Bride and the beauty and strangeness of Labyrinth and Mirrormask. all superimposed on a modern urban landscape where danger hides around every corner. but seriously, banality needs work if not outright removal. standing in line at the post office and getting a bank loan should not mean death to my supposedly immortal faery soul. also some work on its image and presentation so that it doesn't come off as childish as it does to so many, my self included. yes i know its an annoying stereotype but really the way the book presents it is Growing up= bad, never growing up = good. it may not be the whole picture but it is there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T10:33:23-07:00","id":150536,"title":"","content":"Could some of the difficulty with breadth of Kith choices stem from the source myths used? For most gamelines, the core concept is basically one core thing: a human-animal shapeshifter, a human-turned vampire, a spellcasting human, an enlightened human scientist, a human ghost, etc.<br /> <br /> But then in Changeling, it seems to me that a much wider variety of mythical beings are brought in as possibilities. Your origin isn't human, your themes aren't tied down to one culture or just to animal aesthetics or just science or just death, etc. There seems to be as much variety of potential myth-origin in one single Kith as in an entire fatsplat of most other gamelines. As a result, the variety of options that you <b>want</b> to have available in a game of Changeling may feel much wider.<br /> <br /> I could be misinterpreting, of course. Not a Changeling player.<br /> <br /> <br /> (That said, if I were making from scratch a game about all the variety of mythic and folkloric creatures that could loosely be interpreted as faerie or gods, I'd make their magic as flexible as Mage spheres.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-27-2014, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T10:38:48-07:00","id":150542,"title":"","content":"Have any changeling fans read Tithe or its follow ups by Holly Black? That is my ideal changeling setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T11:54:01-07:00","id":150665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=150536#post150536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could some of the difficulty with breadth of Kith choices stem from the source myths used?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is certainly a problem for CtD.<br /> <br /> There is no real reason CtD needs to be so focused on European specific Kiths in the core book. The game more than adequately expands to lots of other areas. Instead of general Kiths that get reinterpreted slightly on a regional basis, we got &quot;bloat&quot; in the form of a new of Kiths for other cultures. <br /> <br /> Most of the cWOD have a pretty strong focus on the European side of the source myths, but leave far more room for taking the core character types and translating them into other cultures. The African vampire Legacies are mostly just reskinned versions of the extant VtM clans; as an example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T16:56:02-07:00","id":150889,"title":"","content":"CTD core Kiths and concept is built around mostly European style of faerie tales and stories complete with entanglings of Arthurian legend and Norse myth. All of this built on a foundation of Irish classic Tuatha myth. That becomes the cornerstone of the setting and the types of characters. CTL is an awesome game but it is designed to be a very differant game, there's no way of playing in the style of stories that CTD is built around with CTL and vice versa. The utterly malleable Kiths are beautiful in CTL but they really don't fit the concept that CTD presents. This is why the Thallain, Gallain, Inanimae, Denizens and Nunnenhi were all shown in differant ways with differant Arts and other things. It'd be like Werewolf having some Garou, some cursed shifters that only do so at a full moon and are under the command of vampires and others that spread lycanthropy like a disease but all playable in the same group in the same game. CTD just like WTA or even VTM is based of one style and presented mythic thread. The faerie in the things that inspired changeling are of a fairly consistent nature in the tales that tell of them, their variability comes more often in attitude or through magics other than simple innate natures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T21:19:51-07:00","id":151017,"title":"","content":"I outlined my overall philosophy about how CtD20 should be approached in post #32. Applying that to Kiths:<br /> <br /> 1. Start by rewriting the fluff to present them as archtypes rather than stereotypes.<br /> 2. Keep the \u201ctwo Birthrights and one Frailty\u201d thing, but consider revising some of the existing Birthrights and Frailties to be applicable to a wider range of concepts.<br /> 3. Consider giving <i>every</i> Kith in the core book access to a unique Art of its own. This isn\u2019t so much a change from CtD as an expansion on it. There\u2019s also a reason why it\u2019s #3 and not #1. <br /> <br /> Only if the above steps prove inadequate should you get into such things as providing variant Birthrights and/or Frailties for the Kiths; and even then, such options should be presented as <i>options</i>: \u201cPookas have these two Birthrights; if you want, here\u2019s a pair of alternate Birthrights that can replace either or both of them\u201d, as opposed to \u201cevery Pooka has two of the four following Birthrights\u201d. Mechanically, these two options are virtually identical; but in terms of presentation, the former preserves more of the existing rules structure while the latter uproots it. The former also allows the \u201cvariations on the theme\u201d to be moved to an Appendix or the Companion, should the writers choose to do so; the latter forces you to present all four up front.<br /> <br /> I have similar thoughts about the Arts: start by seeing how much you can do with what you have; and if you need to broaden them, start by providing optional Cantrip alternatives for existing Arts (much like Wraith did in its Guildbooks for the Arcanoi), then consider adding some new Arts (such as the aforementioned \u201cone Art per Kith\u201d idea). I\u2019ve been toying with an \u201cUnleashing the Realms\u201d flexible magic system for CtD, inspired by DAFae\u2019s \u201cUnleashing the Dominions\u201d; but such a thing doesn\u2019t belong in the CtD20 core book. An optional system in a Companion book? Sure! But not presented as part of the core book\u2019s magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T06:37:45-07:00","id":151258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=151017#post151017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve been toying with an \u201cUnleashing the Realms\u201d flexible magic system for CtD, inspired by DAFae\u2019s \u201cUnleashing the Dominions\u201d; but such a thing doesn\u2019t belong in the CtD20 core book. An optional system in a Companion book? Sure! But not presented as part of the core book\u2019s magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think folks don't give the flexibility of the Art + Realm system enough credit. Creative players can go absolutely nuts with it! Admittedly, some of the realms could use a bit of revision to make them more usable, but the idea of the core magic system is really only beaten by Mage for flexibility out of the original World of Darkness games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T07:37:04-07:00","id":151285,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is that saying, &quot;the Arts + Realms system is really flexible compared to the rest of the cWOD,&quot; is a bit off point. It is in many ways, but the Realms especially often caused weird caps on creativity. And there are plenty of older games that do this sort of thing. A fairly on point example for the cWOD is Ars Magica which is right smack in the middle of CtD and Mage. Like CtD what you can do is governed by two interacting traits (Techniques and Forms), but like Mage they are more broad and malleable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T09:16:31-07:00","id":151347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=151017#post151017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">consider revising some of the existing Birthrights and Frailties to be applicable to a wider range of concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still fail to see concepts that couldn't work with pretty much any Kith we currently have so this point continues to elude me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T11:33:58-07:00","id":151522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=151285#post151285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem is that saying, &quot;the Arts + Realms system is really flexible compared to the rest of the cWOD,&quot; is a bit off point. It is in many ways, but the Realms especially often caused weird caps on creativity. And there are plenty of older games that do this sort of thing. A fairly on point example for the cWOD is Ars Magica which is right smack in the middle of CtD and Mage. Like CtD what you can do is governed by two interacting traits (Techniques and Forms), but like Mage they are more broad and malleable.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. And again, some sort of \u201cUnleashing the Realms\u201d thing would <i>not</i> be something that I\u2019d put into the CtD20 core book: if it appears <i>at all</i>, I\u2019d want it in the Companion, in much the same way that <b>Trinity</b> got a flexible psionic powers system in its Player\u2019s Guide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=151347#post151347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still fail to see concepts that couldn't work with pretty much any Kith we currently have so this point continues to elude me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that I said \u201cconsider\u201d: I was presenting a checklist to go down in terms of deciding what sorts of things to do to the Kiths in a CtD20 book, <i>not</i> a mandate of things they <i>should</i> do.<br /> <br /> That said, some things I\u2019d consider in terms of revising the Birthrights and Frailties (bearing in mind that I haven\u2019t read the Kithbooks):<br /> \u2022 Boggan Craftwork could stand to have the \u201ctime taken to complete task when unobserved\u201d expanded: instead of a flat \u201cone third the time\u201d, maybe make it something that scales with your permanent Glamour, or possibly make it something that lets you reduce the time for a lengthy task down to a single night.<br /> \u2022 Eshu Spirit Pathways could use some mechanics.<br /> \u2022 Pooka shapechanging shouldn\u2019t cost Glamour; but Calling On the Wyrd should be called out as a way of extending the shapechange to the mortal world.<br /> \u2022 Pooka Lies should be renamed at the very least; broadening them so that they\u2019re not always about deceit.<br /> \u2022 Every Kith other than Nocker and Redcap defines a class of rolls that it cannot botch; I\u2019d expand it to include Nockers and Redcaps, too (e.g., Redcaps can\u2019t botch Intimidation).<br /> <br /> The point is to stick to comparatively minor revisions, not total rewrites; and when you revise, focus on wider applicability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T13:56:10-07:00","id":151655,"title":"","content":"There is though, a standing question when it comes to C20:<br /> <br /> Will C20 be a Revised update to the system as well as a 20th Anniversary Edition, since it never got a Revised edition?<br /> <br /> Because how the design philosophy on C20 is determined is going to be pretty significant towards how much room there is for discussion of more significant system changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T14:19:56-07:00","id":151678,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know how much of an impact switching to Revised rules will have on the design; for the most part, it boils down to \u201cbotches are rare now\u201d \u2014 which was only an issue in <b>Mage</b> because its existing magic rules relied so heavily on botches, and wasn\u2019t much of an issue for [b]Vampire[/i] or <b>Werewolf</b> at all. Most of the controvertial changes in the Revised games were metaplot-related; and the 20th Anniversary Editions have thus far been universally metaplot-agnostic. So I wouldn\u2019t expect C20 to start laying down a \u201cHigh King David is back!\u201d thing, or \u201cthe gates of Arcadia have reopened!\u201d thing \u2014 at least, not as default changes to the status quo. Certainly, they\u2019re not going to declare that an entire Kith or House has been wiped out or withdrawn from Kithain society, or that Calling on the Wyrd inflicts damage to the changeling doing it (though I do think that adding some consequences to Calling On the Wyrd would not be inappropriate \u2014 just not as a \u201coh, look; the world has changed!\u201d thing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T16:19:44-07:00","id":151798,"title":"","content":"There were a lot more individual rules changes to things like supernatural powers, adding/subtracting/changing systems, and such. I don't just mean the Revised general rules, but what Revised CtD would have looked like (like probably including more of the 2e supplemental Kiths in the corebook, addressing some of the Banality and Glamour mechanics, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T22:01:12-07:00","id":160570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=151522#post151522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, some things I\u2019d consider in terms of revising the Birthrights and Frailties (bearing in mind that I haven\u2019t read the Kithbooks):<br /> \u2022 Boggan Craftwork could stand to have the \u201ctime taken to complete task when unobserved\u201d expanded: instead of a flat \u201cone third the time\u201d, maybe make it something that scales with your permanent Glamour, or possibly make it something that lets you reduce the time for a lengthy task down to a single night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trouble is, Glamour goes to 10; scaling it at Glamour then causes all sorts of weird issues, where at lower ends its just no good, while at higher ends it's TOO good... And it also means that childlings and wilders are better sat it than grumps... which when you think about it, makes no sense. if you ask me, Boggans should be the most greybeard-friendly of kiths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Eshu Spirit Pathways could use some mechanics. </div> </div> </div>Couldn't disagree harder. The whole point of this Boon is narrative, not systemic. Now, that said... maybe htey just <i>need a different boon</i> - Spirit pathways isn't something the player character can actively use or not, it's something htye have no control over, and as you point out gives no mechanical benefit... and if you have a weak changeling ST, this birthright is really wasted space.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Pooka Lies should be renamed at the very least; broadening them so that they\u2019re not always about deceit. </div> </div> </div>One idea came to me as i was listening to my Labyrinth soundtrack - in specific, Bowie's song &quot;Underground&quot;<br /> <br /> - Don't tell me the truth hurts, little girl; 'cause it <i>hurts like hell</i>.<br /> <br /> That is the crux of pooka lying right there. They lie and deceive <i>because the truth hurts</i>. Better to create a play fantasy than to let reality sneak in and bite you.<br /> <br /> There's another line in that one - &quot;it's only forever; not long at all&quot; which is stellar Sidhe material, i think. Idea being, maybe there ought to be a phrase that conveys the archetype of the kiths, both positive and negative<br /> <br /> - Sometimes the truth hurts<br /> - Forever's not long enough<br /> - Rolling stones gather no moss<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> [qupte]\u2022 Every Kith other than Nocker and Redcap defines a class of rolls that it cannot botch; I\u2019d expand it to include Nockers and Redcaps, too (e.g., Redcaps can\u2019t botch Intimidation).[/quote]<br /> <br /> 1st edition Nockers couldn't botch Crafts or Security rolls. Redcaps didn't get this type of bonus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T22:54:42-07:00","id":160602,"title":"","content":"Your response to my point about the Pooka misses the heart of my point. As written, the Pooka are the only \u201canimal fae\u201d, and they\u2019re <i>universally compulsive liars</i>. If I want to do an Owl changeling, there\u2019s no room to diversify: I either have to write him up as a Pooka (which means that he never tells the truth) or I have to invent a new Kith from scratch and convince my Storyteller to accept it. What I\u2019m looking for here is wording that suggests possibilities such as cryptic answers as an alternative to \u201calways incorporate lies into what they say\u201d \u2014 something like \u201cnever say what you mean\u201d. That <i>could</i> be interpreted as \u201clying\u201d, and usually would be; but it could also cover the \u201cwise elder\u201d archetype who encourages you to figure things out for yourself. He never attempts to deceive you; but you\u2019ll never get a straight answer out of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T04:26:19-07:00","id":160716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=160602#post160602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your response to my point about the Pooka misses the heart of my point. As written, the Pooka are the only \u201canimal fae\u201d, and they\u2019re <i>universally compulsive liars</i>. If I want to do an Owl changeling, there\u2019s no room to diversify: I either have to write him up as a Pooka (which means that he never tells the truth) or I have to invent a new Kith from scratch and convince my Storyteller to accept it. What I\u2019m looking for here is wording that suggests possibilities such as cryptic answers as an alternative to \u201calways incorporate lies into what they say\u201d \u2014 something like \u201cnever say what you mean\u201d. That <i>could</i> be interpreted as \u201clying\u201d, and usually would be; but it could also cover the \u201cwise elder\u201d archetype who encourages you to figure things out for yourself. He never attempts to deceive you; but you\u2019ll never get a straight answer out of him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, yeah, I kind of went off on my own ramble there.<br /> <br /> You have a valid point. Rather than &quot;Pooka lie,&quot; it could be changed to &quot;pooka can't tell the plain truth.&quot; Deception and falsehood don't necessarily mean LIES, after all. This is explored in the kithbook... and is possibly the only part of the kithbook worth reading. All that needs be is that the listener is not receiving &quot;the truth&quot; - maybe they can get there on their own from clues and cues, but that's from their own thinking and not the Pooka making it easy for them.<br /> <br /> Opposite-speak should garner banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T06:35:40-07:00","id":160758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=160602#post160602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As written, the Pooka are the only \u201canimal fae\u201d, and they\u2019re <i>universally compulsive liars</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the Fuaths? They are animal Fae, I think Owl is even mentioned in their description text as an example. In addition to these two animal Fae almost every Kith has associations with animals, insects or arachnids and with the Metamorphosis Art the Pooka are not even alone in the capability to transform into an animal form.<br /> <br /> I thought we already danced this dance, I and other people as well gave you multiple ways to do the wise owl fae that are perfectly within the rules and systems of CtD as it currently is. I also went through the Pooka issue rather throughoutly, I thought I did at least, explaining that them needing to Lie can mean a whole lot of things some of them exactly fitting for a wise owl seer archtype. Really read through the Kithbook: Pooka and it's explanation of Pookaese if you do not believe me. Also it explicitly says in the description of the Frailty that you can never tell the full truth but must mix in some lies as well. It doesn't say that you must lie about everything halftruths are perfect vessel for cryptic advice for a seer to give as are riddles, where you actually do neither lie nor tell the truth instead allowing the listener to draw their own conclusions. <br /> <br /> The open wording is already there in the Frailty if you read past the Frailty name which is simply Lies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T07:57:40-07:00","id":160803,"title":"","content":"Possessed: do me a favor and get off your high horse \u2014 don\u2019t assume that I\u2019m ignorant of what the book says or that I think that pookas need to be completely reinvented from the ground up; neither is true. In fact, we\u2019re not even in disagreement, for the most part. Bear with me for a moment, and I\u2019ll explain:<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s the complete text of the Pooka Frailty, from the 2nd Edition:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">\u2022 <b>Lies</b> \u2014 People may trust a pooka, but no one in their right mind would believe one. They\u2019re infamous for their elaborate lies. No matter how important a issue may be, a pooka must always mix in a lie. It\u2019s her nature. A pooka must make a Willpower roll (difficulty 8) to tell the whole truth.<br /> <br /> Different pooka have different styles of lying. Some Seelie pooka always say the opposite of what they mean, while many Unseelie purposefully tell the truth now and then to throw listeners off-guard. Unseelie pooka sometimes couch their lies very carefully \u2014 if an Unseelie makes his Willpower roll at the beginning of a scene, he can mix lies and truth freely. This can make him even more dangerous....</span></div>I agree that \u201clie\u201d can be interpreted more broadly than the above text suggests, and I\u2019ll take you at your word that <b>Kithbook Pooka</b> addresses this issue. Indeed, it can be potentially be interpreted so broadly that the label \u201clie\u201d is no longer technically accurate, as a \u201clie\u201d is technically an effort to deceive: a Seelie pooka who engages in opposite-speak isn\u2019t trying to deceive; quite the opposite, in fact. An owl-pooka who \u201clies\u201d by speaking in riddles or parables intended to force the listener to think <i>also</i> isn\u2019t trying to deceive. These fit the strictly mechanical requirement of having to make a Willpower roll to tell the full truth; but they\u2019re not attempts to conceal the truth, and so technically don\u2019t qualify as what most people think of as \u201clies\u201d \u2014 which is why I\u2019d like a different name for this Frailty.<br /> <br /> As for the text itself: I don\u2019t want every reader of C20 to have to go to the message boards to get advice from veteran Changeling fans or to have to buy <b>Kithbook Pooka</b> in order to realize just how broad this Frailty can be. I want C20\u2019s text for this Frailty to more clearly spell out how flexibly it can be interpreted. As I said at the top of my first post on this issue, I want C20 to address these things first by clarifying existing rules, and only resorting to rules rewrites if clarification is inadequate. And if a rewrite of the mechanics <i>is</i> needed, try a rewrite that expands on the original functionality rather than replacing it: rewriting a Frailty to do something entirely different from what it did in 2e should be a last resort for only the most broken of rules.<br /> <br /> In summary: The issue I\u2019m talking about concerning pooka Lies <i>is</i> addressed in the 2e gameline \u2014 but it\u2019s addressed in a supplement; in C20, I want it to be addressed in the core rulebook, so that nobody walks away from reading its description of the Pooka with the impression that there\u2019s only one way that they\u2019re intended to be played. Broad archetype, not narrow stereotype.<br /> <br /> On the Fuath: which supplement were they published in? I\u2019ll grant that they <i>may </i>address my concern; but one issue that C20 is going to have to deal with that V20, W20, and M20 didn\u2019t is the sheer number of Kiths out there \u2014 especially if you go beyond the Kithain and try to include Menehune, Nunene (sp?), Thallain, Inanimae, Adhene, etc.: unless you go with super-condensed write-ups for each, the Kith write-ups would fill up a book all by themselves: I just don\u2019t see including every Kith in the corebook as a practical option. I\u2019d want to restrict the core book to Kithain and Thallain (and even the Thallain I\u2019d present in highly condensed form, as boxes attached to their Kithain counterparts), with other kinds of Fae being addressed later in a supplement dedicated to them, much like <b>Changing Breeds</b> did for W20.<br /> <br /> So are the Fuath Kithain who would end up in the core book, or are they among the many Gallain who would end up in a supplement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-06-2014, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T08:32:53-07:00","id":160856,"title":"","content":"To illustrate what I\u2019m thinking, here\u2019s a very rough draft of how I\u2019d like the Pooka Frailty to read:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">\u2022 <b>Guile</b> \u2014 pooka never give you a straight answer; in order to tell the truth, the whole truth, and nothing <i>but</i> the truth, without omitting anything significant, misrepresenting some fact, or embelishing on the truth, a pooka must win a Willpower roll (difficulty 8).<br /> <br /> This is most famously used to deceive; but it can be done for other purposes as well, such as mocking someone or encouraging him to come up with his own answers.</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-06-2014, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T12:59:50-07:00","id":161030,"title":"","content":"Didn't mean to sound all high horsey and stuff it's just that I thought we went through this all earlier and it sounded like the very same complain as earlier.<br /> <br /> The Fuath are Adhene so they can be found in the Denizens of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> If it's merely about changing the wording of the Frailty, in a way that holds true to the original concept, that eases you instead of changing the Frailty itself I have no complaints. Especially if you manage to get it described with lesser word count, as you did above, it's all good. I mistakenly, probably because I was a bit preoccupied by other matters as I responded, understood your issue to be with the actual Frailty itself instead of merely re-wording it to be clearer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T15:23:30-07:00","id":161186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=161030#post161030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't mean to sound all high horsey and stuff it's just that I thought we went through this all earlier and it sounded like the very same complain as earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. FWIW, I was implicitly referencing the earlier discussion. Largely because I agree with it, and would like something to that effect written into C20\u2019s core book. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=161030#post161030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fuath are Adhene so they can be found in the Denizens of the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK; then not suitable for inclusion in C20\u2019s core book. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=161030#post161030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's merely about changing the wording of the Frailty, in a way that holds true to the original concept, that eases you instead of changing the Frailty itself I have no complaints. Especially if you manage to get it described with lesser word count, as you did above, it's all good. I mistakenly, probably because I was a bit preoccupied by other matters as I responded, understood your issue to be with the actual Frailty itself instead of merely re-wording it to be clearer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, post #93 <i>does</i> change the actual game mechanics of the Frailty: as written in 2e, a pooka only needs to make the Willpower roll in order to tell \u201cthe whole truth\u201d: that is, it would require a Willpower roll to be factually accurate but in a deceptive way (e.g., saying something that\u2019s 100% true but in a sarcastic tone of voice that carries the subtext that what you just said is obviously false). The above rephrasing not only conforms better to what I understand the intended spirit of the rule to be; but it also suggests possibilities where deception doesn\u2019t even enter the picture. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T18:58:34-07:00","id":161332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=78279#post78279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FWXoCXMo_IM\" data-code=\"FWXoCXMo_IM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/FWXoCXMo_IM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Yep, I <i>really</i> want a Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm torn on Kithbook: Boggans. On the one hand, it would be nice to have an official book. On the other other hand, back when it seemed like Changeling: The Dreaming would never in a million years have any chance of coming back, the fan community at the time pulled together and created a fantastic fan version of the book Thad's writing is just as good, or better than, most of the published Kithbooks. A lot of great artists, including Melissa Uran, pitched in art. I tried to do the layout so that it would look indistinguishable from the other Kithbooks. It would be nice if all that effort could be acknowledged in some way. If you're interested in it, there's a link to the book in my sig.<br /> <br /> As for Book of Glamour, I'd love to see it if it could be released now. Otherwise, we're getting very close to Dreaming's 20th Anniversary. It was intended to be a mostly rules book to update Changeling's magic system to revised standards without the expense of actually released a revised core book for the game. If there's going to be a C20 and Book of Glamour could only be released close to it, I'd kind of rather they just put the effort into updating the rules to revised standards and roll any extras into C20 itself.<br /> <br /> I'd rather see the stretch goals used for new things that might not have any chance of happening otherwise - a Book of Nod style book for Changeling, updating the cantrip card rules to C20, print on demand cantrip cards, something that really delves into the Changeling Way ritual and covers the difference between changelings and arcadian fae, and a book on how things transitioned from DA: Fae to C:tD and maybe show how some of the things that weren't mentioned in DA: Fae work in the Dark Ages: the noble houses, the Tuatha, the Fomorians, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>did you make that video?<br /> <br /> It was great, I loved it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T19:16:46-07:00","id":161338,"title":"","content":"I did! Thank you, I'm glad you enjoyed it! I had a lot of fun making it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T20:01:32-07:00","id":161363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=161338#post161338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did! Thank you, I'm glad you enjoyed it! I had a lot of fun making it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Amazeballs! Well you just earned my funding for C20!<br /> <br /> I didn't fund anything on kickstarter, not even Mage 20 which is the only game I'll even buy but thanks to your work, I'll throw in some money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T15:26:43-07:00","id":215147,"title":"","content":"I did a lot of research about Changeling: The Dreaming and I'd love to add something from myself.<br /> I think I gathered thinkings of many people.<br /> <br /> Main research includes:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.shadownesssence.com/forum/index.php?/topic/36246-20th-anniversary-edition-of-changeling-2nd-edition-feedback/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.shadownesssence.com/forum...tion-feedback/</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://oathcircle.com/wiki/Icons\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://oathcircle.com/wiki/Icons\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://oathcircle.com/wiki/Icons\" target=\"_blank\"> http://oathcircle.com/wiki/Icons </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1. First, the Dreaming deserves being renovated. In my country (Poland) for example the big three (Werewolf, Vampire, Mage) are totally popular games and both Wraith and Changeling (not to mention smaller games) are totally unknown to most players. What's more, Changeling: The Lost won the audience and gained really large fame. If somebody talks about Changeling, he thinks about The Lost. People laugh at Dreaming and don't even get this, but still main statement is such that Dreaming has zero gloom, dark of World of Darkness and WoD players love creepy and dark fairy tales, Pan's Labirynth etc. so they insist on The Lost as being best Changeling game and that The Dreaming is not worth even reading. And the reading probably often turns them off even if they are really curious about changelings.<br /> <br /> 2. Secondary, this is the biggest trouble that The Dreaming line was trying (and 20th edition has to) fight. We can see it by handbooks like Shattered Dream: War in Concordia which destroys USA-centrality of the game and ideas od unknown kingdoms which waste so much of space (Canada as big large icy wasteland..). We can see it by enormously famous The Shadow Court, by Autumn People, by exotic Land of Eight Million Dreams, we see it in Denizens of the Dreaming. All of them introduced more and more gloomy, obscure and gothic ways into the Changeling. Even such thinks as Empire of Dolls from Inanimae has something creepy in it.<br /> Typical &quot;Lost&quot; from C:TL can be only one of many options avaiable in C:TD - and that's the advantage of The Dreaming. Would love to make use of it.<br /> Sadly, later and later handbooks just like all Changeling game line were not profitable so they were made in black&amp;white color scheme.<br /> <br /> Maybe the way for darkening The Dreaming the way it deserves if not only the Winter chill (which kills every dream, good of bad), but introducing Dark Glamour (mentioned somewhere, probably Book of Glamour?) and that The Dreaming is half a Nightmare (or more often a Nightmare due to mankind state of soul..). I love the concept of comparing the layers of The Dreaming (Umbra) to the states of humand dream. This is totally awesome in so many ways. Also helps to understand the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Near Dreaming is sentient Superego. Far Dreaming is Ego and totally insane, nonlogical Deep Dreaming, also the source of all nightmares (and pervesities) not only in the Changeling game, is the most primal part of mind called Id. Thinking about Deep Dreaming and Arcadia as places of Id... it concludes shocking awareness that Arcadia od C:TD must be the same selfish, insane place of godly beings with children brains, and being trapped there is a true horror. So... C:TD Arcadia would be much the same as C:TL.. right?! This gives some more horror into this modern fantasy game if you think about it this way. Dreams &amp; Nightmares handbook describes Arcadia as hostile place which kills any changeling on sight. This could be really true more over than not!<br /> <br /> That's the way to give more glooooom it was lacking and the people stated that it was the advantage of C:TL over C:TD. Am I right?<br /> <br /> 3. Let's face it - there is huge need for geographical information. WoD is really known outside US and Changeling doesnt even give a hint about Slavic counterparts, Arabian lands, etc. This concluded into many fan-made books I didn't even seen, but let's just see this: <a href=\"http://oathcircle.com/wiki/Icons\" target=\"_blank\">http://oathcircle.com/wiki/Icons</a><br /> People totally love Changeling colours and estetics. These symbolics and filling empty holes where creators forgot about symbol for some art, kith, whatever.. are the best proof.<br /> But we were talking about geographics. Yes, with it I mean many other kiths, courts, politics.<br /> You do not have to forget about US and UK which had been described in Immortal Eyes Trilogy etc. Have you played Gray Matter adventure game by Jane Jensen? Let's face it, Oxford is totally mystical and fairy city. Would love to see it described this way somehow. And many other European and non-European cities deserve this fate. Even Dark Ages: Fae ignored slavic lands in medieval reality (why..).<br /> <br /> Fans invented skandinavian, slavic, arabian, african etc. lands for changelings, with their own dreamings/chimerical worlds, politics, kingdoms etc. This is what we really need. Are slavic changelings similar to old kiths (just having different names and courts) or totally new kiths all around just like Nunnehi, Menehune etc.?<br /> And somehow Slavic lands are ignored in many games, while aside with german and celtic myths and folklore, slavic is the richest source of supernaturals in culture. Not ignored that much in Vampire of Werelwolf.. but in Changeling..? Why? Fanmade material is full of vilas, rusalka, swan maidens and domowoye (as sub-kith of boggans ). We Slavs also have many intriguing faerie (we don't call them faeries, every supernatural thing is demon by name <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) like for example poludnik (meaning &quot;both south and noon&quot;) who suffocate people who sleep at full noon in the corn field ;&gt;<br /> So.. this isn't only remaking mistakes in the C:TD. It is also showing unpublished books and still wanted information about rest of the world. World of Darkness 2 ed. geographical handbook was one of the most popular, telling nearly about every corner of the Earth.. even if out of date information, still best for playing for example in mentioned Middle East.<br /> <br /> Probably Changeling would be separated into core book with Kithain etc. + another additional book with all other Gallain (additional Kithain, Thallain, Adhene, Hsien, Menehune, Nunnehi, Dauntan&amp;Autumn Fae, Merfolk + mooore kiths from all around the world, beforementioned) in the same way Werewolf made Changing Breeds another handbook.<br /> <br /> 4. I had thought once that arabian changelings are naturally djinn. People told me they are just Umbrood from Mage: The Ascension (Lost Paths book). So I was really surprised when I found out in the link above in #3 that someone invented separately genies as changelings for arabian people. That's totally amazing that instinctively we saw it this way. We are only fed with Naraka as Denizens of Indian heritage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Why I am speaking about it? Beucase people talk about infamous Book of Glamour, which had to have many fantastic new theories and secrets about dreaming and very nature of glamour.<br /> But nobody mentioned that in the Year of the Scarab (2001) which resolved around arabian, egyptian, mummy moods.. had also handbook for Changeling, named Keys to the Kingdom. Never released. No single mention what was this about. Keys to the Kingdom... which kingdom? And how does it resolve around not easy lands on Middle East? Did they want to add genies or.. something else? As we know, before Islam arabians had a plenty (I mean, PLENTY) of little gods, other than genis, worshiped somehow on the desert. So... this is also alive in their lands.<br /> The only small information, traces about Africa and Arabia are mentioned in Eshu Kithbook. But this isn't too much.<br /> <br /> 5. Morality part. Well, probably this is the thing we shouldn't touch beucase this is the main heart of WoD games, morality. In vampire and demon it is human, empathic morality, in werewolf.. killing a human isn't straightforward sin, but still gives us closer to the wyrm and corrupts heart in this totally awerted morality or primal horror. In mage, morality is a karmic one - bad things resonate and will come back to us (and warp out our deeds and lifes). In changeling.. the only sin is banality.. and doing bad things isn't bad.. the only way to scare players is to wag a finger and send changeling either into banality undoing or into insanity of bedlam. But still it is somehow strange. Playing by default the Seelies, honorable &amp; fluffy doesn't give that much free will. But on the other way if they were so honorable there wouldn't be so much hypocrisy, intrigue and Accordance War between nobles and commoners... Still this thing is the problematic one for many players. Resolved in C:TL.<br /> <br /> 6. Meta-plot. All 20th anniversary are trying to help meta-plot deconstruction of the world. In case of Changeling we have.. death of Ravana from spirit-nuke of Technocracy which gave us awesome Adhene (Denizens of the Dreaming) and much dark. Sadly it is still meta-plot which not everyone likes into their games. This has obviously to be repaired, am I right? Historical events like 1969 year (Moon Landing) + 3-years Accordance War and then Concordia at War years later, vanishing of King David... aw... so much meta-plot and politics in the world of the most chaotic and fluid changelings! It doesn't matter if somebody wants to play typical game in the 90s. But.. if you want to play in another historical time like Changeling: Victorian Age (awesome idea), then you have no sidhe. Did you heard? NO SIDHE! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No nobles. No <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Der Erlk\u00f6nig. Only wandering motleys of commoners who try to play The Carnivale TV series (which is totally awesome and surreal, but still.. no sidhe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> which are like half of the politics and fun and epic constructing the game?) Well, such an important event as Moon Landing and opening gates of Arcadia cannot be changed. But still meta-plot twists and twists.. into anomalies.<br /> Maybe this is only my own feeling?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 07-31-2014, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T22:27:45-07:00","id":215560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=215147#post215147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5. Morality part. Well, probably this is the thing we shouldn't touch beucase this is the main heart of WoD games, morality. In vampire and demon it is human, empathic morality, in werewolf.. killing a human isn't straightforward sin, but still gives us closer to the wyrm and corrupts heart in this totally awerted morality or primal horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. In Werewolf, the consequences of killing are just that - the consequences. There is no meter counting out corruption due to number of humans slain. Instead, there are entanglements and complications resulting from said killing. The heat might get turned up on the characters, and possibly their entire sept, if the killings are seen a certain way. If a character left forensic evidence at the scene, it might result in a warrant and some time cooling heels in the Umbra and hiding from the law as a fugitive. If the slaying offends even the Garou, it will cause the loss of Honor Renown. But Werewolf doesn't go for the slow ruin thing, which is why there's no analog of Humanity or degeneration mechanics, unless, of course, you're dealing with Abominations or the Possessed (and in the latter case, Kami don't carry that baggage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T00:36:42-07:00","id":215652,"title":"","content":"Just read across the thread and just wanted to say I'm in PookaKnight's side. Wholeheartedly and completely. I'm in favour of C:tD20, sick and tired of all the jokes on C:tD and having to explain again and again what the game is about and what it is not, etc... I guess I have been really lucky with my WoD players in these last years, as I have been able to make them interact with and even play Changeling characters without even one teddy bear joke...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T04:26:10-07:00","id":215742,"title":"","content":"One thing that Wraith and Changeling, the two games that never made it to revised edition, have in common is that both take place in another world. The OWoD books have always been, at least in my opinion, rather vague about how the other worlds (the umbra, the shadowlands, the dreaming) function. It's always been my biggest stumbling block with these two game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T07:31:36-07:00","id":215839,"title":"","content":"Rather vague? Are you serious? Have you read The Sea of Shadows, Dreams and Nightmares, Umbra, The Book of Worlds, etc...?<br /> <br /> And Wraith and Changeling do not take place in another world: they take place in this world... It is just that this world, as seen by them, is next to other worlds. And the gates are open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T09:37:08-07:00","id":215932,"title":"","content":"Wraith really more takes place in another world. Unless you count the Penumbra in Werewolf as the same world as the WoD version of the one we walk around in. Wraiths have to have special powers, deal with a barrier, etc. to affect the people and things of this world, aside from sucking up emotional energy and using some senses. <br /> <br /> I agree on Changeling. They are a lot like Werewolves only canted a little more towards having to live and function in the &quot;walking around world&quot; as they can really only access a limited version of the Penumbra of the Dreaming with any ease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T09:41:18-07:00","id":215939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=215652#post215652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just read across the thread and just wanted to say I'm in PookaKnight's side. Wholeheartedly and completely. I'm in favour of C:tD20, sick and tired of all the jokes on C:tD and having to explain again and again what the game is about and what it is not, etc... I guess I have been really lucky with my WoD players in these last years, as I have been able to make them interact with and even play Changeling characters without even one teddy bear joke...</div> </div> </div> </div>In one city-based game, my mages were scared to death of the changelings. They seemed like Marauders who could actually function effectively. None of them were cute or funny except in a slightly off-putting a usually very creepy way. Otherwise they were, at best, a little off-kilter and intriguing or beautiful/horrifying and terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T10:49:21-07:00","id":216008,"title":"","content":"It is true that Wraiths dwell mostly in the Shadowlands, but the Shadowlands are separated from our world just by a thin barrier, the Shroud, which may simple be a veil that prevents living people from seeing 'dead things'. So, Wraiths are all around us; they can see us (through the Shroud) but we cannot see them. The Underworld is important, but Wraiths are chained by their Fetters to the world of the living, not to the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T03:32:11-07:00","id":216635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=215560#post215560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. In Werewolf, the consequences of killing are just that - the consequences. There is no meter counting out corruption due to number of humans slain. Instead, there are entanglements and complications resulting from said killing. The heat might get turned up on the characters, and possibly their entire sept, if the killings are seen a certain way. If a character left forensic evidence at the scene, it might result in a warrant and some time cooling heels in the Umbra and hiding from the law as a fugitive. If the slaying offends even the Garou, it will cause the loss of Honor Renown. But Werewolf doesn't go for the slow ruin thing, which is why there's no analog of Humanity or degeneration mechanics, unless, of course, you're dealing with Abominations or the Possessed (and in the latter case, Kami don't carry that baggage).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, the Renown system is the only way besides &quot;taint on soul&quot; that degradates our werewolf for being a douchebag, malefactor, murderer. Not in every place (neonazi Fenris, wilk syberian Red Talons, would-be-mystical-and-peacful Furies in homeland of art Greece...etc.). But it's okay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=215939#post215939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In one city-based game, my mages were scared to death of the changelings. They seemed like Marauders who could actually function effectively. None of them were cute or funny except in a slightly off-putting a usually very creepy way. Otherwise they were, at best, a little off-kilter and intriguing or beautiful/horrifying and terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeah. We cant have teddy bear changelings on one side or creepy psychopaths on the other side.. Doesn't fit me well. How can we like them, really?<br /> And they say that Vampire is game about throwing cars...<br /> Lets say it: Vampire is full humanity&amp;romanticism game so I don't have to tell why we like vampires and like being them. We empathise their loss. Same with Wraiths. Werewolves are primal and cosmical horror in lovecraftian way, but still - they show problem of the nature&amp;mankind. But we may laught at green-terrorist types. There is also a society problem. I show Werewolves as these who fight there where there is no other justice. I like to mention Africa but lets face it - nobody interferes in these genocides. Only the Swara (cheetahs) are furious spirits, who are maddened by the smell of blood from black African soil. That's enough for me. That doesn't even deserve a commentary. But still it can't help these lands even from supernatural murdering Swara. That's tragic.<br /> Okay, mages... so much of them you can't tell which is romantic, which power-hungry etc. etc. Philosophy is important for me just as religion and technology clash. (I am civil engineer btw.)<br /> And changelings? Fighting for children dreams? Nope, they do not do that really at al... And childrens are the future of the nation. (In magyckal terms - children are tabula rasa which will form the future consensus..)<br /> <br /> I feel that changelings are really like capricious kids which work all about romance, boo-boo and everything that creates Glamour. Rather than metaploting 1969 Moon Landing I would rather want to see that fairies were always by mankind side.<br /> <br /> Medieval folklore, rennaissance (Sheakspeare works) and romanticism (Geothe before and dark fairies in Blake, Poe, Blackwood works... which resulted in gothic and victorian works, faries alongside with victorian spiritualism which Wraith: The Oblivion acquired and Changeling DIDNT <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's a HUGE HOLE in historii od changelings) and modernism/fin de siecl + in periods &lt;3<br /> <br /> Not to mention awesome Interwar Period (Lovecraft and his Unknown Kadath Quest about DREAMLANDS ? Lovecraft who was inspired by Poe and Blackwood works? Not to mention Howards' Hyborian age, which also inspired these works (they exchanged letters between themselves).)<br /> <br /> My own country (Poland) also has awesome writers or romanticism (A.Mickiewicz, K.C.Norwid, J. S\u0142owacki called Three Prophets, and Krasi\u0144ski who wrote fatalistic Non-Divine Comedy.) and in Interwar Period Witkacy. In mostly rural Poland after regaining independence from Russia, Germany and Austria, this wasn't country of technology like France, Germany, England, but still futurism, technologism and other this stuff was really vibrant in these days Warsaw, Cracov, Gda\u0144sk (and Gdynia was exploding city of young, beautiful people - such was it called.) This futurism was embraced in many dramas and works, but despite lacking of technological advancement like western countries, it was observed rather on SPIRITUAL level. And because of that Witkacy's quasi-dystopian works about Automatisation of lifes etc. are MORE Technocratic in feel than Queen Victorias' Court, her royal majesty agents and other Technocratic Unions resolving around world-wide empires (from Catholic Church to British Empire to NATO countries?).<br /> In polish intelligence class this was famous subject - slowly automatisation of our lifes just like in Brave New World of Huxley. And they were damn straight right (BANALITY overflow <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> There is so much damn potential that left huge holes in Changeling works.<br /> <br /> C:TD was really trying in many works to show the role of children in the world. Face it, the oldest grumps have like 30 years? And most changelings are kids or adolescenting people..<br /> <br /> Aaaaand... human history is full of children dreams and nightmares. Because of these nightmares changeling's biggest enemies should be nightmares themselves (just like werewolves overwhelmed by banes and fomori). Because I said about &quot;morality part&quot; - changeling may make kid happy or scare the shit out of him - it is still good for both seelie courts - he gained Glamour for the Dreaming's sake! &lt;3333 So they are psychopaths! How can I like a single changeling?!?!? They should be eradicated. They are only interested in their survival by all means, shit it if these must be happiness or nightmares. I don't get this. And still handbooks say about Seelie&amp;Unseelie friendship etc. Totally f**ked up :/<br /> <br /> And I totally see Sidhe in victorian and other ages. They were totally side by side with humans. Every age, period, gave so much ART to us! As I stated before...<br /> <br /> And War periods.. especially World War II. I think that this is the thing that leaves many nightmares inside dreaming stuuf and faries themselves. They tried to wash children cries and tears (I speak from perspective of TOTALLY ruined Poland with death camps on our territories etc. - subject taken up by Shoah: Charnelhouses of Europe handbook for Wraith.). And that left many bad things into spiritual aura of these lands to THIS VERY DAY.<br /> <br /> May I show you?<br /> Let me show you.<br /> <br /> This is Teresa: <a href=\"http://img7.demotywatoryfb.pl//uploads/201301/1359103219_ak0m2n_600.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://img7.demotywatoryfb.pl//uploa...ak0m2n_600.jpg</a> girl who grew up in the concentration camp. Asked about drawing her home, she drawed *this*<br /> Young 20 y.old. people who fought in war just after their PROMs, wrote really sad poetry (just like K.K.Baczy\u0144ski). Children dreams in many countries are just like that. I don't see good fairies in the Gaza Zone. I see only invisible friends who take the children away from War Reality just like Pan did in Pan's Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> Let me show you something more. Not again Teresa-like-child, but grown up man, who is not so famous, but well known in artistic world. A painter. Beksi\u0144ski. Just google him <a href=\"https://www.google.pl/search?client=opera&amp;q=beksi\u0144ski&amp;sourceid=opera&amp;ie=UTF-8&amp;oe=UTF-8\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.pl/search?client=...UTF-8&amp;oe=UTF-8</a><br /> I'm not saying that afterwar period of PRL (People's Republic of Poland, socialist country) was some kind of really terrible one. No, it was quite good and happy as our fathers and mothers remember, despite what you may read or hear from anti-commies shouters and from TV ladies.<br /> But still, existence maybe was somehow bleak and blanc (maybe because country was rebuilding itself from the very zero???!). But still, this is again a period not of futurism and fears of futurism like interwar period, but again, quite-romanticism, quite-modernism, gray, somehow sad, and changelings would be seen only by really drunk people (which isn't specially rare in Poland since very old times <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> But stilll, reflections about civilisation as a whole are stored in Beksi\u0144ski's works. You just watch them. Half of this stuff are like Wraith: The Oblivion. But if this is surreal reality showing the souls and moods of the people, then this is how changelings would be altered. From the very slavic versions of themselves...<br /> <br /> What after war then in your western countries?<br /> And, again, MURICA. If you wanted to show huge love and explosion of fairies in 1969, I think that psychodelic hippie and other flower-children movements are the better way to show why Glamour escalated quickly. Because of mankinds sickness of war.<br /> <br /> But in Middle East, Africa, latino-countries and Oceania... where children are soldiers (called bayaye - young boys who walk many kilometres from their home villages to find job in countries and the only thing they find are gangs of ravagers, rapists etc. with kalashnikovs and machete). These are places of tragedy and World of Darkness never ignored such themes. World of Darkness resolves around them and doesn't need to add more and more gothic mood to such places. And what Kithbook: Eshu says about Africa..? Nothing about it. Only Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom show kind of truth. Kind of.<br /> <br /> Not to mention genius book American Gods. I totally think that Dauntain are pretty dull, weak nihilists, suicidal babies. Why can't be give technocratical, anti-changeling changelings representing dull powers of reality (of the Weaver) like the Television fairies, Internet fairies, iPod fairies. Or whatever. Today kids are like Toy Story kids. Heads full of anime, games, pokemon collecting.. but still some part of my very soul longs for something primal.<br /> <br /> I won't surprise you if I tell you that my ideal type of girlfriend is Anne of the Green Gables? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This is the mood I would like to show playing for example in 1900 setting.. Changelings watch from old commodes and beds, they watch at babies fighting with pneumonia or pertussis in these hard times. And maybe... the children will *die*, but will awaken in the fairy land like in new game Child of Light? Or maybe.. they will fly over the window like in Peter Pan?<br /> <br /> Or maybe I went just too far...?<br /> <br /> But instintively I have seen in many changeling books that creators wanted to give something like this, but didn't exactly knew how. C:TD game-line is one of the most chaotic in searching for the right mood. That means this is ambitious one.<br /> <br /> Glad if you like my writing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-02-2014, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T09:39:09-07:00","id":216781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And changelings? Fighting for children dreams? Nope, they do not do that really at al... And childrens are the future of the nation. (In magyckal terms - children are tabula rasa which will form the future consensus..)</div> </div> </div> </div>They fight for the Dreaming, Magic and Belief not only for the children but for all. Although Changeling is tied rather strongly to age it is not actually about age but about loss of faith and belief in the world and wonder. It's about fighting Banality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that changelings are really like capricious kids which work all about romance, boo-boo and everything that creates Glamour. Rather than metaploting 1969 Moon Landing I would rather want to see that fairies were always by mankind side.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about kids nearly at all, it's about creativity and imagination and is tied to kids only because kids tend to have those things in abundance. But yes it is about Romance, which actually is normally really not an area that much touches kids as it does include very adult themes of sexuality and relationships, Adventure, Wonder, Fear, Horror, Terror and Joy, it's about all of these things as is life but colored with much starker colors and greater contrast. In Changeling the colors are brighter but that brings with it the fact that shadows are also deeper and the black is blacker. Glamour is created from our Dreams and Nightmares both, it comes from our sense of wonder as surely as our sense of terror.<br /> Also the Fae have always been with mankind, only the Sidhe took a small hiatus from earthly affairs for about 600 or so years and not even all the Sidhe just most of them. So fear not the Fae have always been there and will always be there as long as there exists some creativity, some belief and some small amount of imagination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Medieval folklore, rennaissance (Sheakspeare works) and romanticism (Geothe before and dark fairies in Blake, Poe, Blackwood works... which resulted in gothic and victorian works, faries alongside with victorian spiritualism which Wraith: The Oblivion acquired and Changeling DIDNT <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's a HUGE HOLE in historii od changelings) and modernism/fin de siecl + in periods &lt;3</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really following oyur point here, the Changelings are present during these times, in the medieval they were even much much stronger. Then Banality struck it's deadly blow sundering the Dreaming further away from the Autumn Lands and even through those dark times Changelings were there, even the Sidhe but in smaller numbers. Changeling got it's DA book in DA:Fae even though it uses a completely different, if awesome, system, with the systems only weak point lying in the echo system but that is a discussion for another thread. Still the Victorian age was an age that the Sluagh took as their own, still many of them prefer dress of those times, and it was a good time for Nockers as well who were delighted by the industrial Glamour of steam technology many of their seelie members still hold on to those times not only in their use of steam but also in their aestethic sense. I see no huge hole here, in Changeling history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention awesome Interwar Period (Lovecraft and his Unknown Kadath Quest about DREAMLANDS ? Lovecraft who was inspired by Poe and Blackwood works? Not to mention Howards' Hyborian age, which also inspired these works (they exchanged letters between themselves).)</div> </div> </div> </div>Again see above, I'm sure quite a few Changelings, as well as Thallain, drank deeply of the Dark Glamour born of works of Lovecraft, Poe and others. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own country (Poland) also has awesome writers or romanticism (A.Mickiewicz, K.C.Norwid, J. S\u0142owacki called Three Prophets, and Krasi\u0144ski who wrote fatalistic Non-Divine Comedy.) and in Interwar Period Witkacy. In mostly rural Poland after regaining independence from Russia, Germany and Austria, this wasn't country of technology like France, Germany, England, but still futurism, technologism and other this stuff was really vibrant in these days Warsaw, Cracov, Gda\u0144sk (and Gdynia was exploding city of young, beautiful people - such was it called.) This futurism was embraced in many dramas and works, but despite lacking of technological advancement like western countries, it was observed rather on SPIRITUAL level. And because of that Witkacy's quasi-dystopian works about Automatisation of lifes etc. are MORE Technocratic in feel than Queen Victorias' Court, her royal majesty agents and other Technocratic Unions resolving around world-wide empires (from Catholic Church to British Empire to NATO countries?).<br /> In polish intelligence class this was famous subject - slowly automatisation of our lifes just like in Brave New World of Huxley. And they were damn straight right (BANALITY overflow <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to say I'm not quite getting what you mean as your point here. That people took technology as a new awe inspiring thing? If so that is again times where Nockers would have thrived, and likely did. Changeling is unfortunately one of the most America sentric in it's setting though leaving us little information about how things went in the Old World, but technology that inspires one's imagination is a source of Glamour like any other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is so much damn potential that left huge holes in Changeling works.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I agree with, with the loss of Book of Glamour and Keys to Kingdom and the lack of a a lot of material from Europe and elsewhere much potential was lost. Much of this is strongly tied to not getting a Revised edition as those times were when WW started to expand it's source books to places that had these kind of holes. Still this allowed us to make European Kingdoms to our liking, apart from some rather loose guidelines found in The Fool's Luck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">C:TD was really trying in many works to show the role of children in the world. Face it, the oldest grumps have like 30 years? And most changelings are kids or adolescenting people..</div> </div> </div> </div>Like said it was about children but not exclusively. Considering how time is subjective, somewhat, in the Dreaming and how even the Freeholds tend to halt the aging of Changelings, with plenty of NPC nobles especially who were around since the moon landing and yet shoved little to no signs of slipping to Banality. Still like said multiple times even in this thread CtD did suffer somewhat from a certain type of ageism but as has been presented here on the forums a few times at the least that would be easy matter to correct. Just detach Changeling stages of life from age completely and attach them to one's Banality instead.<br /> Still most changelings being so young brings another type of horror to the table. After all which is more horrifying getting your arm bitten of by a monster disguised as a normal adult or by one that has disguised itself as a child? The Unseelie Childlings are your Damien Thorns where as the Seelie Childings are those who who do not shirk away from the monster closing in, when adults have already lost all composure as an impossible thing approaches, but stand in the way drawing his blade, where the hell did he get that sword anyway, and meeting the monster head on. Though I must say some Seelie may easily be just as creepy as Damien as there are traditions that need to be followed and not all traditions are that suitable to modern sensibilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aaaaand... human history is full of children dreams and nightmares. Because of these nightmares changeling's biggest enemies should be nightmares themselves (just like werewolves overwhelmed by banes and fomori).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the Changelings are themselves both the Nightmares and the Dreams. They fight for the existence of both. Though sometimes enemies in the end both Dreams and Nightmares ally themselves against the forces of Banality which seeks to destroy both. The conflict between Dreams and Nightmares continues as a sort of cold war between the Seelie and Unseelie, Kith and Thallain, Tuatha and Fomorian but still both sides tend to agree on one thing Banality has to be stopped. Though they do disagree of methods as seen in the differences between the Seelie and Unseelie codes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I said about &quot;morality part&quot; - changeling may make kid happy or scare the shit out of him - it is still good for both seelie courts - he gained Glamour for the Dreaming's sake! &lt;3333</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Both Dreams and Nightmares are essential parts of both humanity and the Fae. Strengthening either one will strengthen the Dreaming as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they are psychopaths! How can I like a single changeling?!?!? They should be eradicated. They are only interested in their survival by all means, shit it if these must be happiness or nightmares. I don't get this. And still handbooks say about Seelie&amp;Unseelie friendship etc. Totally f**ked up :/</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a bit harsh. They are not psychopaths, well there might be a few amongst them but same can be said of humanity, but they do tend to think differently. Changeling condition is a bit unique for the True Fae are not in any manner human, they are forces of nature more than anything else. From a human perspective the True Fae may seem deranged even when they are not, they merely follow a different way of thinking as they are not human. Changelings on the other hand are human, at least partially. They are human and Fae and as such tend to be quite a bit more humane than the True Fae were. Still they do have that Fae mentality, can you really claim that a Red Cap is a psychopath for taking a bite out of someone? He is hunger incarnate, it is his nature. Still most control themselves quite well thanks to their human halves. It's a delicate balance. And about being only interested in their survival by all means, are we any different? How would humanity act if slowly suffocated into extinction? They would do what they must to survive, that is human nature, hell that is nature.<br /> Seelie and Unseelie Courts are balanced, they may not be the best of friends but they do get along, although politically they generally don't and currently are not that balanced either, but that is politics. Both Courts face a common enemy in Banality so it only makes sense that they put aside most open conflicts and unite their fronts.<br /> <br /> Besides the survival of the Changelings may actually be to humanitys advantage as they are the ones fighting for our Dreams as well, while our creativity and dreams may be food to them it still benefits us as well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I totally see Sidhe in victorian and other ages. They were totally side by side with humans. Every age, period, gave so much ART to us! As I stated before...</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct they were, at the least those of Houses Liam and Scathach were. Still most of them were absent during the Victorian ages and forward till the moon landing. CtD history would actually loose quite a bit if this were to be changed as it was the return of the Sidhe in great numbers that fired up the Accordance War. As posited by the Fool's Luck this war was pretty damn global as everywhere the Sidhe were returning and as they did they were intent on reclaiming their places as the rulers of Fae society.<br /> May I ask what art are you referring to that has to have been from Sidhe origins instead of another Kith? Or even Muse Adhene inspired?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And War periods.. especially World War II. I think that this is the thing that leaves many nightmares inside dreaming stuuf and faries themselves. They tried to wash children cries and tears (I speak from perspective of TOTALLY ruined Poland with death camps on our territories etc. - subject taken up by Shoah: Charnelhouses of Europe handbook for Wraith.). And that left many bad things into spiritual aura of these lands to THIS VERY DAY.</div> </div> </div> </div>True both World Wars were horrific things and though they may have spawned their share of Nightmares they did way more for Banality. War on this scale particularly crushes dreams and nightmares alike, leaving people traumatized enough that they see no dreams at all. Their spirits are crushed into complete hopelessness instead of inspired or horrified to new heights of imagination. They do not see monsters in the dark corners of the world they see only sorrow and death. The aftermath of the war may inspire Nightmares again after people have somewhat recovered from the numbness inflicted therein but the wars themselves were quite Banal indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is Teresa: <a href=\"http://img7.demotywatoryfb.pl//uploads/201301/1359103219_ak0m2n_600.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://img7.demotywatoryfb.pl//uploa...ak0m2n_600.jpg</a> girl who grew up in the concentration camp. Asked about drawing her home, she drawed *this*</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd call that quite Banal indeed, and quite sad. It shows that she lacks even the imagination to give any sort of face to her pain, it's all a mess. She is a girl in pain who has lost much of her self in the horrors of the war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Young 20 y.old. people who fought in war just after their PROMs, wrote really sad poetry (just like K.K.Baczy\u0144ski). Children dreams in many countries are just like that. I don't see good fairies in the Gaza Zone. I see only invisible friends who take the children away from War Reality just like Pan did in Pan's Labyrinth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like said not all Fae are good, or evil for that matter. The Fae themselves are kinda amoral where as Changelings tend to move a lot more on that scale. Another good movie about the Fae is Don't be Afraid of the Dark it showcases what some might think as evil Fae but they are more or less merely following their nature. Still even in those places, like Gaza, childen and adults alike still cling to hope and can still imagine better times and so both Courts are represented.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me show you something more. Not again Teresa-like-child, but grown up man, who is not so famous, but well known in artistic world. A painter. Beksi\u0144ski. Just google him <a href=\"https://www.google.pl/search?client=opera&amp;q=beksi\u0144ski&amp;sourceid=opera&amp;ie=UTF-8&amp;oe=UTF-8\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.pl/search?client=...UTF-8&amp;oe=UTF-8</a><br /> I'm not saying that afterwar period of PRL (People's Republic of Poland, socialist country) was some kind of really terrible one. No, it was quite good and happy as our fathers and mothers remember, despite what you may read or hear from anti-commies shouters and from TV ladies.<br /> But still, existence maybe was somehow bleak and blanc (maybe because country was rebuilding itself from the very zero???!). But still, this is again a period not of futurism and fears of futurism like interwar period, but again, quite-romanticism, quite-modernism, gray, somehow sad, and changelings would be seen only by really drunk people (which isn't specially rare in Poland since very old times <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> But stilll, reflections about civilisation as a whole are stored in Beksi\u0144ski's works. You just watch them. Half of this stuff are like Wraith: The Oblivion. But if this is surreal reality showing the souls and moods of the people, then this is how changelings would be altered. From the very slavic versions of themselves...</div> </div> </div> </div>Again I'm somewhat at loss of what you are trying to say here, are you saying that his art is proof of Glamour existing even in the bleakest times? Or are you trying to say that the Fae should have changed somehow to resemble that art? For the first one the answer is yes, there is Glamour often even in the darkest most banal times but it is rare and precious and those Changelings gathering around it will do their utmost to savor that spark and try to fan it to flames that could spread amongts the people.<br /> For the latter matter I ask you why? Why would you think that such short times should somehow morph the very nature of the Fae themselves? Surely these times may give birth to new Nightmare Chimerae but to alter the Kiths themselves? That is a bit much. The Kiths, and their Thallain counterparts as well as Adhene etc. tend to personify concepts and these core concepts that have birthed whole species of Fae to cling to themselves are very strong. Passions and Lusts of a Satyr may change in time but the fact that they personify Passion and Lust does not, Sluagh are the things in the dark, the sounds that make our hearts race, they are the boogie men under the beds and in our closets while what we fear may change the Sluagh generally do not as they are the personifications of our Fear of the unknown and unseen, Red Caps are hunger incarnate, they are the biting cold wind that seems to eat you alive in the winter this will not change especially after war time when food is scarce, the Sidhe are our nobles hopes and dreams but htey are also hte tyranny of those in power again there is little in these times that could change such core concepts. etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanted to show huge love and explosion of fairies in 1969, I think that psychodelic hippie and other flower-children movements are the better way to show why Glamour escalated quickly. Because of mankinds sickness of war.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this may have sparked some Glamour in mankind it was only a part of mankind that was touched by this, the hippie movement wasn't that far spread or that huge in the end where as the moon landing touched whole of humanity. It sparked our imaginations as we achieved something impossible, a man walking on moon. If that was possible what else could be? The world was again open to the possibilities that the future might bring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in Middle East, Africa, latino-countries and Oceania... where children are soldiers (called bayaye - young boys who walk many kilometres from their home villages to find job in countries and the only thing they find are gangs of ravagers, rapists etc. with kalashnikovs and machete). These are places of tragedy and World of Darkness never ignored such themes. World of Darkness resolves around them and doesn't need to add more and more gothic mood to such places. And what Kithbook: Eshu says about Africa..? Nothing about it. Only Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom show kind of truth. Kind of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again war like this is Banal not inspiring. They are a tragedy but WW writers were not that familiar with Africa and so, perhaps wisely, detained from writing that much about it. It's a shame that Africa got so little material in WoD but still especially in CtD I would have preferred more material on Europe first before trying to open up Africa.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention genius book American Gods. I totally think that Dauntain are pretty dull, weak nihilists, suicidal babies. Why can't be give technocratical, anti-changeling changelings representing dull powers of reality (of the Weaver) like the Television fairies, Internet fairies, iPod fairies. Or whatever. Today kids are like Toy Story kids. Heads full of anime, games, pokemon collecting.. but still some part of my very soul longs for something primal.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does American Gods have to do with this? Dauntain are dull by their very nature, they are those lost into service of Banality after all, and that wya lies only nothingness so yes they are also suicidal. Makes them no less dangerous though, or horrifying.<br /> Technocratic anti-changeling changelings? You mean Changelings interested in Technology? That we have Unseelie Nockers are the Changelings that embrace new technology and give it that extra push beyond common laws of science and into sci-fi territory. And the rest of the Kiths are just as able to take up the internet and I doubt there are that many stubborn old goats that I couldn't say that most Satyrs likely walk around with an iPod. These things are not dull, for that you have Banality and the Dauntain which you yourself admitted as being dull, in themselves they can be used to inspire and most of those oyu gave as examples are actually a food for inspiration to millions. They can be dull and Banal if used that way but in the end they are just tools like plows and swords of days past, it's more a matter of how than what.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216635#post216635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But instintively I have seen in many changeling books that creators wanted to give something like this, but didn't exactly knew how. C:TD game-line is one of the most chaotic in searching for the right mood. That means this is ambitious one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling is about inspiration, imagination, fear and joy. It's about life. And it is about magic. It's all these things and more, it's about madness of dreams and insanity of banality. And you are quite correct it is an ambitious one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T14:53:14-07:00","id":216957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. First, the Dreaming deserves being renovated. In my country (Poland) for example the big three (Werewolf, Vampire, Mage) are totally popular games and both Wraith and Changeling (not to mention smaller games) are totally unknown to most players. What's more, Changeling: The Lost won the audience and gained really large fame. If somebody talks about Changeling, he thinks about The Lost. People laugh at Dreaming and don't even get this, but still main statement is such that Dreaming has zero gloom, dark of World of Darkness and WoD players love creepy and dark fairy tales, Pan's Labirynth etc. so they insist on The Lost as being best Changeling game and that The Dreaming is not worth even reading. And the reading probably often turns them off even if they are really curious about changelings. </div> </div> </div>I think it has to do with the fact that, at least in my generation, Warhammer Fantasy Roleplay is THE Roleplay, and its popularity shaped expectations of the roleplayers. I will only say I'm not fond of Dreaming, but I at least read the book before reading Lost and judged both IMO fairly, without 'NWoD bias'.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T15:20:25-07:00","id":217010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216957#post216957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it has to do with the fact that, at least in my generation, Warhammer Fantasy Roleplay is THE Roleplay, and its popularity shaped expectations of the roleplayers. I will only say I'm not fond of Dreaming, but I at least read the book before reading Lost and judged both IMO fairly, without 'NWoD bias'.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not the first time you bring up WHFRP and while I have somewhat hard time seeing how it ties to either Changeling games, other than trying to tie Chaos Gods into representing the True Fae of both games in which case I see little difference between the games except that CtL actually has rules for the True Fae whereas CtD does not, unless one wants to claim DA:Fae Fae as the True Fae of cWoD. I too can generally find more common ground with how the True Fae are represented in Lost but since they are mostly unplayable, except if you have a truly exceptionally trusting ST who let's you play one, I have to compare which Changelings I like better and for me the Dreaming Kiths, Thallain and Adhene just have so much more pull than the Seeming/Kith system of Lost. Don't get me wrong I love Lost but I love Dreamings Kiths et al more. As for which game I favour? Both. I truly cannot decide, I've even toyed with the idea of trying to pull Dreaming, Lost and DA:Fae systems together take the best of each and run with that but for now I tend to choose which one I ST on either a whim, player request or according to whatever crazy idea I happen to harbor at that time.<br /> <br /> Ah, but now for my actual question before I forget.<br /> <br /> Which edition of WHFRP are you referring to? I have the 1986 1st edition and have used some 2nd edition material with it, like the Children of the Horned Rat, and it meshes nicely but the third edition by Fantasy Flight Games is just weird and alien to me, and likely completely incompatible with the earlier material. So just to satisfy my curiosity which edition are you referring to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T16:37:11-07:00","id":217051,"title":"","content":"I'd love to read the responses on my bad english<br /> Will try to catch up!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216781#post216781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling condition is a bit unique for the True Fae are not in any manner human, they are forces of nature more than anything else. From a human perspective the True Fae may seem deranged even when they are not, they merely follow a different way of thinking as they are not human.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point my dear. You surely noticed that every single supernatural in the World of Darkness who is intended as protagonist IS partially human. 50% of his life is normal and 50% supernatural. Vampires, werewolfs, mages, changelings, demons and hunters even are ripped apart by their dual-lives, but this is the way we can understand them, emphasize them, and what's most important - understand as a humans their needs and then later role-play it, so we can see their aspirations, motivations i natural manner. And that's the point I don't naturally see changelings.<br /> Well.. by things you said earlier about the children and Seelie vs Unseelie both accepting that banality is worst enemy... then the Dreaming isn't about being psychopaths... but about maintaining something like... the theatre? Like totally in Neverending Story where magic land was eaten by nothingness. Let's push away nothingness, we need fairies who will create nightmares and then defeat these nightmares because that's what mankind neeeeeds - to see and watch it and see good winning evil. Really? So being an unseelie faerie would be like &quot;Okay, I'm kind of scapegoat, yay...&quot;<br /> <br /> I really want to believe it other way, but still I got problems. There is something really inconsistent when I am thinking about their motivations, sense and morality.<br /> Or is it rather - we all want to keep Dreaming alive in human hearts, but by the way we want to make the Dreaming looking in our way! (and Seelie want it ice creams&amp;teddy bears and Unseelie want it nightmares and sweet anarchy. &quot;Glamour is free&quot; really sounds like Star Wars dark side of force.. :&gt; ).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216781#post216781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry to say I'm not quite getting what you mean as your point here. That people took technology as a new awe inspiring thing? If so that is again times where Nockers would have thrived, and likely did. Changeling is unfortunately one of the most America sentric in it's setting though leaving us little information about how things went in the Old World, but technology that inspires one's imagination is a source of Glamour like any other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I admit that was kind of chaotic. Was trying to explain in really intense shortcut about polish local varieties or European intellectual movements and ages like romanticism, enlightenment, modernism, interwar period etc. In this paragraph I wanted to explain that new Poland wasn't technological power at all, but futurism hopes and fears were also alive in our intelligence society class. And when Czech, German and Brithis works showed automatisation of lifes by replacing humans by machines (yeah), the polish ones were more psychological, sociological, about changes like in Orwell of Huxley visions, not quasi cyber-punk ones (If I can use that word to 20s ^^ ).<br /> <br /> And if in Mage: The Ascension we see paradigm by actual intellectual age (in interwar period Mages would be totally visionaries seeing golden cities and near-to-ascend mankind... just to be shocked by WW2 after which Nephandi would gather essence of fear and nihilism all around from the air) then The Dreaming is far more literall in this, right? Aaaand.. nope. Not at all. Changeling core book justified that this way that Sidhe being totally separated since medieval times... still have maintained medieval titles (knights, duchesses, kings, queens, pages etc.). Okay, that maybe makes sense, but still the Dreaming.. I don't know, but I feel something lacking there and being inconsistent. Or maybe I just feel sad about never used potential.<br /> <br /> And yes, I know Changeling described in few paragraphs about all his history since Mythic Age and kithbooks made up some more stories, but still these periods are holes. I have my imagination and can make up stories about victorian sluagh and faeries in interwar Warsaw, but that's not the point, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216781#post216781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This I agree with, with the loss of Book of Glamour and Keys to Kingdom and the lack of a a lot of material from Europe and elsewhere much potential was lost. Much of this is strongly tied to not getting a Revised edition as those times were when WW started to expand it's source books to places that had these kind of holes. Still this allowed us to make European Kingdoms to our liking, apart from some rather loose guidelines found in The Fool's Luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, some loose history and not ignoring part of the world east from Odra river would be very nice. Especially when Slavic culture is one of the hugest treasuries of fairies and folklore. (Same with bloodsuckers, werewolvs, pagan cults, witches, demons..).<br /> Just a few localisations. And I would be also very happy to read about Spanish faeries or Azure Coast faeries living in wineries, nymphs of Mediterranean countries etc. etc.<br /> I think this would help a lot with our thinking. Because the Dreaming conflict is not only US-centered, but also Seelie/Unseelie conflict. Maybe this conflict is not so important in old Europe which may have another courts (Slavic folklor doesn't have seelie/unseelie courts for faeries <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> despite C:T Lost talking about dualistic slavic faiths. Nope, it isn't dualistic at all. But still it is awfully rich. Every fairy tale is creepy and &quot;faeries&quot; are kind of psychopaths <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And faeries also merge with christian religious ideas side by side. The natural world equals spiritual words just like in werewolf (all Romanticism). And supernatural forces are sometimes faeries, sometimes ghosts of deceased (both evil malevolent spirits and white virgin ladies protecting the living..) Peasants in XIX century could be very religious and still afraid by night of faeries. Well, when in UK wiccan songs are lullabies for kids.. in Poland such things are demonized by the Church, but still demonizing it didn't change anything at all ^^. Stubborn nation.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216781#post216781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May I ask what art are you referring to that has to have been from Sidhe origins instead of another Kith? Or even Muse Adhene inspired?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just mean, not to offend commoners, but sidhe as a nobles, high-ups of society, the only ones who can be princesses, heirs of otherwordly kingdom (or little girls living in peasant hut one day discover they can go to the other world being a princess if they are brave enough to drown in the lake nearby... yeah nearly every work looks like Der Erlkonig).<br /> So really I am lacking of these high-ups in all these fascinatings ages I mentioned before.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216781#post216781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True both World Wars were horrific things and though they may have spawned their share of Nightmares they did way more for Banality. War on this scale particularly crushes dreams and nightmares alike, leaving people traumatized enough that they see no dreams at all. Their spirits are crushed into complete hopelessness instead of inspired or horrified to new heights of imagination. They do not see monsters in the dark corners of the world they see only sorrow and death. The aftermath of the war may inspire Nightmares again after people have somewhat recovered from the numbness inflicted therein but the wars themselves were quite Banal indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I didn't want to particularly grief my country, but to mention that old Europe is the world which had experienced awful lot of wars (and two totall world wars). And still conflicts like Jugoslavia, The Troubles, modern-day Ukraine.. aren't something civilized either. But we have to keep that in mind if we want to create dream-shaped kingdoms on these lands.<br /> <br /> And let's look at Concordia, at the USA. The last conflict on these lands was... eradication of native americans? Some horror at the Gettysburg? If somebody writes the mankind dreams from this perspective, if somebody write werewolf, nunnehi, native american myths from this perspective... I think it is missing a point when looking at the Europe which is more delicate matter.<br /> That's maybe an another reason why the Dreaming isn't everywhere the same (I mean, shouldn't, because suggestion is made that Europe is much like Concordia..).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216781#post216781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again I'm somewhat at loss of what you are trying to say here, are you saying that his art is proof of Glamour existing even in the bleakest times? Or are you trying to say that the Fae should have changed somehow to resemble that art?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am just wondering if Beksi\u0144ski's works are rather Dark Glamour source or so much nihilistic that this is huge chasm of Oblivion and Banality combined?<br /> Cause the rainbowy-Glamour thing is something still strange for me. Actually Hsien showed up that Glamour doesn't have to be rainbowy dream-stuff energy. Still we got an echo of teddybear Concordia in the background.<br /> Okay, I don't wanna to change kiths. Only changelings could be hm.. warped out? Damaged? Or maybe European countries have higher Banality starter rating for changelings? Dunno. I'm lot in this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216781#post216781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does American Gods have to do with this? Dauntain are dull by their very nature, they are those lost into service of Banality after all, and that wya lies only nothingness so yes they are also suicidal. Makes them no less dangerous though, or horrifying.<br /> Technocratic anti-changeling changelings? You mean Changelings interested in Technology? That we have Unseelie Nockers are the Changelings that embrace new technology and give it that extra push beyond common laws of science and into sci-fi territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, maybe I am too much lost in comparing mages consensus of mankind with mankind dreams (and I think both things evolve).<br /> Looks like due to Changeling, only consensus evolves, because fairies are frozen at the state of medieval times (handbook says they evolve to catch up with humans, that's why they evolved from tribal to kings).<br /> <br /> American Gods... let's say that gods in the book are like dream-made-stuff of faith (like in D&amp;D) and really change due to power of worship. True fae and changelings alike are somehow the same. So yes, I feel that new gods - media - would have their own Changelings. (Well, the Inanimae probably have Empire of Flickers which would be made of electronics and electricity Inanimae <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but this is digresion).<br /> <br /> Nope, I don't want changelings just interested in technology just like Nockers. I meant just the media. Media which according to the C:TD just dullify society and radiate with banality, cause they ease the proces of imagination (or lack thereof). But still TV is master of many souls by their shows. I wonder why there aren't faeries of TV (cause there aren't much spirits from W:TA of this.<br /> <br /> And another thing.<br /> I wonder if these are mankind dreams which give the Dreaming existence and form so the true fae are made from human dreams (then wars should have huge impact on changelings, not only chimeras etc, which are obvious things) or the Dreaming exists without mankind dreams and souls and only human believing opens trods to Arcadia and let the magic sink in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216781#post216781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd call that quite Banal indeed, and quite sad. It shows that she lacks even the imagination to give any sort of face to her pain, it's all a mess. She is a girl in pain who has lost much of her self in the horrors of the war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting point. Just like killing the childhood kills every magic and impair human ability to dream. Thiniking this way it would be just &quot;banal&quot;, despite the images, lurking terror and huge emotions (which banal people lack) behind it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=216781#post216781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've even toyed with the idea of trying to pull Dreaming, Lost and DA:Fae systems together take the best of each and run with that but for now I tend to choose which one I ST on either a whim</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, people are comparing C:TD and C:TL the most of any games. I think of these &quot;little wars&quot; a &quot;Changeling Translation Guide&quot; might arise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T16:58:47-07:00","id":217061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is not the first time you bring up WHFRP </div> </div> </div>No, I mean that WHFRP's popularity has something to do why Polish players like darker settings. It claimed the nascent market before larger titles like DnD came here (though I know few DnD fans, they are not unheard for) that there are many people who are simply into darker settings than Changeling: Dreaming. I also noted that our own RP settings like Monastyr, Neuroshima, The Witcher RP and Dzikie Pola tend to be on darker spectrum. <br /> <br /> WHFRP's fairie like equivalents are so rare as the element of the setting of Warhammer (mostly localised spirits and elementals that are sometimes part of Wood Elves armies if dangerous enough) that I don't make any comparison since it is moot point. <br /> <br /> I would not recommend tying Chaos Gods with anything Changeling related, since they only make sense when you compare them to the Wyrm Triat and Wyld, as the Four embody concepts that can find parallels with those entities. I heard people joking that Apocalypse is '40K with Werewolves', and while The Wyrm Triat and Chaos are not identical, you could read Chaos Domainw supplements for cool stuff to put when exploring Malfeas, or read Book of Wyrm to spice up your Warhammer sessions.<br /> <br /> As of your question, all three have their following. 1st kickstarted it all, people then moved on to 2nd, and there is a division between those who like 2nd and 3rd. 3rd is really incompatible since it's mechanics is different and it's pre-Storm of Chaos like 1st, but if you have money (it's expensive given whole extra dices and props the core and expansions contain) it's still good thing to try out. But I'm not exactly rich, so I don't own 3rd, I just read good reviews about the changes.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my personal view was always that fae in any RP game serve better as NPCs and antagonists, since in folk legends they are often beings beyond human understanding, so alienness should be a major theme at least when devising faries in setting. Though, since it's Changeling as title, I could imagine sort of existential horror line involving neither fae in human bodies as in Dreaming take nor people kidnapped by fae as in Lost take, but classic Changelings. Beings put in place of the children commonly kidnapped by fae. There could be something disturbing for such PCs in realizing you are not actually a human and just a doppelganger of somebody or that you should have not existed in this world, while being confused about who you really are (and the raised question why some inscrutable beings actually take human children to replace them with their not quite human copies. Let it remain enigma to make people guessing). But that could be something appropiate for New New World of Darkness when some day there will be a third iteration of WoD and creators will again go for some different take than the previous two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T18:31:11-07:00","id":217099,"title":"","content":"I used to love checking on this thread because it was discussing what a Changeling 20th Anniversary book could have as far as what we wished and possible stretch goals. It was a thread more about what got us excited about Changeling as a system. Now it's become more of a critique full of posts on how people think Changeling FAILED as a system. I don't think such posts belong here. Lets please move this discussion back on topic and hope that new people coming to see this thread don't quit reading because it's not about the topic. This isn't a comparison between Dreaming and Lost. Such comparisons may get this thread closed.<br /> <br /> As for Changeling 20th. We'd all like to see the holes in the system get patched. But better than just tweaking the system to work it more of the revision it deserved and never got, how can we expand it to be even better? There's the Grimm Darkness of fae like <i>Pan's Labyrinth</i> and there's the Disney flavor most think of when people say Changeling, and yet there's so much more diversity in legends that Changeling as a system barely scratched the surface, and granted one of it's weaknesses is the fact that it's very Eurocentric. So how about we post legends and creatures we'd use as inspiration and beings we'd use among the Fae of Changeling for what they might bring to the game?<br /> <br /> Lunar mentioned American Gods, but I'm more inclined to use<b> The Sandman</b> world as inspiration for my Changeling games and characters. The entire series is all about the stories of individuals binding reality together and their lives affecting the Dreaming world though they themselves may never know it. All of Human creativity and potential is expressed in a mere graphic series that most would overlook for lack of action or superpowers. Yet I found it to be one of the most thought provoking and inspiring series of writings of my life. When I think about what Glamour is, I think of what The Sandman series has shown me. When I think of the struggle in what being a changeling in modern times must be, I think of <i>Barbie</i> and her fantasy world. When I imagine what being a Duke or Duchess of a realm must be, I think of <i>Morpheus</i> and the weight of his responsibility at war with the need to be admired and loved all while being in control of a vast realm of pure creativity and all that inhabit it. When I imagine Bedlam in a Changeling, I think of <i>Delirium</i> and all her frightening madness, yet somewhere in her mismatched eyes is strength and wisdom few know exists. Changeling is at it's core I think, about the layers of potential that humanity has to go in ANY direction, from the sweetest dreams of cotton candy castles in the sky, to the horrors of night terrors. What Changeling is meant to teach about these extremes is the balance needed by anyone to survive in this world. From the Human and Fae soul coexisting, to the Seelie and Unseelie within us all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T21:23:28-07:00","id":217166,"title":"","content":"I'm all for seeing this stay focused on CtD and C20... but I think the critiques of the old system have a place here. V20 and W20's open development phases had plenty of critiques of their systems discussed. Some of that even ended up in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T22:29:40-07:00","id":217181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=217166#post217166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for seeing this stay focused on CtD and C20... but I think the critiques of the old system have a place here. V20 and W20's open development phases had plenty of critiques of their systems discussed. Some of that even ended up in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's plenty of other threads specifically asking for critiques of Changeling the Dreaming as a system to choose from. (Or have you forgotten your very own thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/79695-my-probelm-with-changeling\">My Problem with Changeling</a>) You even state &quot;I know that there's a C20 thread right now that's gone off tangent a bit towards this, but I felt that I'd rather start a new thread instead of risking derailing that one further.&quot;<br /> <br /> Shall we follow your advice then? Lets not let this sink into another one of those debates and keep people from sharing what people would like to see in a Changeling 20th anniversary edition.<br /> <br /> Back to preconceptions and ideas for Changeling 20th Anniversary:<br /> <br /> I have fervent hopes that Changeling can be resurrected and brought to its full potential or at least fuller potential than it was given in Second edition. It really needs a unified written treatment. Changeling suffered from a lot of different artistic and system directions and more than just a laundry list of mechanics that need straightening out or things that need fixing, I think there's a hopefulness at the heart of Changeling. The feel of it is important. Just as Werewolf 20 was meant to capture a certain spirit that all gamers and fans felt in Second edition, and then felt was missing by revised. There's a certain suspension of disbelief that Changeling 20 will need, as elusive an essence as Changelings are themselves. I felt that the best Changeling games and storytellers kept one foot in the realm of fantasy and the other foot firmly in the realm of plausibility. The Loony Toons type reality of the Dreaming and all things Chimerical were carefully hidden and not slathered on with a trowel. And yet, that place of anything being possible was still much more accessible than the rule books of Changeling would have it. I hope that access to the Dreaming and those wonders would be as reachable to Fae as the Umbra is to Garou or at least as reachable as a Mage can touch the Spirit world. It'd be a precarious sort of balance to make the Dreaming and all its dangers so near at hand and the Players might favor playing around in High fantasy more than the cold world of reality and mortals, but then again... isn't everything about changeling revolving around that balancing act? In for a penny, in for a pound, I say.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T22:46:31-07:00","id":217192,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">I just finished reviewing this thread; and to be fair, from page one, there have been critiques of the game. It\u2019s not a recent development.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">That said, there has also been a push from early on to keep this thread focused on revisions and enhancements to CtD as it is, as opposed to wholesale reimaginings of the game. So please try to approach this thread with the mindset of \u201cCtD is a pretty good game as is, but it has a few areas where it can be improved\u201d rather than\u201cCtD is fundamentally broken, and needs equally fundamental changes to make it viable\u201d. This is mainly because I\u2019m pretty sure that whoever gets the CtD20 assignment will be using the former mindset; so to the extent that this thread is speculation about C20, the former is much more on-topic than the latter.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">For example: <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b> is a great game; and I would love to see an adaptation of it to modern days. But that wouldn\u2019t be C20, and ought to be discussed in a separate topic.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T23:25:06-07:00","id":217224,"title":"","content":"Thank you Dataweaver. I'm hoping that perhaps Phil Brucato will be the one to make a Changeling 20th Anniversary edition. He's recently been spotted at the Oregon festival called <a href=\"http://youtu.be/ZxAZ1HokSIE\" target=\"_blank\">Faerieworlds</a> this last end of July weekend. If having the name Satyros wasn't enough, he's been involved in a lot of other Changeling-ish <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deliria\" target=\"_blank\">projects</a>. I just hope he's not too worn out and otherwise engaged by the time Changeling 20th will get rolling.<br /> <br /> As for <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b>... there was a thread expressing the love (and some critiques) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53897-dark-ages-fae\">here.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T00:39:42-07:00","id":217259,"title":"","content":"I suspect that Phil is going to have his hands full with the M20 line for some time to come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T01:41:31-07:00","id":217264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=217166#post217166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example: <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b> is a great game; and I would love to see an adaptation of it to modern days. But that wouldn\u2019t be C20, and ought to be discussed in a separate topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You got the point there. And still let me guide you. I think you can guess why Fae is so distant from modern Changeling, not only because of the running of ages. It felt these fundamental changes. Somebody learn on this. I still want Neverending Story Fantasia, Child of Light Lemuria and Narnia and Oz. Actually I would like to visit Oz..<br /> Not as fundamental as just creating another C:TL, no.<br /> <br /> Just to make this game a little more playable. The idea with fairy kingdoms just behind every doorstep, corner, (just like magic train to Hogwarts) or maybe sluagh underground kingdoms (being in quasi-real, quasi-dreaming reality, somewhere there) and other stuff. Maybe my problems resolve around mechanics - as did Darling Rose say. I want to create a vision, what my players also want, they want private kingdoms, but not a single one being a Freehold by definition with holy balefire of glamour in the centre. So I must guess that every fairy tale and fairy-games (I like to mention Child of Light and Pan's Labirynth both cause they are new and recognized) where there were faeries households/kingdoms/realms, there should be everywhere a balefire.<br /> That's what the players didnt like in every WoD game - pointing out something that &quot;must totally be there&quot;, politics with Archons and Princes etc. mess-up. We don't even know how balefire looks like (I guess its rainbowy fire). How about writing a paragraph: balefire is just a name, it can take many different forms and just remains &quot;center place of power in the Freehold&quot;, it can be glowing crystal or sacred tree or... This isnt a fundamental change and I think it is more WoD'ish - I mean, easily translateable into every culture or book, fairy tale, game, movie based ideas. Just like VTM, VTA and MTA do it on regular basis with no problem about &quot;fundamentals&quot;.<br /> Uff.. that's what I meant. Game is too much anglo-saxon like no other and if the changelings didn't emigrate to the US, it would be playable only on the British Isles <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But yeah, everything major happens in the US. Or, to make it major, let it happen in the US <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's not called in literature walking a shortcut. It is damn teleporattion.<br /> Okay, let there be High King David. Okay, let there be Kingdoms (and laaarge nothingness&amp;ice kingdom of canada). Do and precise them nicely or leave it alone. Vampire players know the anarch-cammy-sabat map of US dot by dot, city by city and it is described a way that doesn't make it hard. These geo-politcal thing just need a work and thankfully it doesnt attack the fundamentals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=217166#post217166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for seeing this stay focused on CtD and C20... but I think the critiques of the old system have a place here. V20 and W20's open development phases had plenty of critiques of their systems discussed. Some of that even ended up in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe this is my polish character of nation of whining grown-ups <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The more you criticize something means the more you want it to get superb. C:TD deserves bigger audience and many of us speak with words of fandom, why many people walked by C:TD didn't even trying to read it. And those who tried - found it difficult to understand, imagine (yeah, we all are tainted by banality, role-players, huh? ;D ) and even play. Every WoD setting is credible somehow and motivations of changelings are maybe too alien for us to understand or maybe there are too many inconsistencies, mutual contradictions etc. We tried to point them out - and - if this is somehow possible, to rewrite them in the way that easies the process to understand The Dreaming. Everybody catches up Vampire mood, damnation etc.<br /> <br /> If you try to compare C:TD to many fairy stories your acquaintances know (or Play By Forum players as larger audience) you really must mostly depend on their own imagination. And theen... surprise, someone wanted to create their fancy idea and somehow Kiths are problematic (not making it impossible though) to create variety of changelings. But still, Kiths got their opinion not from the thin air, right?<br /> <br /> And WW while writing another and another books went onto a road of inventing more and more kiths and faeries. That's probably the good stuff.<br /> Maybe if meta-plot will go away, nobody will think about dreaming-storms and Ravana..<br /> <br /> The 1969 is cool idea, but still it locks sidhe from many plummy ages of soul and reason alike. Why couldn't it be like &quot;sidhe maybe were there.. but due to big banality they were nearly extinct on earth... and sometime occurencing fluxes of Glamour made by single acts of imagination (I don't know, maybe the founding of Walt Disney ? :&gt; ). And Dauntain entirely are lacking moralizing priests (That's a strong political and moral force influencing people since kids in eastern Europe.).<br /> <br /> If not, it says to me that Romanticism was a Banal period, same with Victorian Age (I prefer calling it Enlightenment because it reaches all world with colonies) and Modernism. If this happens this way - I'd like to see in handbook history why this happens this way. How to interpretate this. I'm not telling this is totally bad :s<br /> <br /> And yes, I know of the golden rule, and I can alone create Eastern Europe, Third World, in any age and modify Kiths to local attributes and local names of local people and boom, I got polish or otherwise Changeling withouth focus and roots of anglo-saxon, wiccan, celtic mysticism (this is powerfuly felt when somebody wants not only translate british, welsh, scottish faeries into their own language and reality which is cultularly totally different, even names and translation are warped out. As I said before, most &quot;faeries&quot; terms are demonized due to high Church influence. And that's why (as did Katsura say) we are the source of many dark games. Maybe we are just retarded in some feelings and can't catch up the Changeling with it's vivid colours, more intense than a Rio canival. But I stated at the begining of my posts that I tell from perspective of polish and potentially nearly everyone who is in country distributing WoD games but outside anglo-saxon area of culture, but still not Asian (which many handbooks do forget <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> So yeah, I know of the golden rule, but we, wod-fans are masters of the Lore, right?<br /> <br /> A small hint why the great 3 are so loved games out there in Poland. Because in Poland only Vampire was released in 2nd and revised edition (the later is famous but only Core Book, all Sabbats, Hunters Hunted etc. are 2nd edition). And both Werewolf and Mage are of 2nd edition. The newest handbooks would be KotE. And of course fans who must go deeeper, find out other games and the problems arise. Everything agrees with that the second edition feel was the spirit every gamer wished.<br /> <br /> What's a big digression if fact that I am big fan of Mummy and the Demon (and maybe a little of Hunter) and I was forced to use the golden rule and re-create meta-plot so there won't be any maelstroms and ends of the world in the demon (God, religious horror is one of the most potent things. Another game with unused potential). But this is really another thread and I'm afraid a really far away future.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=217181#post217181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really needs a unified written treatment. Changeling suffered from a lot of different artistic and system directions and more than just a laundry list of mechanics that need straightening out or things that need fixing, I think there's a hopefulness at the heart of Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mentioned about mechanics earlier. Rather problems with interpretation and localising the Changeling theme (which is not hard and kind of intuitional if somebody wants to localise in their land a big 3 V,W,M and fairy tale theme should also be that easy without doing much homework).<br /> But to the pure mechanics.. I heard there were collecting cards to the very 1st ed. of C:TD. Looks like it wasn't that succeful, but still I think making something like a tarot spread is awesome. If the bunks are some kind of a game... then placing and choosing the cards and combining them at the game session would be also funny and *bunky*. People say it destroyed imagination and options were too limited. Well, after 20 years there were so many games (I once played a game which had only 6 dice cubes with icons on their sides - and how they well rolled, that's the way someone invented a fairy tale going from concept to concept. And I think with almost 200 cards of old C:TD it shouldnt be that problematic to give abstract ideas, catch-ups etc. I guess so.<br /> But I can't find these cards on the internet, so can't tell how they were used. If these C20 are 500 pages books.. then printing another few ready to cut out for a few cards wouldn't be such a problem?<br /> Well, I am a big fan of Mage's tarot deck.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-03-2014, 04:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T17:35:15-07:00","id":217687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=217264#post217264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mentioned about mechanics earlier. Rather problems with interpretation and localising the Changeling theme (which is not hard and kind of intuitional if somebody wants to localise in their land a big 3 V,W,M and fairy tale theme should also be that easy without doing much homework).<br /> But to the pure mechanics.. I heard there were collecting cards to the very 1st ed. of C:TD. Looks like it wasn't that succeful, but still I think making something like a tarot spread is awesome. If the bunks are some kind of a game... then placing and choosing the cards and combining them at the game session would be also funny and *bunky*. People say it destroyed imagination and options were too limited. Well, after 20 years there were so many games (I once played a game which had only 6 dice cubes with icons on their sides - and how they well rolled, that's the way someone invented a fairy tale going from concept to concept. And I think with almost 200 cards of old C:TD it shouldnt be that problematic to give abstract ideas, catch-ups etc. I guess so.<br /> But I can't find these cards on the internet, so can't tell how they were used. If these C20 are 500 pages books.. then printing another few ready to cut out for a few cards wouldn't be such a problem?<br /> Well, I am a big fan of Mage's tarot deck.</div> </div> </div> </div>As to the Cantrip card system, it was interesting but limited and impractical. If bunks are supposed to be random activities that 'activate' the cantrip, the cards are mainly suggestions. In that sense the only practical use for them are to have the cards at quick references for your character's abilities and bunks are what you make up anyways. When the cantrip and bunking rules changed in Changeling 2nd Edition, the cantrip cards were made obsolete. I don't think they should return as Cantrip cards because while the artwork is pretty and interesting, I think it does take away from playing the game to include a bunch of cards at the table rather than a reference sheet. To correct the idea that &quot;printing another few ready to cut out cards wouldn't be such a problem&quot; Yes... yes it is. Because all the cardstock printing would have to be handled by a separate printer than the ones handling the book printing. There have been issues finding printing companies that would handle special book covers and Storyteller screens while the books were printing and still have everything ready all at the same time estimated delivery. Mage 20th is going to have its own battle and delays with that process having a lenticular cover. That's why Onyx Path is not offering things like Posters or Bookmarks or even more trading cards in their stretch goals. All those things would need to be done by printing companies other than the ones handling the book assembly. The expense would be far more than even Kickstarter backers could make worth it. Not that they wouldn't LOVE to offer those things though. It's just not possible due to the expense of making it outweighing the worth.<br /> <br /> That being said I know there are people printing out their own <a href=\"http://www.werewolfcardgame.com/rage/ragelinks.html\" target=\"_blank\">Rage decks</a> and<a href=\"http://ajabahyena.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> creating artwork</a> to keep the game going. It has been suggested before that it would be cool if fans were given permission to do the same for Cantrip and Tarot cards and share them online for others to print out without the Parent company CCP games shooting it down for using copyrighted material.<br /> <br /> There's some information <a href=\"http://rpg.stackexchange.com/questions/26801/how-was-changeling-played-with-cards\" target=\"_blank\">Here on Cantrip card use</a>. But images of the cards are very small and hard to find. I would suggest saving a search on ebay and it will tell you when someone is selling Cantrip cards. That's how I started my collection of them. I collected them mainly for the artwork and not for use in the game because they are next to useless.<br /> <br /> As for Mage Tarot. ....In a word... Ugh... I've gone into detail here about the issues I have with the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/17005-suggestions-for-m20-stretchgoals\">Mage Tarot Deck</a>. I mean, not bad for a first try, but it looks like the <a href=\"http://www.aeclectic.net/tarot/cards/mage-ascension/\" target=\"_blank\">ugly cousin</a> compared to the Gorgeous artwork used in the <a href=\"http://www.aeclectic.net/tarot/cards/mage-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: Awakening deck</a>. Also for those who really know how to Read the Tarot it's mainly a ripoff of a <a href=\"http://www.aeclectic.net/tarot/cards/rider-waite/\" target=\"_blank\">Rider-Waite Deck</a> and as such it shoehorns concepts of Mage into the imagery that just don't work right. A Mage Deck should either go <a href=\"http://www.aeclectic.net/tarot/cards/quick-easy/\" target=\"_blank\">Super Simplified</a> so that anyone unfamiliar with it can understand it, such as having actual words on the pictures might be a start. Or it should have beautiful intricate artwork and not have to shoehorn all the concepts of mage into one deck. OR third option! Once again, give permission to the fans to download a template and make their own Mage artwork decks to share with others online.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T09:36:14-07:00","id":218267,"title":"","content":"The Rage fansets started around 2002-2003 (<i>If I remember correctly for Yahoo Groups</i>' <i>Rage_Info</i>) after the whole thing with Azaral Productions fell through. <a href=\"http://www.werewolfcardgame.com/index.php/about/history\" target=\"_blank\">You can read the whole thing here</a>.<br /> I also remember that the White Wolf website even posted news about the Rage fansets near the end or middle of the New England Block.<br /> <br /> Vampire: The Eternal Struggle was still being made around that time, so it took them much longer to get to the point of making fan-set/printable cards.<br /> <a href=\"http://arcadiaccg.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Arcadia CCG even has some support</a> (<i>No where near as big as Rage or V:TES, but it's something. And I collect the cards as well</i>).<br /> <br /> In addition to the Cantrip cards, there were &quot;Make-your-own&quot; Bunks cards. These make-your-own cards were part of the Changeling Player's Kit (<i>Which you can find on either Amazon or Ebay</i>).<br /> <br /> Ever since the announcement of the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrucards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Drivethrucards.com</a> website, I'm awaiting when they put out cards along with the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrucards.com/browse.php?manufacturers_id=1\" target=\"_blank\">novels and Player's Guides</a>. Also, I remember that I kept coming across online references to a Arcadia Player's Guide book in the past, but the book doesn't exist. Was this just vaporware?<br /> <br /> I would love it if Stephanie Pui-Mun Law would do artwork for Changeling 20th. I remember buying a print (<a href=\"http://i.kinja-img.com/gawker-media/image/upload/s--CXZHyXk---/c_fit,fl_progressive,q_80,w_636/18dy37ru0qw6ojpg.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Catknots</i></a>) from her from the Artist Alley at Anime Expo one year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 08-04-2014, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T19:13:40-07:00","id":218684,"title":"","content":"So... if Changeling 20th is a &quot;letter of love&quot; to the fans of Changeling: the Dreaming, what artists should be included?<br /> <br /> Should it be old favorites, and/or are there new artists who also/better represent the style of C:tD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T05:29:23-07:00","id":218964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=218684#post218684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... if Changeling 20th is a &quot;letter of love&quot; to the fans of Changeling: the Dreaming, what artists should be included?<br /> <br /> Should it be old favorites, and/or are there new artists who also/better represent the style of C:tD?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to see a mix of old and new. Like some work by Tony Diterlizzi if he's not too busy, as well as stuff from Stephanie Pui-Mun Law and Michael Kaluta. There were some artists who I don't think worked so well for Changeling, but were good for other systems like Wraith or Werewolf. I'd actually like to see the artwork more representative of the Concepts of Changeling and not because an artist draws fairies for a living. Otherwise the whole thing could be done by Amy Brown. More of the bizarre and surreal needs to be represented. Changeling has a horrible stereotype of being too bright and fluffy for the World of Darkness. So maybe there needs to be more art or artists like* <a href=\"http://www.design-warez.ru/uploads/posts/2009-11/1259151022_s4w-josephvargo090-fairytale.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Joseph Vargo</a> or maybe even photographs of 3 dimentional media collages like <a href=\"http://diablointhedetails.files.wordpress.com/2007/07/dave04gv6.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Dave McKean's</a> stuff. or even just <a href=\"http://fc09.deviantart.net/fs71/i/2013/282/1/b/tortoise_of_burden_by_creaturesfromel-d6pvk8q.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">surreal</a> stuff in general.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (*I'm not saying specifically these artists, I'm suggesting artists who's work is similar in mood.)<br /> <br /> <br /> PS for Hyena: I see a lot of wonderful inspiring stuff of Stephanie's up on her <a href=\"http://puimun.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant Art</a>. I got one of her prints as well when I met her at Fanime in 2010 I think it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  PS 08-05-2014, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T16:37:57-07:00","id":219608,"title":"","content":"While Tony could probably make the time, I don't think we could afford him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T17:26:49-07:00","id":219664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=219608#post219608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Tony could probably make the time, I don't think we could afford him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a Kickstarter stretch goal to me.<br /> <br /> But if not, I understand. All us fans of his work will let out a collective &quot;awwwww&quot; of disappointment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T19:24:53-07:00","id":219745,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">IIRC, didn't Satyr Phil do several pieced of artwork for the Warcraft PnP RPG? </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">I always thought his work, along those lines, would be a good fit for CtD.<br /> <br /> (This is assuming, of course, I'm not misappropriating the artwork that I'm thinking of...)</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T19:45:58-07:00","id":219758,"title":"","content":"If they do make a C20, I would really hope they would make it less childlike and more darkly serious- less colourful prettiness and more washed out and desperate (or maybe things may have changed in the last ten years?).<br /> <br /> I'd want it also to be more similar to actual faerie lore than what it was originally. I.e. no female satyrs, less 'goodly' fae and more alien fae. Ramp up the 'fair folk' trope. Ditch the whole 'possessing mortals' bodies' crap too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2204-toreador","name":"Toreador","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T01:18:44-07:00","id":219985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toreador</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=219758#post219758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they do make a C20, I would really hope they would make it less childlike and more darkly serious- less colourful prettiness and more washed out and desperate (or maybe things may have changed in the last ten years?).<br /> <br /> I'd want it also to be more similar to actual faerie lore than what it was originally. I.e. no female satyrs, less 'goodly' fae and more alien fae. Ramp up the 'fair folk' trope. Ditch the whole 'possessing mortals' bodies' crap too.</div> </div> </div> </div>No female satyrs? They do exist in folklore actually, just not termed Satyrs or even Fauns perse, but a very similar creature called a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glaistig\" target=\"_blank\">Glaistig</a> with the same concept nonetheless. Maybe a bit on the Unseelie side. There's plenty of Ungoodly fae in Changeliing if you dig a llittle deeper. Every 'good' fae and a 'bad' side.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you make any kind of playable character type one exclusive gender, you're going to run into trouble with the fan base that demands gender equality even if historically it might not be accurate. That and they'll just go one making female satyrs in their games anyways that there will be a devoted following of retcon rules adding them in anyways. Might as well save the headache and include them.<br /> <br /> Dunno what you have against the possessing Mortals bodies part since that's the definition of why it's called Changeling in the first place. Different from Changeling: the Lost in that the people who become Fae are not actually stolen or even taken away somewhere else, in Changeling: the Dreaming, the human gets an Extra soul. They are for all intents and purposes possessed, but it doesn't mean they are unaware of who they are or were or what is going on with the new world they find themselves living in or the fae spirit that is now a part of them. At least for Commoners. When the Fae soul goes dormant or dies, the Human souls forget everything that happened and years have possibly gone by so they find themselves someplace else and older and friends and loved ones can only explain it as if they were abducted by something else and replaced by someone different. That doesn't mean the human and fae person did not conciously make the choices in everything they did.<br /> <br /> The Exception to this of course are the Sidhe. The human soul gets replaced entirely, possibly consumed and when the Sidhe soul dies, the human could be left an empty shell if it survives at all. If you want a Darkly serious game, why leave the soul eating out?<br /> <br /> I'm all for making changeling a bit more 'grown up' though in terms of the imagery and impression it gives people. Less Wizard of Oz, more Return to Oz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  The tribbles are eating my toes! 08-06-2014, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T01:37:24-07:00","id":219988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=219745#post219745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">IIRC, didn't Satyr Phil do several pieced of artwork for the Warcraft PnP RPG? </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">I always thought his work, along those lines, would be a good fit for CtD.<br /> <br /> (This is assuming, of course, I'm not misappropriating the artwork that I'm thinking of...)</span></div> </div> </div> </div> That sounded awesome, but I can't seem to find any information on artwork listing Phil or Satyros in art credits, nor can I find anything on Phil's websites about him having done any art. Maybe if he's around he can set the record straight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T06:49:08-07:00","id":220117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=219985#post219985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno what you have against the possessing Mortals bodies part since that's the definition of why it's called Changeling in the first place. Different from Changeling: the Lost in that the people who become Fae are not actually stolen or even taken away somewhere else, in Changeling: the Dreaming, the human gets an Extra soul. They are for all intents and purposes possessed, but it doesn't mean they are unaware of who they are or were or what is going on with the new world they find themselves living in or the fae spirit that is now a part of them. At least for Commoners. When the Fae soul goes dormant or dies, the Human souls forget everything that happened and years have possibly gone by so they find themselves someplace else and older and friends and loved ones can only explain it as if they were abducted by something else and replaced by someone different. That doesn't mean the human and fae person did not conciously make the choices in everything they did.<br /> <br /> The Exception to this of course are the Sidhe. The human soul gets replaced entirely, possibly consumed and when the Sidhe soul dies, the human could be left an empty shell if it survives at all. If you want a Darkly serious game, why leave the soul eating out?</div> </div> </div> </div>If he's referring to how changelings lived as humans until their Crysalis, and even now have both a mortal Seeming and a faerie Seeming \u2014 if that's what he means by &quot;possessing mortals' bodies&quot; \u2014 then that's exactly the sort of alteration of the game that <i>should not</i> be considered for C20. If you want something without the Chimerical/Banal duality, you're no longer talking about <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>, and would be better off adapting <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b> to the present. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=219985#post219985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for making changeling a bit more 'grown up' though in terms of the imagery and impression it gives people. Less Wizard of Oz, more Return to Oz.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or more like &quot;the Wonderful Wizard of Oz&quot;, the book on which Judy Garland's movie was based. It was considerably darker in tone than the movie in many ways; though it at least avoided the business about Glinda being a master manipulator who arranged to send a teenaged girl on a suicide mission. &quot;Return to Oz&quot; managed to capture the feel of the next two books of the series (&quot;Marvelous Land of Oz&quot; and &quot;Ozma of Oz&quot;) quite well; and they were comparable in tone to the original book. It wasn't until the fourth book of the series (&quot;Dorothy and the Wizard of Oz&quot;) that the series began to derail into &quot;light and fluffy&quot; territory, with the return of the Wizard and the whitewashing of his character from &quot;usurper of the throne&quot; to &quot;good-natured crank&quot;. <br /> <br /> But I digress. Yes, the illustrations of a cartoonish anthropomorphic bear need to go. I wouldn't go with washed-out colors; that's suitable to the Banal side of things only; the Chimerical side needs to be mad with color \u2014 emphasis on &quot;mad&quot;. Have you seen the Witches' Labyriths in Puella Magi Madoka Magica? That's the sort of insanity that needs to come through when portraying the Dreaming. Changelings, meanwhile, exist in the balance between the insanity that the Chimerical World can be and the drudgery that the Banal World can be. You know the illustrations on pages 32 and 33 of CtD2e, with a faeire looking down on mirror images of the World of Darkness and the Enchanted World? The World of Darkness side is OK, though it would be improved by being a bit more drab (doing it in monochrome would have helped considerably); but the Enchanted World side is a bit too cheerful in its presentation. If I were to change <i>just one thing</i> in it, I'd have the elf's eye open, with the sort of glint of insanity in it that you'd expect of Heath Ledger's Joker. <br /> <br /> The last line of the &quot;Enchanted World&quot; text understates what needs to be stated: <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;Like, yet unlike, the rest of the World of Darkness, it is a little brighter, a little more colorful, but sometimes no less frightening.&quot;</span> Strike &quot;a little&quot; and &quot;sometimes&quot; from that: the Enchanted World is <i>much</i> brighter than the Banal World, and it's <i>much</i> more colorful; and in spite of \u2014 no, <i>because of</i> that, it is every bit as frightening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T10:40:55-07:00","id":220328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=219988#post219988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> That sounded awesome, but I can't seem to find any information on artwork listing Phil or Satyros in art credits, nor can I find anything on Phil's websites about him having done any art. Maybe if he's around he can set the record straight?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I found my copy of <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><i>Horde Player\u2019s Guide</i></span>.<br /> Flipping through it, all the artwork I remembered \u2013 art that I thought would be an appropriate style and tone for CtD - is signed by \u201cSATYR.\u201d<br /> <br /> In the Credits, under \u201cInterior Artists\u201d the only name listed is \u201cSaytr.\u201d<br /> <br /> The <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><i>Alliance Player\u2019s Guide</i></span> has a similar set of circumstances.<br /> <br /> Satyr is Phil, right? <br /> Einhorn is Finkel?<br /> Or is my overactive imagination connecting chimerical dots again?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T11:08:22-07:00","id":220349,"title":"","content":"I believe this is the Satyr artist you're thinking of:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://artroomdigital.com/gallery/main.php?g2_itemId=372\" target=\"_blank\">http://artroomdigital.com/gallery/ma...?g2_itemId=372</a><br /> <br /> It is not Satyros Phil Brucato. Unfortunately, the above image is too small for me to clearly make out his full name. Chris Ready, maybe?<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Yep, I made out the name better than I thought I did. He's Chris &quot;Satyr&quot; Ready.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit2:</b> It occurs to me I don't know if I'm using the correct pronoun or not. If I have it wrong, my most sincere apologies to Satyr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 08-06-2014, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T11:23:50-07:00","id":220362,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">@Pookaknight<br /> <br /> Thank you!<br /> That is, indeed, the artist I was thinking of. <br /> <br /> My apologies for misleading anyone.<br /> <br /> Good C20 art style?<br /> Or are my underdeveloped aesthetics showing again?</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T11:44:25-07:00","id":220371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=219664#post219664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like a Kickstarter stretch goal to me.<br /> <br /> But if not, I understand. All us fans of his work will let out a collective &quot;awwwww&quot; of disappointment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of my favorite pieces by him was from Werewolf, where a Garou was carrying a mask. I remember bringing my W:tA books to the high school library and photo-copying the images for art references for my art class. I remember that I had a lot from Prescott, Andrew Bates, and that piece that Tony did.<br /> So yeah, I support the Kickstarter stretch goal idea, as long as it is a much later revealed goal down the funding road (<i>Since I'm more interested in extra books or book expansion type-goals</i>).<br /> <br /> I've met <a href=\"http://www.baxaart.com/home.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Tom Baxa</a> at the Monsterpalooza Convention in Burbank to sign two Rage Across Las Vegas cards he did. He talked to me about how he loved working on the Arcadia CCG, so he might be able to do dark stuff for Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T13:58:01-07:00","id":220424,"title":"","content":"<br /> I'm glad for cantrip cards discussion. I understand printic, economical restrictions.<br /> I just wanted to present statement that a quite large deck of cards, especially with random and abstract conceptions would create infinite bunks. Because lets see - a Mage has to focus on specific foci and style. Changeling... also has his own style - I mean good players invent something remarkable about their players, but they are not ristricted so by MECHANICS as are Mage players. I know, handbooks invented &quot;typical&quot; exemplars of bunks for every kith and every standard Art - that was helpful about creating.<br /> Well, this would lead to abuse of one player using some easy bunk. There are some rules (leaving decision to the Storyteller) that more impressive and better fitting to the kith, Art, situation bunks give better buffs for rolling a dice - but still somehow inconstistent <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toreador</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=219758#post219758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they do make a C20, I would really hope they would make it less childlike and more darkly serious- less colourful prettiness and more washed out and desperate (or maybe things may have changed in the last ten years?).<br /> <br /> I'd want it also to be more similar to actual faerie lore than what it was originally. I.e. no female satyrs, less 'goodly' fae and more alien fae. Ramp up the 'fair folk' trope. Ditch the whole 'possessing mortals' bodies' crap too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that we cannot change the Changeling, but can only make use of not-pointed-out parts of both Chageling and World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Well, about giving the World of Darkness darker theme is partially job of The Antagonists chapter (even if it is &quot;sadly&quot; called an Appendix&quot;). That's what went on my mind when I was reading The Dreaming again.<br /> <br /> Okay, every game-line can have enemies from other games. But each game also has it's own ones (and people avoid cross-overs from obvious reasons). Vampires have the horror of sabbath, tzimisce, ghouls and tremere expeiments as most horrific dangers. Werewolf have both fomori, banes and Pentex subsidiaries. Mage has all who aren't Tradition mages + Umbrood + weird shit anomalies + paradox phenomena (while mage is a magnet for the last 3).. Wraiths is terrific in it's own trivial soulforging.. but even then we have typical variety spectres, then barghest, drones, and even lovecraftian tempest dwellers.<br /> <br /> And then.. Changeling. There were mentioned Fomori as being really bad Unseelie, banal and unnerving of glamour, but still werewolves took care of them mostly. If you remove all other-game-antagonists there are chimera. And there are pretty dark, gloomy chimera. Looks like playing a changeling, especially walking the suburbs at night, would end in meeting large spiders from the trashcans, Black Dogs, tentacles from sewages etc. That feels me with lovely terror. Then it would be a much darker, peculiar and sinister game if they made Changeling: The Bloodlines :s<br /> <br /> And another thing I read from core book. Theme: Nightmares in narration. Looks like changelings would fight the nightmares, but they are so scared by most of them that they instinctively want to run into embrace of Banality just to kill these nightmares. So.. there is a world of nightmares and dreams alike, but you can't kill nightmares cause it will cost you banality? Tragic conflict.<br /> <br /> But still I can't imagine the chimerical world. When I did a reading in Mage handbook about Penumbra, it was really intuitive that mage sees true selves of people and things. That lovely book glows with warm, touchable emotions. The same as forest hut. In Changeling the chimerical reality is just like the same. But still it isn't something easy to narrate. Is EVERY thing seen as some kind of hyper-reality. From sewers thru lanterns to the very starry night, is everything chimerical? What is %-tage of meeting wandering, creeping chimeras, good or bad. It is somehow another world not seen by any other supernatural (just like the Wraith game) so both inanimate and animate chimeras would make cities crowded with fairy stuff? Or not? Well I don't think the book explains it best to me. The setting isn't unequivocally clear for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-06-2014, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T17:51:47-07:00","id":220611,"title":"","content":"The Chimerical world seen by the Changelings co-exists with the mortal world. It's 100% present to the changelings (mostly made of incidental chimera) but is not an exact superimposition. Chimera exist independent of mortal forms and things but often there is a match up close enough that the differences do not matter. The chimerical world is something far more vivid than the mortal world (just check out the description of a tree in the core book), but that doesn't mean 'fluffy' or just 'colourful and pretty', for example SIN City is a very vivid visual experience. Chimera are made of emotional imprints and that's the world the changelings see with their faerie eyes. An alley may just be an alley to their flesh and blood retinas, strewn with refuse and so on, but to the faerie sight it may be infested with (or utterly composed of, or just be a) nightmarish chimera. It's also important to remember that the dimensions of your Fae Mein possibly (and probably) don't fit those of your human body, a 10 year old boy human could have a fae mein of a 6ft sidhe knight. Interacting with the chimerical world is where the perception of madness comes in from outside viewers, just like Don Quixote tilting at a windmill that he sees as a four armed giant, but ignoring your fae mein or that chimerical world gains you banality.You're equally limited by your mortal flesh in the interactions and also witnesses so no using a chimerical doorway if there is no corresponding mortal passage in a wall unless you Wyrd. Often it's easiest to keep things close with a dash of flavouring. A city should certainly be strewn with Fairy stuff (your wraith connection is pretty good actually Lunar) not perceived by any other supernatural, but only so much as it facilitates the game. <br /> <br /> Enemies? Changeling has plenty, but much like in Vampire there most common one (in the core) is themselves. The play of politics, duels, adventures, vendettas, balls and pageantry are the crux of the core book changeling game. Seelie vs Unseelie, Nobles vs Commoners, Houses versus Houses, Oathcircles vs Motleys, Court vs Court even personal conflicts, it's all there. Then you also have the chimera which gives you every creature of legend you could ever want. That alley I mentioned? What if it's effecting mortals? Or attracting dangerous changelings to the oathcircle? What if its nightmares are sentient? Just as the chimera are born of emotion so they can too feed and thrive from it and a wily or wary (or brave) had best be willing (especially as a PC) to deal with the ones that threaten themselves, dreamers or the Dreaming. You don;t always (or even often) gain Banality from killing Chimera, even finally. The Story is an important factor in what you can or cannot get away with in Changeling (much like in Discworld there is a force of narrative) because Changelings are literally living stories. <br /> <br /> So, we have Changelings with Internal (political/idealogical) Conflict and having to deal with the dangerous things that creep out of the minds of mortals (and themselves for that matter, see the intro story CTD 2nd). Be nice to see that still in the CTD20, but there are also a lot more. You mention the Fomori, well the WTA creatures are not the things that the faerie are talking about (it's something they touch on in the core, and in fact they're named for the creatues that the Fianna used to fight in the days of myth and legend) the real threat, the actual Fomori are something far more dangerous and we first see them really presented in Denizens of the Dreaming. CTD actually have a series of enemies that are their own. <br /> <br /> Chimera, literally can be anything you want or need for a story and you have the totality of myth, legend, urban legend, net myth and any unique ideas in your head to choose from. After all who can protect your from the monsters only you can see? <br /> The Fomorians. On a par with the Maeljin Incarna and so on, truly terrifying and needing heroes and antiherpoes of great talent to turn aside. <br /> The Denizens as detailed in Denizens of the Dreaming and would be nice to see them presented in CTD20 as it gives you a faerie foe on equal footing with the Changelings that are not themselves and are not chimera either. Can present interest situations of friend and foe, respect as per the old celtic tales and so forth. <br /> The Dauntain and Autumn People. Terrifying reflections of nihilism and people who suck the life and magic out of the world purely by existing, some of which (many in fact) may not even be &quot;bad people&quot;. Need a mention in the CTD20 book, but nothing as in depth as Autumn People went to. <br /> <br /> And... of course... The ShadowCourt. This gives us the Thallain and the Sabbat/BSD/Nephandi version of the Changeling game line. The original book was nice and something of an addition to CTD20 would be cool (like the Rage across the world, book of the wyrm, vamp companion etc). Remember that the Unseelie Court, while they enjoy Dark Glamour and Nightmare type dreams and use Ravaging more often than Musing are not the same as the ShadowCourt. Both Seelie and Unseelie can be kind or cruel, good or bad depending on the fae in question, but the ShadowCourt are deliberately wicked and evil. Not in the way of the Redcaps brutal savagery but in ways far far more sinister.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T21:08:56-07:00","id":220720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=220611#post220611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... of course... The ShadowCourt. This gives us the Thallain and the Sabbat/BSD/Nephandi version of the Changeling game line. The original book was nice and something of an addition to CTD20 would be cool (like the Rage across the world, book of the wyrm, vamp companion etc). Remember that the Unseelie Court, while they enjoy Dark Glamour and Nightmare type dreams and use Ravaging more often than Musing are not the same as the ShadowCourt. Both Seelie and Unseelie can be kind or cruel, good or bad depending on the fae in question, but the ShadowCourt are deliberately wicked and evil. Not in the way of the Redcaps brutal savagery but in ways far far more sinister.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really very accurate to equate the Sabbat with BSDs. The former are just vampires that exult in vampirism. As bad as that is, Dancers are all broken before the very face of corruption. The self-indulgent atrocities that they engage in are only the surface of the problem they present. They can't really be converted back as easily as someone might convert to a sect, going from Sabbat to Camarilla to Independent and so on. They're bent out of shape for good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T22:11:56-07:00","id":220754,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">I could see CtD20 incorporating the Shadow Court and the Dauntain into the core book, at least enough for them to be used as antagonists. The Denizens are problematic in that they\u2019re tied rather firmly to what I call the Latter Days Metaplot: they, and the fomorians that they serve, were introduced into Changeling as a result of the Week of Nightmares. I\u2019d be fine with including them in an abbreviated Antagonists format (I\u2019m picturing something akin to how the non-Solar Exalted were handled in the first two editions\u2019 core books for Exalted) along with notes on how they were originally introduced into the game and how they might be incorporated into a Changeling game that lacks the Latter Days Metaplot. All this with one caveat:</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">CtD20 needs at least two supplements: a book of Allies (non-Kithain changelings and Kinain), and a book of Enemies (Dauntain, Thallain, Denizens of the Dreaming, etc. in all their dark glory): in effect, books that are to Changeling as Changing Breeds and Book of the Wyrm are to WtA20. CtD20 itself should have more than just the original eight Kiths in it; but huge swaths of character types for Changeling (particularly ones that required special rules to use) oughtn\u2019t be incorporated into the core book beyond an abbreviated \u201chow to approximate them as Storyteller characters\u201d section; there are just <i>too many</i> of them.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T03:32:37-07:00","id":220906,"title":"","content":"That was fascinating explanation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=220611#post220611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mention the Fomori, well the WTA creatures are not the things that the faerie are talking about (it's something they touch on in the core, and in fact they're named for the creatues that the Fianna used to fight in the days of myth and legend) the real threat, the actual Fomori are something far more dangerous and we first see them really presented in Denizens of the Dreaming. CTD actually have a series of enemies that are their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait wait... are Fomorians from Denizens of the Dreamind the same as fomori from WTA? I thought not.<br /> Fomori are bane possessed humans (animals?), and they probably could be known to changelings through the Fianna.<br /> Fomorians are somehow malfean-like-version-of-nightmares-in-the-dreaming (if I think about this, they could be powerful banes..), antagonists of god-like Tuatha de Danaan?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=220611#post220611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... of course... The ShadowCourt. This gives us the Thallain and the Sabbat/BSD/Nephandi version of the Changeling game line. The original book was nice and something of an addition to CTD20 would be cool (like the Rage across the world, book of the wyrm, vamp companion etc). Remember that the Unseelie Court, while they enjoy Dark Glamour and Nightmare type dreams and use Ravaging more often than Musing are not the same as the ShadowCourt. Both Seelie and Unseelie can be kind or cruel, good or bad depending on the fae in question, but the ShadowCourt are deliberately wicked and evil. Not in the way of the Redcaps brutal savagery but in ways far far more sinister.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, let's remember that CTD never reached Revised edition. And in Vampire 2 ed. there were only Camarilla clans mentioned, so it was really shock for people when indemendents and sabbath appeared in Revised (which was the first handbook I ever read of WoD, in my native language, after being somewhat fascinated with Demon).<br /> <br /> So I wonder if CTD20 would have all Gallain described or is this too much stuff and they would need to release another book (just like Changing Breeds for WTA20). But still it would be lovely if the knowledge about every single noble house, every single kith and their seelie/unseelie counterparts were finally placed in one place, cause this was totally impacted meta-plot and it can be messy when someone wants to catch up every single one.<br /> <br /> And yep, the Shadow Court is for me the elitarist group like, I guess, something between Sabbath and Inconnu, they are just level lower than high-up godlike True Fae of CTL.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=220611#post220611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that the Unseelie Court, while they enjoy Dark Glamour and Nightmare type dreams and use Ravaging more often than Musing are not the same as the ShadowCourt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still I would love to see some additional mechanics about karma-morality-penalty like in Mage (what we did disscussed pages ago). If somebody ravages and takes Dark Glamour, it should have warping way on him, his fae mien, etc. Maybe his cantrips are so warped they can be only sinister and cruel. Something that Book of Glamour would like to introduce finally.<br /> <br /> About Denizens, they aren't so easy to role-play, cause while changelings like every core supernatural of WoD are half human and we can role-play humans with something changed in them (well, the very mood of WoD is that every supernatural is like cursed or damned with his life, fate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). And Denizens are purely of dreams, never felt mortal world and lives (even Inanimae can be role-played which I catched finally at the exemplary characters like baseball-fanatic Inanimae who lived in baseball gauntlet or smth - so a human with dreaming imprint made on important item, that was cool.). And Denizens who finally gave us &quot;lacking kiths from all around the world&quot; like Moirae/Norns/Furies (what do you like call their counterparts), with hindu Naraka and other muses. That's what we love. If we can't have changelings sadly in every region of the world, then let's spread Denizens, who are taken from many myths and cultures. I like it. And they awesomely fit into Werewolf myths (Greek, Norse, Slavic culture circles).<br /> <br /> Well, what we are totally sure we want that unfinished notes about Keys to the Kingdom and Book of Glamour were found out and used in CTD20. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Dataweaver has a point. It would be lovely, though althouth 3 books for a smaller game is like wanting too much (Wraith players would have even that). But all depends on funds at kickstarter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It didn't hurt WTA20 to have 80 pages long Allies chapter and 50 pages long Enemies chapter. Somehow it would be a perfect shortcut for Kithain, Inanimae, Nunnehi, Menehune, and then Dauntain, Thallain, Denizens and maybe something more which had to reveal never released handbooks. (And not to mention regionalisms, additional geographics, court-plays in another parts of the world, worked together with stuff from Kithbooks).<br /> <br /> WTA20 is really precious with that cause it had to catch up a big material and describes it beautifuly. Never before the Umbra was described so fantastic as for me. People were fighting each other how do you travel Umbra. And in Umbral Travel paragraph we can read all these ideas working together. I'd love to see the Dreaming explained this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-07-2014, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T04:27:55-07:00","id":220919,"title":"","content":"Changeling had probably one big problem. If you take a look to every WoD game each one of them has a big conflict, an human conflict. Vampire is about being a monster, fight that or embrace it. Wraith is about death and life, about find redemption from yourself accept the darkest parts of your soul or conquer them. You have hundreds of conflicts in the Kindred world or in the Shadowlands, but above every of them you have a conflict with yourself.<br /> Most of people forgot that in Changeling, probably even the writers forgot it.<br /> The problem with Changeling is not just everybody only took the bright parts and forgot the Shadow Court or the Fomorians. The problem is all of us forgot that conflict.<br /> <br /> Changeling is about hope in darkness. You are a flickering hope, one of the last lights in a world sunk in shadows that are longer and longer each day. And you're forgetting you're one. Every year you're getting closer to be a grump, closer to forget you're not just another human, closer to forget all the wonders than surround you. The light ones an the dark ones.<br /> But that doesn't make you good. Hope can be treacherous, just like dreams. You can hope for forgiveness when you know you'll never get it. You can hope to someone to overcome an illness that will kill him piece by piece everyday. You can hope hundreds of terrible things that will hurt you, because they'll never be, and you know they'll never be. You can even hope to never forget, but you'll do, because you're a god with alzhemeir's disease. And you know it.<br /> <br /> Now look the world of Changeling. Look again knowing that.<br /> You're a dream. And every dream can turn into a nightmare just with a blink of an eye. Today you can be Seelie, tomorrow Unseelie. The day after tomorrow you could have forgotten who you are. You have so many fights to fight and so little time. Because every day you're a little older and that means you're forgetting something more, another piece of yourself.<br /> And that's the darkness problem. The darkness in Changeling should come not just from without, but from within too. Faeries had always swift their humour so suddenly, the've been so inhuman, so alien. If they're dreamstuff..., well all of us know how unstable a dream is, much more if you think that the human part of a changeling is in a perpetual state of knowing it's running out of time.<br /> That could make you angry, that could make you wanna rebelt against everything and everyone, that could make you embrace all your darkest parts, enjoy all the pleasure while you still have time. Or could make you the kindest person in the world, trying to make this world a better place, because you'll forget but there'll be other that don't and they deserve a better place.<br /> <br /> Changeling could be terrible. Sadly, we all forget that, and we only took the funny adventure part. And that's good, we enjoyed it a lot, but without this creepy dishearting part, it's not Changeling, it's another completely different game.<br /> <br /> About Changeling 20th, I really hope we'll get it. I'm sure we'll do it.<br /> The corebook should cover the kithain with a chapter explaining all the other changeling families. And then we should get a <i>Book of the Gallain</i> (in Changing Breeds style) so all the families get all the pages they need. The hsien, the adhene, the nunnehi, the menehune, the inanimae... Perhaps even some new families from those books we never got (I always missed Keys to the Kingdom so much).<br /> I liked the magic system, but it should get some revision, no doubt about that. All that Book of Glamour should have been should be in Changeling 20th.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/n6g3njp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/kpa5GS5Mp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/93820aaad7.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/584-eliseo-ap-liam","name":"Eliseo ap Liam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T10:00:26-07:00","id":221105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eliseo ap Liam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=220919#post220919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling had probably one big problem. If you take a look to every WoD game each one of them has a big conflict, an human conflict. Vampire is about being a monster, fight that or embrace it. Wraith is about death and life, about find redemption from yourself accept the darkest parts of your soul or conquer them. You have hundreds of conflicts in the Kindred world or in the Shadowlands, but above every of them you have a conflict with yourself.<br /> Most of people forgot that in Changeling, probably even the writers forgot it.<br /> The problem with Changeling is not just everybody only took the bright parts and forgot the Shadow Court or the Fomorians. The problem is all of us forgot that conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Changelings conflict resembles to most Mage in Traditions &lt; - &gt; Technocracy war if we perceive the biggest conflict as Changelings vs Banality of the world, because the chill of incoming Endless Winter is the biggest horror outside. Being Undone for changeling is like total Oblivion for wraith.<br /> <br /> Moirdryd counted from the handbook all changeling conflicts:<br /> - Seelie vs Unseelie (so.. internal changeling &quot;good&quot; vs &quot;evil&quot;)<br /> - Changeling vs Mortal (so.. antagonists from other games + hunters)<br /> - \u200bChangeling vs Vampire<br /> - \u200bChangeling vs Werewolf<br /> - \u200bChangeling vs Mage<br /> - \u200bChangeling vs Wraith<br /> - Grump vs Wilder vs Childling vs Themselves (never never grow up?)<br /> - House vs House (nobles house infighting)<br /> - Noble vs Commoner (well, still commoners remember Accordance War when nobles took most freeholds as theirs)<br /> - Ravagers vs Musers (parallel to seelie vs unseelie in shortcut)<br /> - Changelings vs Banality (something like Ascension War ^^)<br /> <br /> We have isolation/alienation instead of vampiric damnation. We have family theme (as being also lost like Lost from CTL). We got romance theme (especially it is indicated for nobles), and vampiric stories also have romance, but this is &quot;chanson de geste&quot; version of romance, not gothic one (but still chanson de geste inspiried stories of gothic age). Then we got wonder (that's the teddy-bear part). Then we have nightmares which is what makes changelings creepy and allien for every other supernaturals. Freedom/Wildness is kind of being spontaneous and primitive, but it is Madness theme that gives us the chill (well, actually madness is about changelings never raised in freeholds, so.. we got a ronin, pariah, orphans here!) And the last one, Humor... well humor as teddy-bear seen. Wicked humor is part of Nuwisha and really creepy humor is how the Faerie are described (as Wild Ones) in VTM20.<br /> <br /> By the way, I am still dissapointed that VTM20 never mentioned about islamic Ashirra sect. I thought it is important part of culture and the world and islamic brethen vampires would be influential even in 1st world countries (not to mention fantastic middle east stories).<br /> <br /> Okay, maybe I will stop crying about orientalism (But hell no, XIX-XX modernism is full fascination of orientalism. People to survive fin de siecl mood fell into 3 things: hedonism&amp;sex but it didn't help much for profligates, orientalism and learning another ways of enlightenment in eastern philosophies and religions, e.g. many translation of holy vedas were made that time, and the third way was to look upon peasantry, natural life-cycle, because rural, country people lived stronger tied to nature harmony, seasonal calendar + church calendar and many marriages were made between gray, skinny, sensitive, artistic townman and buxom, vital, beautiful peasantry girls.), beucase if we cut off orientalism.. still we have so much fairy tales stuff which was abandonned hardly in Changeling.<br /> Not to mention my Slavic land origins, let's talk about your western countries. Medieval France and mentioned chanson de geste about knights, dragons, magic, giants and other stuff. Germany with surrounding Switzerland, Austria.. these are the lands where Hans Christian Andersen fairy tales are taking place! Why I can't meet the Snow Queen itself or many other faerie nymphs that live in ice-topped mountains of Switzerland?<br /> We have Rugia with it's chalk rocks (yes, I'm talking about the painiting). We have Der Erlkonig from Geothe about both passionate and demonical cours of elves.<br /> We have grim Grimm Brothers (word humour huh ^-^ ) fairy tales. I'm not telling you that we need Red Riding Hood kith, but we need ana access that will revive local moods. Okay, enough about romanistic (french) and german cultures. If Satyrs are from Greece, then show us more greece faeries and nymphas. If Trolls are from Scandinavia, show something more. I'd love to see Lios Alfar and Svartal Alfar conflicts are localized Seelie&amp;Unseelie fights <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And if we are at Scandinavia, for gods sake, do you know novel series which gave your girlfriends the first erotic chills? Yeah, I am talking about <b>The Legend of the Ice People</b>. These 47 series of books consist of pagantry, witches, werewolves (well, Tengel is so animalistic and erotic in allwhatsoever.. both), vampires, dark magic, more dark magic and more dark secrets... won.. by innocence of children and light. BUT THIS IS STILL DARK STORY, yes, children won the darkness thru martyrdom and suffering, but odds were overwhelming. These are curtural ROOTS of everything the changeling tries to trace from. I really encourage to read about Ice People Saga, cause this is toy-box of fairy tales shaken together with erotism, gothic mood etc...<br /> Like it or not, this is the folklor from which all other WoD games came from.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I think CTD is perfectly working only in California, the first very setting meant for them. And you can guess why California made the term Californication alive.. US has one european heritage and this is strangely warped out from depths and roots. Okay, maybe leave it teddy-bear in US, but even english Harry Potter is pretty dark as books for both kids and adults, helping to fight fears and growing up (and helping growing-up is main function of fairy tales, while Red Riding Hood is psychologically considered about not only keeping kids out from forest, but also about rape. Just like the Tarot is old-time psychological study of soul archetypes the same way fairy-tales are about psychoanalysis of our lifes, and kids being tabula rasa and learning to respect the world, nature, unknown things). If you would add material to the Europe outside British Isles (I really like the Black Dog idea and other nightmares stalking UK rural streets. But still it is sad that Black Dog protecting women didn't exist in XIX East End &amp; White Chapel :&gt; ). And I bet the European material would be most loved due to darkiness which isn't a fetish &quot;because this is WoD' but because original fairy tales are kind of psycho tales. Teaching to stay out from the wild, cause fairies can be... at best playful, but being playful may end in pregnancy, drunkenness, endless dances, fighting with evil (Seelie) or drowning by erotic nympha, decapitation or year long slavery (Unseelie. Still not CTL.<br /> <br /> And yeah, since changelings has paladins, knights, castles and Arthurian Legends (which are still dark and brutal imho)... they left christian values. Okay, children aren't bigots nor do they want fairy tales with Jesus and stuff. But still, almost every fairy tale mixed with ghost stories has with Good vs Evil theme some kind of Light which helps the protagonists. Because how else could small little girls win with overwhelming evil full of supernatural minions? Vampire had no problem with white-face virgins who by the mere presence (and Presence ^-^) can make fairy tales more true than CTD.<br /> <br /> And I am not telling in this paragraph that we are lacking Art for cantrip named &quot;Innocence Jesus&amp;Maria Blessings&quot;. The parental blessings are pagan in origin and predate christianisation of these lands (especialy in eastern and northern Europe cause even in King Arthur movie with Owen we know he was roman warrior/knight ;&gt; )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eliseo ap Liam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=220919#post220919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Changeling 20th, I really hope we'll get it. I'm sure we'll do it.<br /> The corebook should cover the kithain with a chapter explaining all the other changeling families. And then we should get a <i>Book of the Gallain</i> (in Changing Breeds style) so all the families get all the pages they need. The hsien, the adhene, the nunnehi, the menehune, the inanimae... Perhaps even some new families from those books we never got (I always missed Keys to the Kingdom so much).<br /> I liked the magic system, but it should get some revision, no doubt about that. All that Book of Glamour should have been should be in Changeling 20th.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they could fit into one 80-pages long chapter &quot;Book of Glamour&quot; somewhere. Glamour Systems chapter shouldn't be expanded more than needed. So we can get BoG and KttK by separate chapters or embedding into other stuff.<br /> But still handbook should be separated into 3 books (Childling, Wilder, Grump + Appendix).<br /> <br /> PS - In Dark Ages: Fae it is sstrongly indicated that Djinn are arabian fae (just like the elder gods are fae). So we wait for arabian djinn kiths subchapter just like Hsien and the rest <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-07-2014, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T12:53:49-07:00","id":221218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=221105#post221105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes I think CTD is perfectly working only in California, the first very setting meant for them. And you can guess why California made the term Californication alive.. US has one european heritage and this is strangely warped out from depths and roots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had to quote this because I live in California. Please remember, California is a huge state, so there are many different cultures and different environments. The main setting for Changeling 1st edition was San Francisco, CA. Which is nothing like the desert environment of Death Valley, the Chaparral environment of Ventura County, the snowy/mountain environment of the Sierra Nevada, mass etc.<br /> <br /> Also the name for California comes from a Spanish story, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etymology_of_California#From_the_novel_Las_Sergas_de_Esplandi.C3.A1n\" target=\"_blank\"><i><b>Las Sergas de Esplandi\u00e1n</b></i> by Garci Rodr\u00edguez de Montalvo</a>, which was published in 1510. In the story, the Island of California was ruled by the female Queen, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calafia\" target=\"_blank\">Calafia</a> (<i>Not to mention that there were also 500 man-eating Griffons on the island</i>).<br /> <br /> California also had the most populous and largest Native American Tribes, and there are many books with native myths about the place. The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chumash_people\" target=\"_blank\">Chumash</a> even had their own, &quot;Once upon a time&quot;, where most of their stories start with the line, &quot;When the animals were people&quot;.<br /> <br /> So I was disappointed there wasn't much conflict mentioned between Changelings and the local Nunnehi for the area in the Changeling: Immortal Eyes' The Toybox book. Or no later mentions in other books of areas where Hsien would/might show up.<br /> <br /> Different areas of the US also have vastly different influences and cultures as well. So the idea that it would only work in California doesn't really hold merit. *Cough* <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fearsome_critters\" target=\"_blank\">Fearsome Critters</a> *Cough* Tall Tales *Cough* Folk Tales *Cough*, etc.<br /> <br /> However, I would like to see a book about all the different Kingdoms around the world, though, sort of like Rage Across the World.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T15:24:01-07:00","id":221285,"title":"","content":"Well, glad we have a local patriot out there. I really admit that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> That's what I pointed out, California, being stereotypical as it could be, the capital of everything American..? Not only media though.<br /> And the only cultural roots US has are Native Americans Nunnehi - which are really interesting, but treated really passively, something like redskins taken into indian reservation. Well, this looks like the Changelings are mirroring the mankind's thinking - nobody thinks about Native Americans folklore so we have weak and distrustful Nunnehi without a claw. But then again from the other way we have surviving medieval society and thinkings of the european immigrants.. Inconsistency <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> Inconsistency or.. give a way for all other fairy tales.<br /> <br /> If somebody wants to play WoD, he is fascinated by the very nature of supernatural kind.. and then he must get his reading through all politics, kingdoms and history (which all are inconsistent or somehow pretty dull cause they are lacking depth, as mentioned above). Kingdom descriptions should be a lot loooser in description, giving just overall view like (in Spain and France the changelings are more like this... and still they call their dreaming Castillia.. ). Well, if somebody was working heavily on Concordia map - let's be it. Names are names, but the description..<br /> <br /> Yup, Rage Across the World would be fantastic. But even Mage didn't have such handbooks..? We got only smth by night and rage across. But somehow Wraith had it's handbooks Necropolis *smth*. (Everybody loves other Dark Kingdoms and it would be too awesome to see for example Necropolis Delhi.. but that's not that thread)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T17:56:27-07:00","id":221372,"title":"","content":"Isle of the Mighy, Kingdom of Willows, Immortal Eyes Trilogy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T18:26:09-07:00","id":221390,"title":"","content":"Wow a lot has been posted. Gone a few days and this is what happens.<br /> <br /> Lunar: Mage has 1 city book Fallen Tower based on Las Vegas. Wraith has some Necropoli books and Changeling has the Immortal Eyes trilogy and a few area specific books. As well as half of Sea of Shadows (or was it Blood Dimmed Tides?) which deals with Aquatic fae who justifiably outnumber land based Fae by a huge amount and get the least amount of attention.<br /> <br /> I don't want to get into the critiquing comments because it's either preaching to the choir or shouldn't distract from the thread topic.<br /> <br /> I wanna give a rousing round of applause and AMEN to what Dataweaver said. Having more than one 20th supplement for Changeling the way Werewolf and Vampire needed more is probably the only way there's going to be any over all coverage of all the things us fans would like to see expanded about Changeling.<br /> <br /> Laughing Hyena: I second everything you said about Cali. There's so much more here in folklore than is presented anywhere in the game lines. It's probably going to take fans and natives like us networking with our own fan material to really do the settings justice. I'm still down for starting up a website like Yakacen's Cyber record where people can make their own write-ups of locations and contribute them in a supplement style format for others to use. But I'm gonna need help and it should probably a network like how Cities by Night and Mind's Eye Society started out. This would include fan expansion of development between different Changeling Kingdoms I hope.<br /> <br /> If anyone else is interested in this idea and wants to help, please send me a note.<br /> <br /> <br /> And last but not least, I hope for Changeling 20th, I want to readdress the need for Changeling lifespans to be adjusted a little bit. If a Duke or Duchess or Lord of an area or Kingdom is a Sidhe and only manages to live to their 20s as a Fae before Banality or Bedlam snuffs em out, then there would be all kinds of turmoil in the kingdoms constantly regarding succession. I might be missing something stated in the books, but that bit seemed to be overlooked and my group was just discussing it with a newbie and we couldn't seem to find the information anywhere that those in charge live any longer than normal fae unless they have a merit that grants them long life at character creation. Just something that has been bugging me lately.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  Burped up some moths... scuze me. 08-07-2014, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T02:00:29-07:00","id":221783,"title":"","content":"You don't age while in a Freehold, also while there you're more than likely keeping Banality away too. So the nobles (who possess a lot of freeholds and can even make more) age slow and tend to avoid gaining banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T02:09:55-07:00","id":221789,"title":"","content":"Incidentally... While I'd love to see some of the expanded culture stuff in practice it'd be a nightmare to produce. There's only so much room to play with and the developers back in the day chose to pick the Celtic Mythological Cycle (upto and inclusive of the stories that became the Authurian Legends) as their centerpoint from which to build from, even then it's a surface scratch for core inspiration. I do love CTL's kith system but I don't feel it translates as well across to CTD with the Kiths having cultural backgrounds etc. It would be nice but ultimately you'd end up confusing the issue instead of producing a playable game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T03:40:51-07:00","id":221836,"title":"","content":"So we got Florida+New Orleans, Hawaii Islands and yup, British Isles. Yeah, that's totally describing the places from which all the folklore traces their roots. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Most fairy tales you know are even from the outside of England. Celtic folklore wasn't bordered by the La Manche. And if you want to show England (beautiful scenery and culture) then I would like to see for example mentioned Oxford the same way it was showed in Gray Matter game by Jane Jensen. Feel da magic from the very street and national heritage buildings (Carfex Towers would be typical cross-roads fairies/demons magical node sites or smth like this. I'm lacking such local cultural relishes. If you have rich culture, boast with it. Because the way Concordia was showed isn't exactly the way to being proud of heritage.).<br /> <br /> But Changeling: The Dreaming should be better called an American Dream of small dreamtowns like childhood of Stephen King with the music of Modoc from Fallout 2 <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TzMHvvBqVuY\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TzMHvvBqVuY</a> Well, these are your American dreams. Or maybe something familiar for people from all over the world like me, who find my 90s. childhood very similiar to American apple-pie-childhood in 60s of Stephen King (while I read the books I feel like this). Well, on the other hand in WTA we have uPhone fetish, so CTD20 would go with the feel of time and we will get american media disaster as new dreaming magic + maybe Japanese game/dance/whatsoever clubs like in Wasabi movie).<br /> <br /> But okay, let then Tokyo and Los Angeles be teddy-bear-like. But as I am reading through A World of Darkness Second Edition (geographical handbook) in 5th chapter &quot;Tales of the old country Europe by night&quot;, the changelings paragraph:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Europe is a center for fine art as well as magnificent craftsmanship, and many changelings have found the Continent to be a bountiful source of dreamers and Glamour. Counterbalancing this is the overcrowding of cities, the violence in the Balkan states and the dwindling of wild places. The Kithain of Europe, clinging to their precious sources of Glamour, avoid the Kindred at all costs, finding their cold ways and worldly lifestyles to be horribly Banal. </div> </div> </div>there is a huge chance that treating the Europe as still being in XIX century (and eastern europe both with Russia being wild, dark, gloomy and Baba Yaga reigned, while this is the most funny thing that Baba Yaga is something rather from children fairy tale, not a powerful god-like nosferatu... This is the effect of not doing homework and not understanding the folklore of distant countries. Or the more funny paragraph about Cracow (while it was bigger city and had bigger castle than french Luwr one in some time in history..) autors suggest us that the Kindred were not ever interested in Cracow as a city and polish lands. Yeah, things which are ridiculous and too funny can be totally rebuilt. (About suggestions that CTD20 shouldnt change the world as such. Well, you can't change somthing that wasn't even written in CTD.. and is a blank gap. )<br /> Or the love letter falls into narrow audience..<br /> I think this is mainly the reason of why CTD isn't like Dark Ages: Fae. But hey, is Europe is so dark so there is more chances for this part of world being more like DA:Fae then..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-08-2014, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T03:42:35-07:00","id":221837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=221783#post221783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't age while in a Freehold, also while there you're more than likely keeping Banality away too. So the nobles (who possess a lot of freeholds and can even make more) age slow and tend to avoid gaining banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't make the fae immune to Bedlam though. They become too disconnected with reality and sink deeper into the narrow sight of their castles and rooms. The rolls and difficulty levels in just keeping a fae sane enough to function are going to make that a struggle that will inevitably lose, despite age or protection from Banality. That's why it seems like such a catch 22 for anyone playing a ruler. You have to stay in a Freehold to not age, but stay in one too long and you go crazy. Stay out of one too long, you forget yourself. All to avoid aging or being a grump in your 20's. Yet some of the rulers of the Kingdoms have been that way for decades. It's one of those details that seems to have slipped the cracks. In a Changeling 20th, I'd like that to be addressed more squarely. I don't think it should be limited so painfully rigid to the age of the character dictating the life span of the changeling. Heck, there's probably the possibility of the re-emergence of a fae soul in Old age in some cases. Adventures of Baron Von Munchausen anyone?<br /> <br /> I do agree on the nightmare to produce. While I don't think they should try to encapsulate everything around the world in one book, there's more than enough to allude to and encourage players to look up the folklore of their region and give them a framework to incorporate it into their games as Possibly fae and not relegated to being Chimera because the writers are not willing to write a supplement or even more than a few sentences about a particular bit of folklore. While that might open a Pandora's box of potential Changelings and may fundamentally mean C:tD has to change, I think it's possible to make a strong enough framework and open up the possibilities without altering what Changeling 1 and 2 were too much.<br /> <br /> Now that I think of it, it would make the framework of Kiths, more like Traditions in Mage. There's many crafts and Sub traditions within Mage Traditions themselves. The Thallain, Gallain, and Kiths as a whole can stand to be a little looser in their definitions of what makes a Fae. If the Kith system can be tweaked just enough for it to translate across from Changeling Lost to Changeling Dreaming and still be distinctive to the Dreaming game, then by all means, it should be done. I think what has been stated most in the critiques is the inconsistency of Changeling. That's the main hope fans have for Changeling 20th.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  Typos... and RUN! THE BEES GOT OUT! 08-08-2014, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T04:03:17-07:00","id":221866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now that I think of it, it would make the framework of Kiths, more like Traditions in Mage. There's many crafts and Sub traditions within Mage Traditions themselves. The Thallain, Gallain, and Kiths as a whole can stand to be a little looser in their definitions of what makes a Fae. If the Kith system can be tweaked just enough for it to translate across from Changeling Lost to Changeling Dreaming and still be distinctive to the Dreaming game, then by all means, it should be done. I think what has been stated most in the critiques is the inconsistency of Changeling. That's the main hope fans have for Changeling 20th. </div> </div> </div>That's what I'm talking about. Not necessarily new kiths, but... hell, let's do your homework writers! You have many beautiful works about folklore and fairy tales to read through to understand which kind of faries, dryads, nymphs, swanmays (swan maidens), rusalka, vila (wi\u0142y), dziwo\u017cona, will'o wisp (b\u0142\u0119dny ognik), skrzat (fairy dwarf). Cause we don't have brownies, killmoulis, goblins, redcaps but have many similiar..<br /> And I didn't start to mention French, Spanish, German/Switz and Skandinavian faeries.. Kiths are what are they called &quot;Families&quot; or &quot;People&quot; (that's how I translate this because &quot;Acquaintances&quot; isn't a good translation into my language). And every culture has it's boggans, okay.. but let's do more homework to ease the job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-08-2014, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T11:41:06-07:00","id":222319,"title":"","content":"I think the idea World of Darkness/World of Rage book for Changeling is fantastic! Only a very small portion of the world ever got covered in Changeling's original run. It would be great to see what kithain affairs are like in South America, Africa, the rest of Europe, and Asia. It could be called something like A World of Dream and Nightmare.<br /> <br /> Actually, thinking about it, I wouldn't mind seeing the concept of Concordia expanded. Instead of just being the High King of the United States, have it be the High King of all Faerie. Concordia would be a kingdom nominally composed of all the faerie kingdoms. It would be a good parallel to the Camarilla, the Garou Nation, and the Traditions Council. And must like the others, there would be parts of the world firmly under Concordia, areas that pay lip service, areas in open rebellion, and places that just ignore Concordia altogether. The Parliament of Dreams would be a truly grand thing! The House of Lords would be comprised of rulers or their representatives from across the planet. The House of Commons would be a raucous assembly of elected representatives from all sorts of opposed cultures. It would also justify why the Shadow Court is so intent on the destruction of Concordia. It wouldn't just be North America at stake. It would be an opportunity to impose the Fomorian Dream on the whole world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T11:59:48-07:00","id":222337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, thinking about it, I wouldn't mind seeing the concept of Concordia expanded. Instead of just being the High King of the United States, have it be the High King of all Faerie. </div> </div> </div>This might go too far. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> A WoD 2ed. handbook speaks about Latin and South American faeries, but unknown to nunnehi - so they do not know the politics of US.<br /> Same with Hsien who ignore faeries outside Asian world of darkness.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see many different kingdoms or even regions without kingdoms with wild faeries courts. (Something that occured after Shattered Dream)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T12:06:02-07:00","id":222343,"title":"","content":"Well sure, like I said in the post, there would be places where Concordia doesn't hold sway. I can just imagine a group of knights meeting the fair folk of an uncontacted tribe for the first time. The knights try to explain they're representatives from Concordia, and the indigenous fae say &quot;who?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T18:05:45-07:00","id":222627,"title":"","content":"I haven't said anything in this thread?<br /> <br /> Fix this.<br /> <br /> I will glady throw over $300 at C20. My love for <i>Dreaming</i> is quite deep considering I only have the 2nd Edition Core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T20:44:36-07:00","id":222765,"title":"","content":"Once again pookaKnight, you come up with another idea as good as Dataweaver's and it makes me all excited to see if this is actually possible and squirming to see if I can help somehow or convince OPP that this is the direction C20 should go. Garg! I wish I knew this system better than I do to freelance write for it. I'd need a committee of other Changeling gamers and STs. I'm willing to put in time working with writing, gathering references and resources, or fact checking the system books, or even website wrangling in order to present these ideas as a freelance project to OPP if anyone else is interested in doing so. I just can't do it alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T08:21:24-07:00","id":223291,"title":"","content":"Interested. But I'm not qualified. Only read the first ed CtD book and the only Changeling game I played was a CtL game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T22:35:24-07:00","id":223884,"title":"","content":"Something I'd like to see in C20, would be a nice big section for The Enchanted. And as much as Mage fans, of which I'm one, wouldn't want his time split, I'd like to see it written by Satyros. After reading his work in Deleria, I've got an entirely new perspective on these, sometimes hapless, mortal allies, that I'd love to see woven into Changeling. Just my two cents, with Deleria YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/399-disthanes","name":"disthanes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T16:27:58-07:00","id":224595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>disthanes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=223884#post223884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I'd like to see in C20, would be a nice big section for The Enchanted. And as much as Mage fans, of which I'm one, wouldn't want his time split, I'd like to see it written by Satyros. After reading his work in Deleria, I've got an entirely new perspective on these, sometimes hapless, mortal allies, that I'd love to see woven into Changeling. Just my two cents, with Deleria YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this. Though I hope that it doesn't conflict with his Deleria work if they are too similar. The Enchanted does need it's own serious section in a core book because I don't think that it got enough emphasis and attention originally and many can overlook the Enchanted Supplement book where it's revealed just how dangerous it is for anyone being Enchanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T05:04:29-07:00","id":224981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once again pookaKnight, you come up with another idea as good as Dataweaver's and it makes me all excited to see if this is actually possible and squirming to see if I can help somehow or convince OPP that this is the direction C20 should go. Garg! I wish I knew this system better than I do to freelance write for it. I'd need a committee of other Changeling gamers and STs. I'm willing to put in time working with writing, gathering references and resources, or fact checking the system books, or even website wrangling in order to present these ideas as a freelance project to OPP if anyone else is interested in doing so. I just can't do it alone. </div> </div> </div>Well, Imo the best way is to contribute to White Wolf wikia articles about CTD <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Enchanted does need it's own serious section in a core book because I don't think that it got enough emphasis and attention originally and many can overlook the Enchanted Supplement book where it's revealed just how dangerous it is for anyone being Enchanted. </div> </div> </div>Ghouls along with tzimisce ghoul families found their place in VTM20 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As well as every single important Bloodline (with historical ones too). Same with Changing Breeds in WTA20. CTD20 deserves revision + additional areas of the world and german/scandinavian/romanian/slavic faeries :&gt;&gt;&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-11-2014, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T16:21:18-07:00","id":225387,"title":"","content":"I feel wary about using Wikia mainly due to the anyone can make an account and edit content, deleting pages. For something this important I think a little more quality control should be used. Especially if it's fan developed content that isn't cannon (yet*crosses fingers*) to the C:tD universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T21:00:48-07:00","id":226765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=140217#post140217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also a little lost on why banality would be overtaking the whole world, just because science and rationality are in vogue in the West and some other Developed countries. There are still huge swaths of the globe where religion and &amp;quot;superstition&amp;quot; and belief in magic are very alive and strong, so wouldn't those regions have Fae who have no need to become Changelings? Or just boast open trods back to Arcadia? How can the world be sliding into Winter if only part of humanity has embraced a purely mundane, anti-supernatural, pure-science worldview?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My preferred explanation for this is that the Dreaming and the Autumn World were once in a closer &quot;orbit&quot; of each other, but a disaster caused in the wake of the rise of the Technocracy broke their close connection and caused the Dreaming to drift away until it was summoned back in a ritual centered around humanity beholding the moon landing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T06:50:52-07:00","id":226987,"title":"","content":"I just have to note, science does not equal banality.<br /> <br /> DA: Darkening Sky has a bit in it about the Shattering. While I don't care for the DA: Fae adventure in it overall, it does have one nugget of brilliance. The Fae created weapons they didn't truly understand, and used them on each other. They were essentially bombs created from pure banality. The Fae themselves did the metaphysical equivalent of nuking the Dreaming and rendering Earth inhospitable to faerie kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T01:26:56-07:00","id":227709,"title":"","content":"Well, one another thing went into my mind and I'm eager to share.<br /> <br /> As being a big translator of Changeling (and many other stuff) in smth called polish fandom (I'm quite separating from it, but okay) I am sometimes really crushed when authors use anachronic scottish-irish-welsh terms. It's not a problem if I can find something in such dictionaries, thesauruses etc. but sometimes it makes me uneasy to decide which of many translations (every equally bad or good) should I finally take. That's also a problem of richness of my own language. But still I need to dig to the meaning. A simple example would be a Krofted Inanimae. I found that croft is Scottish farm pen, good. But Kroft? And only *one single* paragraph assured me it is *this* meaning, when I read &quot;Gladeling versus Krofted&quot; in the book. So metaphorically they really ment farmpen, good for them. And for me.<br /> <br /> Okay, that's one example, but still we have many more different. How do you for example read and understand words, kith, kin, kithain, kinain?<br /> The only thing that dictionary has, are kith and kin (friends and acquaintances). Occasionary I made some kind of rotten compromise: translated kith as &quot;the people&quot; in my language, and kin like &quot;kindred&quot; (the same term was in Werewolf translation so it wasn't hard). But still WTA didn't translate kinain so I didn't do also, treating it like.. too anachronic term so it must stay as proper noun, never translated, stayed as original. So.. my players are Kithain (and sometimes they declinate this word..) but when talking about kiths (which is a normal word, but comparing to clan, tribe etc. the literall translation just sucks, I translated it as our word for &quot;the people&quot;. Much better than terms who sound like your &quot;bros&quot;.) And then this is problematic when the handbook speaks like Kithain is derived from the word kith... &lt;mindblows&gt; A hard thing for me to this day.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I translate your anachronic term from anglo-saxon culture (like Escheat) into my culture similiar anachronic term (prawo Kaduka - law of &quot;Kaduk&quot; , which sound properly somehow) .<br /> <br /> Or totally hardcore: greymayre word. Even google is silent.<br /> <br /> So in the end, I'd love to see in lexicon a small sidebar explaining some term, especially if someone is from the outside of anglosax culture circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-14-2014, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T07:36:00-07:00","id":227924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=226987#post226987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just have to note, science does not equal banality.<br /> <br /> DA: Darkening Sky has a bit in it about the Shattering. While I don't care for the DA: Fae adventure in it overall, it does have one nugget of brilliance. The Fae created weapons they didn't truly understand, and used them on each other. They were essentially bombs created from pure banality. The Fae themselves did the metaphysical equivalent of nuking the Dreaming and rendering Earth inhospitable to faerie kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beautiful.<br /> <br /> And... Damn you! Now I have to buy Darkening Sky.... &lt;grumble, grumble&gt;<br /> <br /> Also, yes science does not = banality. Especially if a key element in the return of the Sidhe was the scientific accomplishment of having mundane, normal, non-Technocract, Sleeper humans set foot on the Moon (which was already spooky but known territory to mages of all sorts, powerful werewolves, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 08-14-2014, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T13:20:41-07:00","id":228437,"title":"","content":"Nothing official yet, but hopeful rumblings coming out of GenCon today!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://\u200bhttps://twitter.com/sandchigger/status/500012591364980736\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/sandchigger/status/500012591364980736</a><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T18:44:37-07:00","id":228631,"title":"","content":"The link was giving me trouble since I'm not on twitter, but I eventually found my way around it. call me Officially Unofficially excited too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T03:20:05-07:00","id":228953,"title":"","content":"Since many people prefer FB than Twitter, I'd love to see news requoted right there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T05:08:18-07:00","id":228990,"title":"","content":"There's no official news, only rumors. This is just a post from a Changeling fan who isn't connected to CCP or Onyx Path. If there is actual news, I'm sure it'll be posted everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T20:00:01-07:00","id":229881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=227924#post227924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beautiful.<br /> <br /> And... Damn you! Now I have to buy Darkening Sky.... &lt;grumble, grumble&gt;<br /> <br /> Also, yes science does not = banality. Especially if a key element in the return of the Sidhe was the scientific accomplishment of having mundane, normal, non-Technocract, Sleeper humans set foot on the Moon (which was already spooky but known territory to mages of all sorts, powerful werewolves, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it is actually a pretty interesting adventure book regardless of which DA line you play. And it's Fae section is another thing that's been making me consider picking up CtD either before the C20 KS or if C20 doesn't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T13:33:57-07:00","id":230483,"title":"","content":"Onyx Path's What's Up with the Classic World of Darkness panel is going on right now at GenCon. Is it bad that I'm constantly hitting refresh on Twitter to see any news coming out of it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T15:20:55-07:00","id":230611,"title":"","content":"Over an hour after the Classic World of Darkness panel and everywhere is completely silent on Changeling. It's not looking good....<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> And just when I post that someone comments that the subject came up in the panel. Hopefully there will be some information soon!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 08-16-2014, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T15:38:37-07:00","id":230620,"title":"","content":"And there's word from Onyx Path's Twitter! &quot;The word is 'yes.'&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/TheOnyxPath/status/500771973018824705\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/TheOnyxPath/stat...71973018824705</a><br /> <br /> Edit to add: Let's celebrate!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FWXoCXMo_IM&amp;list=UUBtAtYzuzBIHvfBwOQqJm-g\" data-code=\"FWXoCXMo_IM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/FWXoCXMo_IM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 08-16-2014, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T17:04:34-07:00","id":230703,"title":"","content":"Well congratulations CtD fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T20:50:12-07:00","id":230953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=230620#post230620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's word from Onyx Path's Twitter! &quot;The word is 'yes.'&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/TheOnyxPath/status/500771973018824705\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/TheOnyxPath/stat...71973018824705</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any word of what was actually said at GenCon about CtD? Was hoping for something a little more substantial... Not that a yes isn't great, just the one lone tweet lacks some of the authority of a nice anouncement on the onyx path blog, or appearing on the release calendar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2538-trashheap","name":"trashHeap","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T21:22:30-07:00","id":230978,"title":"","content":"That's all I've got! I'm surprised at the lack of reporting coming out of GenCon this year, but hopefully there'll be more when folks get back home.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to hearing about who'll be developing it. Will they have Ian Lemke, Nicky Rae, or Jackie Cassada back, or will they go with someone else? Exciting times!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T01:20:32-07:00","id":231192,"title":"","content":"Very, very, good news. I'm very happy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T13:39:58-07:00","id":231922,"title":"","content":"Woo! Though I was a huge fan of WoD in the 90's, I never got the chance to run or play WtO or CtD. So glad they are both going to be 20th editions. It's going to be great to have the whole collection.<br /> This thread has me pretty excited to see Changeling. I know literally nothing about it (or Wraith for that matter.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3651-grimmshade","name":"Grimmshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T15:58:14-07:00","id":232042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=230978#post230978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's all I've got! I'm surprised at the lack of reporting coming out of GenCon this year, but hopefully there'll be more when folks get back home.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to hearing about who'll be developing it. Will they have Ian Lemke, Nicky Rae, or Jackie Cassada back, or will they go with someone else? Exciting times!</div> </div> </div> </div>I was at the panel. There wasn\u2019t much news beyond, \u201cYes\u201d about Changeling. Rich was asked about a developer, but he said that he\u2019s not yet named one, and hasn\u2019t decided if it\u2019s just going to be one person or more.<br /> <br /> Also, the potential of the missing kithbooks was discussed. But I think like most of the core books that it depends on the success of the Kickstarter and how much enthusiasm there is for the line.<br /> <br /> As someone who also never played Changeling (or Wraith), I\u2019m excited, and will help kickstart. I think the way Onyx Path is doing the 20th Anniversary editions it makes it easier to get into a game, only really having to buy one book as opposed to many. Or maybe I\u2019m just 15 years older and have a little more disposable income.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T19:29:03-07:00","id":232203,"title":"","content":"Darker Days was video-recording the panel, and so I expect to see it up on their website and/or YouTube shortly.<br /> Eddy Webb also (hopefully) audio-recorded the panel, so if there are audio issues, it should be clean on that.<br /> <br /> I was there as well, and when it comes to C:tD, it's pretty sparse right now.<br /> In the past, they seem to have already had Developers lined-up when they made the announcement, but right now, he only has &quot;a few people in mind, who have expressed interest&quot; (paraphrased), and has no artists in mind either.<br /> <br /> Toni DiTerlizzi has recently published a book that revisits his RPG illustration-days, but it sounds like (at least right now), he doesn't have interest in doing any RPG Illustrations these days. Then again, it's a year away, so you never know... Kinds like W20, I don't think we really got any info until December, and even that was getting feedback on the Ron Spencer sketches before the writing was in full-swing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T09:02:18-07:00","id":232873,"title":"","content":"Holden posted some great stuff over on RPG.net that he would like to see in C20. I'm reposting it here because it's just too good not to share:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Carl Sagan ought to be a Dreamer, yes. By contrast, I imagine it would be acutely painful to share an elevator ride with Christopher Hitchens. Doubly so if you're a changeling.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given my druthers, I would rather equate Banality with apathy and reductive cynicism rather than simple rationality, and certainly not with &quot;science.&quot; One of the Kiths are a bunch of mad engineers, for Chrissakes. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was trying, but I think it's safe to say that Changeling was a bit of a mess, and yawed around missing a lot of what it was swinging for much of the time. (I'm thinking specifically of the lead-in for Noblesse Oblige, where the narrator shudders in revulsion at the mention of the theory of evolution.) A lot of this, I think, goes back to Changeling releasing in '95 and getting most of its formative supplements in '95-'96, which is the absolute apex of White Wolf's infatuation with cosmology crossover, before they reversed course HARD around '98. That means Changeling got a lot of conceptual carry-over from Werewolf's Weaver and Mage's Technocracy that didn't necessarily belong in the game. </div> </div> </div>(source: </span></span><a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?734360-Changeling-20-confirmed\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...g-20-confirmed</a> )<br /> <br /> That last one in particular speaks to me. Changeling always seemed so afraid to stake out it's own territory and accidentally step on the toes of another gameline. Changeling: The Dreaming shouldn't care that there's an enemy in Werewolf called the Fomori. Changeling should own the Formorians without apology or making excuses why the two have the same name. Dreams and Nightmares does it too. Everyone thinks Changelings are unplayable in the Dreaming because the book spends so much word count explaining how Mages perceive Changelings in the Dreaming, and only one sentence saying that's not how Changeling's see themselves. Why do the Nunnehi care about the Umbra and not the Dreaming?<br /> <br /> I'd love to see Changeling get out of the shadow of the other game lines and stand just as independently as Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Hunter, and Demon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T12:01:15-07:00","id":233107,"title":"","content":"I noticed what the last quotation talks about a lot in going over Changeling Books. Before any 20th editions came out, I was doing research for the Rage CCG fansets and making reference lists so the fansets could stick as close to canon material. After going over and reading all the Werewolf books I had, I noticed that I had to go over other White Wolf books for any other references. So I now own all the Changeling, Hunter, KoftE, and Wraith books (<i>missing Great War book for now, though</i>). Still working on the other lines.<br /> <br /> It's interesting to see the huge contrast between Wraith and Changeling. Wraith mentions how to crossover, but barely mentions other supernaturals (<i>At most, it covers some Vampire characters</i>). Meanwhile, Changeling has NPC stats for Garou, Vampire, Mages, and Wraiths in various books.<br /> Hunter does kinda rely on the shadow of the other lines despite being vague about it. If you are familiar with any of the other lines, you'll easily catch blatant references to objects, books, and characters. Such as Dr. Anton Stark having NPC stats in Hunter: First Contact.<br /> <br /> I wonder if that has to do with Hunter being published after 1998, and so White Wolf was slowly loosing up a little over the hard &quot;Anti-crossover' stance from 1998. Which slowly lead to tool-kit style approach in the Time of Judgement books and NWOD.<br /> <br /> But I will back Changeling 20th went it comes after Wraith 20th. But I know it might be a year from now or so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:04:58-07:00","id":233475,"title":"","content":"I'm very excited at the prospect of adding this to my shelf.<br /> <br /> It's weird. I used to think that growing older put me farther away from getting into the Changeling headspace. But I think it's actually brought me closer. Standing on the banal side of things, it's very easy to see the lure of wanting to forget the fae world, just walk away, it's hurt you enough, it's taking all your time, you could create so much more if you focused on your real life. You're already on the edge, just take a couple more steps, if you turn away you know you'll lose it forever, but how much will you really be losing? Force yourself to forget, force yourself not to care, it's not real, it's not important, maybe just a quirk of a mental disorder you could never let go of, but if you keep walking away you can finally be whole.<br /> <br /> I could never quite take the game seriously enough from the perspective of a childling, I couldn't quite make myself care with a wilder, but I think I've finally made a solid connection with the grumps of the Changeling world.<br /> <br /> I used to find that just too depressing, but I guess I don't anymore. After all, it's only sad for the ones they leave behind--and in the end, even for someone who was once fae, a real life in the real world is worthy of respect. There's valid reasons to want to turn to banality. But when I look at holding onto Glamour as the real sacrifice--not the act of turning away from it--it becomes more rare and beautiful.<br /> <br /> I might be missing the point again, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:22:28-07:00","id":233847,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m hoping that C20 will handle the Grumps more sympathetically than previous editions did. In general, the books seemed to be written from a hybrid of the childling and wilder Seemings\u2019 perspectives, with Grumps coming across as dying changelings who were slightly better than Dauntain, albeit more pitiful than scary. Something like Traveller\u2019s description above would help immensely, IMHO. It would also help a bit with Changeling\u2019s reputation for being juvenile. <br /> <br /> Something else that would help would be if they\u2019d tone down the parallel between the Seemings and childhood, teenagers, and adults: give samples of fully-grown Childlings who are still full of wonder, and of teens or children who have taken on the mindset of a Grump; and make it possible (if difficult) to reverse the general childling \u27a1 wilder \u27a1 grump progression. This would both make it a two-way street and more of a \u201cchoice of which attitude you want to play\u201d as opposed to three-stage \u201cmorality meter\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T04:04:46-07:00","id":234050,"title":"","content":"Yup, that's really complicated if somebody wants to buy for example Medicine cause he is Pet Doctor... and what? He has to be like 30 years old, so he must be a Grump.<br /> Or he is maybe Wilder, kt\u00f3ry sustained himself in freehold, did medicine studies (not likely to happen) and is a Per Doctor living 50 years but in body of 18 year old? I don't actually get it. And exemplar characters of changelings aren't that much kids as you read through them or watch pictures..<br /> Yes, it is more juvenile spirit inside a human body, but still..<br /> <br /> By the way, have you seen that: <a href=\"http://tekh.org/changeling/\" target=\"_blank\">http://tekh.org/changeling/</a><br /> Not exactly my feelings (mine are still mainly geographical and Kith ones) how it should be redone, but.. just showing you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-19-2014, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T07:01:09-07:00","id":234151,"title":"","content":"Well...<br /> <br /> Here's hoping 20th takes a few tone cues concerning Beautiful Madness from Lost, rather than copy all the old stuff. Really, while oChangeling is my least favorite cWoD game (Primarily due to the extremely creepy implications of Childling Satyr's and a rather... annoying section of its fan-base, along with a sense of it really not fitting in with the rest of the cWoD) I wish for 20th to be a gift to old fans without totally pandering to them, and still stay accessible to those curious about Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:40:28-07:00","id":234388,"title":"","content":"Lost is getting a second edition. Changeling: The Dreaming needs to stand apart. Dreaming is the storytelling game of urban fantasy. Lost is the storytelling game of beautiful madness.<br /> <br /> Madness is a threat in Dreaming, but it's not the primary one. Dreaming's threat is the death of wonder. It's theme is to discover and create the fantastic, not be overwhelmed by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:42:10-07:00","id":234448,"title":"","content":"There cannot be Beautiful Madness in CTD only.<br /> But still this madness is just one of MANY jewels around in The Dreaming.<br /> And The Dreaming should be game overlapping all major cultures. Grimm, Andersen, Sandemo works, Classic fairy tales and classic dark folklore. Celtic, German, Scadinavian, Slavic... and KttK genies and Latin America and Africa and Asia (Hsien) redone.<br /> And the roleplaying problems with playing children/adolescence.. and taking all physiology of changelings in one place (only in The Enchanted we can literally directly read that 40% of offspring of changeling and changeling is a changeling and the rest is kinain... I couldn't find this out by Changeling core book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:29:03-07:00","id":234724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=234388#post234388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lost is getting a second edition. Changeling: The Dreaming needs to stand apart. Dreaming is the storytelling game of urban fantasy. Lost is the storytelling game of beautiful madness.<br /> <br /> Madness is a threat in Dreaming, but it's not the primary one. Dreaming's threat is the death of wonder. It's theme is to discover and create the fantastic, not be overwhelmed by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean is making Bedlam a little scarier a concept than it was. That sort of Beautiful Madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:33:34-07:00","id":234728,"title":"","content":"Personally, I want it stressed that Enchanting non-Changelings is not so different, or IS, mind-raping them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T16:06:37-07:00","id":234746,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd say addicting, just like ghouls and acolytes. And they have also kinain as allies, same feeling as with werewolf kinfolk.<br /> <br /> So.. bedlam as beautiful madness?<br /> I'd rather see why Nightmare itself comes from Banality. Well, just sayin it is Oblivion for faerie, so it must be creepy, but nightmares are sometimes told to be part of dreams and sometimes something contradictory.<br /> Same with another concepts: kryos as being too banal power (since crystalline works are like the Weaver job and cold is like a chill of Winter - this is somehow... ya know. weird. Snow Queen and crystals are beautiful dream-stuff..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-19-2014, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T17:55:24-07:00","id":234842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=234728#post234728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I want it stressed that Enchanting non-Changelings is not so different, or IS, mind-raping them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's called ravaging in Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:00:22-07:00","id":234845,"title":"","content":"Semantics. Basically every mind-influencing supernatural power used on a mortal, regardless of splat, is intrusion into his or her mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:12:12-07:00","id":234857,"title":"","content":"The degree to which I vehemently disagree means that I have nothing productive to add along these lines, so I will bow out of the talk of enchanting as mind rape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T02:51:17-07:00","id":235228,"title":"","content":"Hell no, Reverie isn't raping at all. It is loooong time friendship, giving some inspiration and taking a part of an effect. Like a beekeeper who first places much sugar in beehive and after sum takes some honey (but not every honey, cause bees also have to eat something). In a shortcut.<br /> <br /> That's famous review cumulating your discussion: <a href=\"http://www.somethingawful.com/dungeons-and-dragons/changeling-white-wolf/1/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.somethingawful.com/dungeo...-white-wolf/1/</a><br /> <br /> I still wonder what would be arabian fae from KttK. One Thousand and One Nights has no particular faeries or equivalents of changelings (only genies are appropiate with very specific rules and bans). And original is part fairy tale, part cruel and chauvinistic reality of Golden Age of Islam. This would be very hard to write to acquire mythic origins, folklore of poor people alongside civilational might. Bagdad was the most powerful city these times, with universities, temples, biggest palaces.. and when Europe was stinking dirt, even kings, these same times arabians were clean folk with baths like in ancient Rome.<br /> What should be changelings out there for you?<br /> Or maybe would-be-writers of Keys to the Kingdom aren't quite dead now and can be asked what was that about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","user":"Lunar","date":". 08-20-2014, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T03:43:43-07:00","id":235261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell no, Reverie isn't raping at all. It is loooong time friendship, giving some inspiration and taking a part of an effect. Like a beekeeper who first places much sugar in beehive and after sum takes some honey (but not every honey, cause bees also have to eat something). In a shortcut. </div> </div> </div>I don't see how's that any different from exploiting humans. A pragmatic vampire with high self-control can also behave like a beekeeper. Ultimately every supernatural uses mortals in some way. Vampires must drink blood and animal blood is not enough in most cases (if you use VTR rules, there is even mechanical representation). Werewolves need Kinfolk for procreation and it's not unheard of to treat them like cannon fodder and breeding stock in certain Septs. Mages try to affect beliefs of the Masses to wage their philosophical wars on how the reality should be.<br /> <br /> A hunter, a normal dude who knows something about the supernatural, would certainly not see it in such way like Changelings of Dreaming do. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T16:17:59-07:00","id":235848,"title":"","content":"Well, the game in question is <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>; so I would tend to think that the way changelings see things would take precedent. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s also worth noting that when White Wolf came out with <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b>, the core abilities that they gave to their Imbued hunters were immunity to mental effects that take away human agency, and illusion-piercing powers that let the hunters act without being kept in the dark. Enchanting a mortal so that he can see Chimerical reality isn\u2019t a mental effect that takes away human agency; it\u2019s opening the mortal\u2019s eyes to things going on around him so he can make informed choices. I suspect that hunters who go after faeries would <i>want</i> to be Enchanted, so that they can see what they\u2019re dealing with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T16:50:15-07:00","id":235901,"title":"","content":"Being enchanted makes hunters vulnerable to the dreaming stuff. That's totally not the way to hunt faeries <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3612-lunar","name":"Lunar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:04:41-07:00","id":236000,"title":"","content":"&gt;Lets them see the Dreaming<br /> <br /> Ok. Let me get this straight. How is this *not* mindshattering, considering how the dreaming is supposed to be this crazy wild out of control sort of thing filled with nightmares?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3503-arch-magos","name":"Arch-Magos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:21:10-07:00","id":236011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Carl Sagan ought to be a Dreamer, yes. By contrast, I imagine it would be acutely painful to share an elevator ride with Christopher Hitchens. Doubly so if you're a changeling. </div> </div> </div>&quot;changelings aren't nice people. They insult, they destroy, and they kill. And they are euphoric when it happens, not because of some phony god's blessing, but because they are enlightened by their own Wyrd.&quot; from <a href=\"http://projects.inklesspen.com/fatal-and-friends/gerund/changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\">http://projects.inklesspen.com/fatal...ling-the-lost/</a><br /> <br /> PS. But seriously, what the heck, Holden, using deceased people in metaphors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:28:46-07:00","id":236020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arch-Magos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=236000#post236000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;Lets them see the Dreaming<br /> <br /> Ok. Let me get this straight. How is this *not* mindshattering, considering how the dreaming is supposed to be this crazy wild out of control sort of thing filled with nightmares?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were to take a mortal into the Deep Dreaming, sure. The Chimerical Reality that exists as an overlay of the physical world <i>can</i> contain scary things, just as the physical world itself can; but mostly it\u2019s more <i>weird</i> than <i>nightmarish</i>; whether it\u2019s nightmarish or wondrous depends on what you encounter there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:47:44-07:00","id":236035,"title":"","content":"Or fulfilling - finally experiencing that part of the world that, deep down, the person has always known was missing in their life but could never put their finger on. Even if the person doesn't consciously remember it, the experience could still touch their soul and give them renewed purpose in life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T19:16:43-07:00","id":236061,"title":"","content":"Exactly. While earlier editions may have focused a bit too much on the positive aspects of the Dreaming, giving the impression that it\u2019s a bright and cheery place of kids with balloons and cartoon bears who paint, those aspects should not be excised from the Dreaming in C20; merely de-kidified and put into context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T07:34:07-07:00","id":236471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=236061#post236061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. While earlier editions may have focused a bit too much on the positive aspects of the Dreaming, giving the impression that it\u2019s a bright and cheery place of kids with balloons and cartoon bears who paint, those aspects should not be excised from the Dreaming in C20; merely de-kidified and put into context.</div> </div> </div> </div>All balloons to be distributed by Pennywise, all painting cartoon bears to use human blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T14:09:58-07:00","id":236916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pennywise, </div> </div> </div>Changeling: The Slasher.<br /> <br /> For some reason Mister Sandman song reminds me of psycho kille