rom Onyx Paths games and from WW for a long time (since 2004 in fact, when the cWoD exploded).<br /> <br /> Now, I'm back thanks to the wondrous news that C20 is being done.<br /> <br /> I just want to give my 2c to some of the discussions here.<br /> <br /> The very first post of this thread asks whether or not a KB: Boggans should be done, and to that I say yes! Having worked on it, if only a little, with Chris Howard, trust me when I say that it deserves to be done.<br /> <br /> Also, Book of Glamour.<br /> <br /> And, finally, here is a post I wrote on FB:<br /> <br /> Now, my dream-edition would have <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/ian.lemke\" target=\"_blank\">Ian Lemke</a> as developer and the full team of authors gathered up for this very special occasion, i.e. <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/choward465\" target=\"_blank\">Christopher Howard</a> (nobles, Scathach, nockers and... boggans!), <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/jackie.cassada\" target=\"_blank\">Jackie Cassada</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=100004735576915\" target=\"_blank\">Nicky Rea</a> (Unseelie and Shadow Courts), <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/richard.dansky\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Dansky</a> (San Francisco and sluagh), R. S. Martin (aka &quot;glass&quot;), the wonderful author of Dreams &amp; Nightmares, and many others I forget<br /> <br /> The illustrations by <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TonyDiterlizzi\" target=\"_blank\">Tony DiTerlizzi</a> should be there, in this new edition, of course.<br /> <br /> Also: I want as a stretch goal to do the Black Compendium which would include the stories of the War of Trees, the Nine Battles won by the sidhe over the Fomorians and the breaking of the Casque of Sorrows. And it would be illustrated, once again, by Tony DiTerlizzi.<br /> <br /> I am so looking for this, just as 20 years ago, when it first came out, I went on the very first day to my RPG bookstore (where I had been harassing the staff for over two months, asking them when it was due to come) disguised as a fairy! <br /> <br /> And I remember my first reading of the book: it was one of the most wonderful and beautiful thing I had (and have since then) ever seen, especially the gorgeous introduction written by True Thomas (I even learnt to write like the script used) with splendid pictures. This is what I want to find again in the C20: while the 2nd edition was well done, the first was much more poetic and inspiring, thanks to the Grand Pooka, aka Ian Lemke.<br /> <br /> Please, make me dream again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T12:18:34-07:00","id":237233,"title":"","content":"Walking on the memory lane...<br /> <br /> You remember the advertising leaflet that was distributed just before Changeling first came out? I do. I read and re-read it countless times, imagining the game that it advertised to. I had previously done the same thing with the few hints here and there, published in sourcebooks for Werewolf and Mage.<br /> <br /> But with these 16 pages (yes, most of the illustrations take two pages each), I had a heretofore unparalleled glimpse into the game. And it was wonderful! Before even owning the book, I was anticipating the Immortal Eyes chronicle (and books!). And I loved the cards. I really did. I loved the fact that you could spread them out before you on the table and that other player-characters could use one of them to cast their own cantrips. And I liked the idea of drawing your Bunk at random, to better illustrate the chaos and playfulness of Glamour.<br /> <br /> I got hold of this in the early Summer, just after graduating from high school and I had it when my brother and I went on holidays surfing. I read the Lord of the Rings this Summer before coming back in August.<br /> <br /> And lo and behold! The book had arrived (yes, in those times, in the far-flung 90s, you had to wait for your retail store to order a book and you had to wait for group orders, so it took time, unlike today when you order anything just as it comes out).<br /> <br /> I ran soon enough my first story from the book, &quot;Toys will be toys&quot; and then I embarked on the Immortal Eyes trilogy of novels (I read the first one in my bus trips to and from the university, I actually took on liking these bus trips because I could read this book).<br /> <br /> Good days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T14:07:41-07:00","id":237299,"title":"","content":"It would be really nice if they could get Chris Howard back. His writing was always a wonderful blend of the mythic and the modern. I don't know if he'll come back though. He seemed to withdraw pretty heavily when they didn't do the digital release of Book of Glamour.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I'd love to see as much of the old band back together again as possible along with the new writers who are chomping at the bit to put their mark on Changeling!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T23:14:27-07:00","id":237933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=222319#post222319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea World of Darkness/World of Rage book for Changeling is fantastic! Only a very small portion of the world ever got covered in Changeling's original run. It would be great to see what kithain affairs are like in South America, Africa, the rest of Europe, and Asia. It could be called something like A World of Dream and Nightmare.<br /> <br /> Actually, thinking about it, I wouldn't mind seeing the concept of Concordia expanded. Instead of just being the High King of the United States, have it be the High King of all Faerie. Concordia would be a kingdom nominally composed of all the faerie kingdoms. It would be a good parallel to the Camarilla, the Garou Nation, and the Traditions Council. And must like the others, there would be parts of the world firmly under Concordia, areas that pay lip service, areas in open rebellion, and places that just ignore Concordia altogether. The Parliament of Dreams would be a truly grand thing! The House of Lords would be comprised of rulers or their representatives from across the planet. The House of Commons would be a raucous assembly of elected representatives from all sorts of opposed cultures. It would also justify why the Shadow Court is so intent on the destruction of Concordia. It wouldn't just be North America at stake. It would be an opportunity to impose the Fomorian Dream on the whole world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this idea of Concordia being for all the fae of Earth.<br /> <br /> And before the Changeling line got cancelled, there was a World of Dreams book on the pipelines. I even wrote the chapter on France/ Neustria though it was yet unapproved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T23:35:34-07:00","id":237951,"title":"","content":"It's nice to see some familiar faces again. I'm not sure if both of you remember me, PookaKnight, Mattboggan, but it has been ages and I have to say, I am quite happy to see all of you around here. Let's hope CD20 is, at least, as half as good as it is in our dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T23:56:30-07:00","id":237962,"title":"","content":"Of course, I remember you, Mr. Fomorian! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Have you continued your work on this?<br /> <br /> Btw, what happened to Shadownessence? Last time I tried to reach the forums, I couldn't. I don't know why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T23:58:09-07:00","id":237966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=233107#post233107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter does kinda rely on the shadow of the other lines despite being vague about it. If you are familiar with any of the other lines, you'll easily catch blatant references to objects, books, and characters. Such as Dr. Anton Stark having NPC stats in Hunter: First Contact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you be so kind as to post these stats on the forum (maybe in another thread), please? I have long wondered what Stark's traits would look like, especially his Dauntain powers (he's a Dautain, right? or maybe just a &quot;regular&quot; Autumn People). Well, I would really appreciate it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T00:11:29-07:00","id":237980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=146575#post146575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second... Can we get a few more Arts, or some variety on what's there? Maybe even a few kith-specific arts (yes, we have Chronos, Infusion, and... and... urk, hurp, Talecraft). It was always a little bewildering that the supposedly most magical of the WoD's inhabitants... actually get the least variety in their magic. Much of the variety that is there is behind locked doors (These arts are for Nobles only. These Arts are Shadow Court only. These arts are mer only, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The flexibility in C:tD comes from the different options that you can get out of the combination of Art + Realm (and even multiple Realms, and let's not talk about Fae 5).<br /> <br /> In BoG, Chris (Howard) had written a introductory section to the Arts and Realms chapter about how they can be paired with much more flexibility that was up until then thought possible. One of the guidelines he gave me when I designed the boggan Art was that each level of the Art should be playable with each Realm.<br /> <br /> Of course, some Arts are designed to be paired with Actor and/ or Fae and that is fine because, most of the time, these Arts are wonderfully flexible in their own right (I'm thinking about Chicanery and Sovereign here). For instance, I recently watched Maleficent and had fun finding out her Traits in Changeling. In the film, Maleficent often used a sleep spell. I wondered: &quot;Hey, this is classical fairy-tale stuff and I wouldn't know how to do it in Changeling&quot; and my wife -- who plays Changeling with me -- said: &quot;easy, it's a Dictum. Sleep!&quot; And I realized that she exactly hit it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T00:27:26-07:00","id":237997,"title":"","content":"I perused this thread and often see people complaining about how childish Changeling supposedly is.<br /> <br /> One of the biggest misconceptions about the games in the cWoD lies in this assumption. It comes from the confusion between tone/ aesthetics and maturity. Yes, Vampire is &quot;dark,&quot; aesthetically speaking. But in now way can you relate to a vampire from V:tM. These are alien, blood-drinking creatures driven by their Beast. And this is why I would argue that V:tM is the most fun because the less mature of the games. You play one of these inhuman creatures, for Dana's sake! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In Changeling, the issues and themes are deeply relevant to our everyday life. It's about what it means to grow old, to face everyday dreariness and to try to keep your sense of wonder from falling under cynicism and despair. In the 1st edition book, the prologue was called &quot;Never, never grow up&quot; and the author wrote about how changelings were embodiments of people who played RPGs. Gamers try to find fun and recreation in games of imagination; changelings must do it, because this is what they are. Now, you have to try to play one of these guys.<br /> <br /> Actually, if you think really about this, you may find out that Changeling is the most mature game of all.<br /> <br /> So it doesn't need to be &quot;dark&quot; aesthetically. It is dark enough. And since it's set in the gothic-punk environment of the WoD it shares the dark aesthetics of the other games. Just describe a mental hospital to Changeling characters with that (and Terry Gilliam's films like Brazil, Fisher King and Twelve Monkeys) in mind... To the contrary, the focus is -- rightly so -- on the fantasy elements of the game. However, what I find difficult to do, as a storyteller, and I think what most people find difficult to do is how to set these fantasy elements in an &quot;urban&quot; setting in order to produce urban fantasy. This is what the storytelling section of the book should focus on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T01:50:42-07:00","id":238038,"title":"","content":"Hey, Mr. Fomorian, that is nice... After the fall of Shadownessence, for a while I kept in touch with Thomas Milare and his wonderfully talented wife, and also with LostSoul, who helped me so much with the Fomorian project... Concerning Thomas, I'm still in touch with him through Facebook.<br /> <br /> I had a couple of truly bad years; roleplaying become something secondary for me. The Fomorian Project stopped growing, at least in written form; nevertheless, I use it nowadays in my C:tD games, and all my players love it, but I don't really know if I would have the energy and drive to finish it in a printable form, the way you were able to do Kithbook: Boggan.<br /> <br /> I have been able to integrate all the ideas a lot of wonderful people poured into the Fomorian Project into my C:tD games, and I will always be in their debt. In fact, I would like -someday- to offer them some kind of gesture, some kind of monument to their ingenuity, creativity and wit... The wonderfully talented Melissa Uran even sent me some free art for the Fomorian Project, and they are some of the most treasured computer files I keep in my hard drives.<br /> <br /> I was also in touch, for some months, with Chris Howard (at least, I think he was Chris Howard) concerning Book of Glamour. I even sent him revised versions of the Arts I had invented for the Fomorian Project (Maoin, Dolum, Soulcraft and Necrotics) and there was some talk about including them in the Book.<br /> <br /> Then he disappeared, I fell into really hard times, and that is the last I heard from him. I heard something about him burning all his books (or was it someone else?), including the manuscripts for Keys to the Kingdom and Book of Glamour.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if I am mistaken, it all happened a real long time ago for me. They were very difficult years for me and maybe my memory is not as good as I would like it to be.<br /> <br /> All in all, it is good to read you again, Mattboggan. Another good thing brought by the upcoming Changeling: the Dreaming 20th anniversary edition.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 08-23-2014, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T05:10:59-07:00","id":238093,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry to hear that you went through such difficult times. You seem to be out of these hard times, though, and for that I'm glad.<br /> <br /> Chris didn't burn his books, not that I know of, but yes, he distanced himself from games and from WW but mainly for personal reasons.<br /> <br /> As for me, I went on my life, devoting time to my family and to my job as a teacher and researcher of history. But, yes, you're right, C20 is bringing forth a surge of Glamour for all of us, grumps.<br /> <br /> I didn't know that Shadownessence fell. What happened?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T07:23:08-07:00","id":238175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, if you think really about this, you may find out that Changeling is the most mature game of all. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but isn't Dreaming about basically escapism?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T07:35:02-07:00","id":238179,"title":"","content":"MattBoggan: I am not sure. I think they are on-line again, but I don't know. Oh, I am also a teacher. It is nice to find another colleague who loves C:tD. I even managed to get a book published (an anthology of science-fiction stories)<br /> <br /> Katsura: No, it is not. C:tD is about the death of creativity, fantasy and imagination, and the struggle to stop that from happening or, at least, to make it as painless as possible. At least, that has always been one of its main themes for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T09:18:48-07:00","id":238252,"title":"","content":"The Dreaming is both a realm, the collective unconscious of humanity, if you will, and it designates all those who live in the enchanted world, all those who participate in the creation of Glamour.<br /> <br /> And Glamour isn't about escapism. Sidhe believe that, but sidhe are often wrong, though they are loathe to admit it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T10:02:35-07:00","id":238296,"title":"","content":"Oh, Matt, I forgot to tell you how much I use KB: Boggan in my games. It is a very good resource, worthy of having been published by WW itself. Also, how I use Boggans around the &quot;Fomorians&quot; I wrote up in the Fomorian Project... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This is totally embarrassing but, as PookaKnight has gently reminded me, it looks like I was totally mistaken about the authorship of KB: Boggan. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":3586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","user":"Alqamar Alaswad","date":". 08-23-2014, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T10:51:57-07:00","id":238344,"title":"","content":"Thaddeus Papke, aka Gatharion on the old Changeling forums, was the primary author on the fan KB: Boggans that's linked in my sig <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T10:57:01-07:00","id":238346,"title":"","content":"Oops... I told you, my memory of those good old days is not as good as it should be... Woah... I really was thinking it had been written by Mattboggan. Games our mind plays with us, I guess... Thanks, PookaKnight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T11:42:15-07:00","id":238398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=237966#post237966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you be so kind as to post these stats on the forum (maybe in another thread), please? I have long wondered what Stark's traits would look like, especially his Dauntain powers (he's a Dautain, right? or maybe just a &quot;regular&quot; Autumn People). Well, I would really appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's listed as Sample Dauntain in the book along with another Dauntain NPC: Martain Chambers. Basic stats have him at Glamour: 4, Banality: 9, and Willpower: 7. Any special powers/charms/etc. have been renamed to what the Hunter setting calls them instead (<i>List of powers can be found in the Hunter Corebook, Storytellers Handbook, and Storytellers Companion for Changelings or what Hunter calls them: Goblins or Nightmares</i>). His &quot;spells&quot; are: Ban, Enslave, Forget, Go Seek.<br /> The other book that talks about Changelings is Hunter: Urban Legends. In that, a Hunter comes across a Unseelie Satyr and has no idea what it is (<i>Thinks it's a Werewolf at first</i>). The section on rules has a Old Grandma (<i>Nightmare</i>) NPC.<br /> Hunters Survival Guide has a little bit on Changelings, but not much (<i>Hunter's 'around the world' book</i>).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T00:35:35-07:00","id":238931,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I really appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T17:49:41-07:00","id":239728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=230620#post230620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's word from Onyx Path's Twitter! &quot;The word is 'yes.'&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/TheOnyxPath/status/500771973018824705\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/TheOnyxPath/stat...71973018824705</a><br /> <br /> Edit to add: Let's celebrate!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FWXoCXMo_IM&amp;list=UUBtAtYzuzBIHvfBwOQqJm-g\" data-code=\"FWXoCXMo_IM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/FWXoCXMo_IM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Off the boards for a week and look what I miss. YAY! so excited. I was jazzed when you first posted that PookaKnight but didn't wanna get my hopes up too high. Now I'm spazzing out because it finally looks like its got the green light.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path, do I really have to post <a href=\"http://9to5google.files.wordpress.com/2012/04/1520931-take_my_money_super-500x313.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">THIS</a><br /> <br /> Yeah.. Do it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T17:59:19-07:00","id":239738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=237299#post237299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be really nice if they could get Chris Howard back. His writing was always a wonderful blend of the mythic and the modern. I don't know if he'll come back though. He seemed to withdraw pretty heavily when they didn't do the digital release of Book of Glamour.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I'd love to see as much of the old band back together again as possible along with the new writers who are chomping at the bit to put their mark on Changeling!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any idea what number of new writers might be working on this? Are you one of them? I'm wondering for the context because I'd like to get in on writing for this book too, but it sounds like OPP's writers call out is asking for Sections of writing. I guess what I'm asking is how do we know if there's already 12 writers trying to submit their Glamour or Arts writing and if no one is working on writing for Changeling history? Is there any way to find out? I guess I could Email Rich T, but I feel like I would be either bothering him with stuff that's unknown at this time or my email would just get lost in all the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:06:12-07:00","id":239749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mattboggan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=237997#post237997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I perused this thread and often see people complaining about how childish Changeling supposedly is.<br /> <br /> One of the biggest misconceptions about the games in the cWoD lies in this assumption. It comes from the confusion between tone/ aesthetics and maturity. Yes, Vampire is &quot;dark,&quot; aesthetically speaking. But in now way can you relate to a vampire from V:tM. These are alien, blood-drinking creatures driven by their Beast. And this is why I would argue that V:tM is the most fun because the less mature of the games. You play one of these inhuman creatures, for Dana's sake! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In Changeling, the issues and themes are deeply relevant to our everyday life. It's about what it means to grow old, to face everyday dreariness and to try to keep your sense of wonder from falling under cynicism and despair. In the 1st edition book, the prologue was called &quot;Never, never grow up&quot; and the author wrote about how changelings were embodiments of people who played RPGs. Gamers try to find fun and recreation in games of imagination; changelings must do it, because this is what they are. Now, you have to try to play one of these guys.<br /> <br /> Actually, if you think really about this, you may find out that Changeling is the most mature game of all.<br /> <br /> So it doesn't need to be &quot;dark&quot; aesthetically. It is dark enough. And since it's set in the gothic-punk environment of the WoD it shares the dark aesthetics of the other games. Just describe a mental hospital to Changeling characters with that (and Terry Gilliam's films like Brazil, Fisher King and Twelve Monkeys) in mind... To the contrary, the focus is -- rightly so -- on the fantasy elements of the game. However, what I find difficult to do, as a storyteller, and I think what most people find difficult to do is how to set these fantasy elements in an &quot;urban&quot; setting in order to produce urban fantasy. This is what the storytelling section of the book should focus on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with all of this and more. I often wonder just what is is about Changeling that gives people the impression that Changeling is all silly rainbows when actually very little in the books is rose-colored glasses. I think maybe it's an unconscious association given that the system previous to this was Wraith: the Oblivion core book AKA &quot;The Big Gray Book of Depression&quot;, and along comes Changeling in full bright (sometimes eye stabby) color and apparently it's about Faeries, so without even <i>reading</i> it, people get the contrast impression that it must be the opposite extreme of Wraith and therefore happy shiny even though it's still set in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> *Shrugs* Just my ponderings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:08:33-07:00","id":239753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=238175#post238175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, but isn't Dreaming about basically escapism?</div> </div> </div> </div>All games are about escapism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:16:08-07:00","id":239762,"title":"","content":"Questions for PookaKnight, Mattboggan and Alqamar Alaswad, if you guys know that is.<br /> <br /> Just how many people were writing for Changeling on projects that never got finished? Any idea? I'm hearing more and more from different people who &quot;knew someone&quot; who was working on written work for Changeling and then for whatever reason (Changeling put on hold, called off to war etc) they never got to finish. A roomie of mine knew someone and was actually with them gathering history and background info to make a Changeling book for Seattle, but was called in to service before he got half way. There is a remote chance of getting back in touch with him still and a lot of these old works I'm hearing about sound like they could be resurrected and updated. Do you guys think that would help or hinder the amount of material that could be submitted for a C20 book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:35:56-07:00","id":239776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=239762#post239762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A roomie of mine knew someone and was actually with them gathering history and background info to make a Changeling book for Seattle, but was called in to service before he got half way. There is a remote chance of getting back in touch with him still and a lot of these old works I'm hearing about sound like they could be resurrected and updated. Do you guys think that would help or hinder the amount of material that could be submitted for a C20 book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know of someone from the Rage CCG forums that was doing work for the Dark Ages: Italy book before it got canned.<br /> Seeing as it was brought up in the discussion a bit before, probably the info/research on Seattle could go into the big Changeling's 20th Around the World book idea.<br /> Would love a section on NorCal, Oregon, and Washington just for a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gravity_Falls\" target=\"_blank\">Gravity Falls</a>-ish atmosphere for Changeling.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.giveneyestosee.com/changeling/lostbooks.html\" target=\"_blank\">This old site, Changeling: the Dreaming Resource,</a><a href=\"http://www.giveneyestosee.com/changeling/lostbooks.html\" target=\"_blank\"> has info on the writers for the lost books</a>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:50:44-07:00","id":239783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=239738#post239738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there any idea what number of new writers might be working on this? Are you one of them? I'm wondering for the context because I'd like to get in on writing for this book too, but it sounds like OPP's writers call out is asking for Sections of writing. I guess what I'm asking is how do we know if there's already 12 writers trying to submit their Glamour or Arts writing and if no one is working on writing for Changeling history? Is there any way to find out? I guess I could Email Rich T, but I feel like I would be either bothering him with stuff that's unknown at this time or my email would just get lost in all the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is basically all that was said at the Gen Con &quot;What's Up with Classic World of Darkness Q&amp;A&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/aL9D2_pGucY?t=25m31s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/aL9D2_pGucY?t=25m31s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/aL9D2_pGucY?t=25m31s\" target=\"_blank\"> http://youtu.be/aL9D2_pGucY?t=25m31s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;...probably in the Fall of next year (2015)... ...next year we'll be doing Changeling: the Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition. We're all very excited about it. I think you're all going to LOVE this new idea we have for these collectible cantrip cards...&quot; [joking, but realization that they can be done through DriveThruCards.com]. &quot;If we do it, it would be an add-on and not anything you had to have in order to play the game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/aL9D2_pGucY?t=40m24s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/aL9D2_pGucY?t=40m24s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/aL9D2_pGucY?t=40m24s\" target=\"_blank\"> http://youtu.be/aL9D2_pGucY?t=40m24s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Question: &quot;Are you in a place to anounce the developer for Changeling 20th?&quot;<br /> Richard Thomas: &quot;I am not. It's a bunch of people who've expressed interest, and there's some actual discussion about the person having more of a development team because different people are coming into it with different perspectives and... and experiences.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:55:32-07:00","id":239785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=239762#post239762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just how many people were writing for Changeling on projects that never got finished?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends. There were two unreleased books officially on the release schedule at the time Changeling got put on hiatus - Keys to the Kingdom and Book of Glamour.<br /> <br /> KB: Boggans was an unannounced book that everyone was certain was being planned. Given how far in advance books had to be started in order to meet their release date on the old supplement treadmill, there were probably a few other books in the early stages that were never announced publicly. Mattboggan's World of Dreams would fall under that category. The only people who would know the complete list of those would be Nicky Rae, Jackie Cassada, and who ever was over Arthaus at the time.<br /> <br /> There are a whole lot of fan books that got started shortly after the game got put on hiatus. Most of those never went anywhere. A few got significant progress, but were never completed like Alqamar's Formorian book. The only one I know of that got finished was KB: Boggans.<br /> <br /> Your friend's Seattle book is almost certainly a fan book. Location source books were (and still are) terrible sellers. Changeling did marginal sales back in the day, which is why it got moved to Arthaus. As I understood it under Arthaus, books didn't need to sell as many copies to be a success, but if a book sold particularly poorly, it was pretty much the death of the line. I have no insider information, so I don't know if that's what happened to Changeling, Wild West, Sorcerer's Crusade or not. I would be willing to bet, though, that they never would have wasted a book slot on something that was guaranteed to sell dismally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 08-24-2014, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T19:12:05-07:00","id":239789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=239738#post239738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any idea what number of new writers might be working on this? Are you one of them? I'm wondering for the context because I'd like to get in on writing for this book too, but it sounds like OPP's writers call out is asking for Sections of writing. I guess what I'm asking is how do we know if there's already 12 writers trying to submit their Glamour or Arts writing and if no one is working on writing for Changeling history? Is there any way to find out? I guess I could Email Rich T, but I feel like I would be either bothering him with stuff that's unknown at this time or my email would just get lost in all the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add a bit to what Torakhan said about this, the writing sample is just a sample. Whatever you submit almost certainly wouldn't be used in a book even if you do get asked to write for Onyx Path. The exact process varies from developer to developer and team to team. For the most part, a developer will contact writers who he or she thinks would do the best for a particular section. For new writers discovered through the all call, my guess would be the developer would try them out in a small section first to see the person's quality and reliability before giving them larger assignments.<br /> <br /> I did send in a writing sample for Changeling. I have no idea if anything will come of it, and it's far too early to expect any sort of word either way yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T22:03:51-07:00","id":239916,"title":"","content":"Thank you <b>Torakhan</b> and <b>PookaKnight</b> for your replies. That does give me a better idea of where things lie in terms of writers. I apologize if I might come off as impatient or nosy to some.<br /> <br /> This is something I really believe in as a project and I'd really like to contribute in some way beyond throwing loads of cash at it for funding. My dream job is actually in movie production both Pre Production story boarding and Post Production editing, (and heck why not some costuming for production itself.) So in my spare time I've been familiarizing myself with courses and speaking to a lot of people in various unions who've worked on movies in some capacity or another. There's so many different jobs it's overwhelming, but every movie starts out as a project outline of some sort and from what I'm told of others' experience it can take up to a year of just brainstorming on a whiteboard, hashing out script draft after script draft and doodling hundreds of storyboard panels before the project moves forward into finalization of one idea before talk of filming and casting even begins. So even though it's a year away, the planning skills I've picked up are <u><i>Screaming</i></u> at me to find out what the state of the C20 project is right now. OPP most likely doesn't work on their projects in the same way that movie studios do I'm sure, but the amount of preparation before hand is probably very similar and just as important. It might be too early for anyone from OPP to focus on it, I'm sure it must be a madhouse of all kinds of projects and deadlines to focus on for them, but to me, it's never too early to start discovering the resources at hand.<br /> <br /> Another reason for my questions, being I am still brainstorming with friends the possibility to start up a fan resource page involving cities and areas that can be used in the World of Darkness. (Thank you VERY much <b>Laughing Hyena</b> for that link. You're awesome.) Not just for fan made Caerns or Necropoli, but for all systems and I don't want to step on anyone's toes if there's going to be resources like that already in the works for future releases from OPP. Once I have more of a backbone of contributors for such a project, then I would be emailing Rich about it, but first I wanted to make sure that I haven't missed any information that would conflict with a fan based project. Thank you all for answering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T00:34:56-07:00","id":239987,"title":"","content":"It would have been nice to have worked in Book of Glamour. I guess it will never happen now, of course. Maybe I should send some samples to Onyx Path. Ummm...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T01:16:19-07:00","id":240014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=239987#post239987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would have been nice to have worked in Book of Glamour. I guess it will never happen now, of course. Maybe I should send some samples to Onyx Path. Ummm...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I don't know about that. I think in a C20 there could be room for a section that condenses what would have been in the Book of Glamour and can then be put into the C20 book. Or take a page from the Mage kickstarter. There was so much extra material that will be coming out in PDF form now because backers were willing to put in the money for it. Or even the Penny Dreadful fiction. That existed for years as only a PDF and because it was a stretch goal it's now going to be available in Print on Demand. If the material is sound, I don't see any reason why Book of Glamour as well as other unfinished works can't be offered to OPP for upgrade to whatever revisements they put into C20 and be added to the system core book or as a PDF stretch goal edition/addition. All we have to so is show OPP how much there is a demand for it. Maybe someone can put up a Forum poll? I dunno if we can do that here or if only moderators can do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T03:45:49-07:00","id":240097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All games are about escapism. </div> </div> </div>I mean, I see one of original motives of OChangeling that &quot;growing up&quot; is not exactly good thing as a form of escapism and rejection of the world we live in. I would not say I'm most mature person (I'm eccentric, I will admit), but for one I don't see a progression to more adult and grounded behavior as something negative. But that's opinion. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T04:15:31-07:00","id":240114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=240097#post240097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I see one of original motives of OChangeling that &quot;growing up&quot; is not exactly good thing as a form of escapism and rejection of the world we live in. I would not say I'm most mature person (I'm eccentric, I will admit), but for one I don't see a progression to more adult and grounded behavior as something negative. But that's opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your definition of 'growing up' The definition is subjective. If &quot;growing up&quot; means not only do you put away childish things as the saying goes, but you also stop laughing in delight or having any kind of wonder or joy in your life and it's all seriousness with a 9-5 job, stress and conforming to expectations, then yeah.. that is bad. That's what banality is. Some people choose to live that way and they like it. Good for them. That doesn't mean all of us have to live that way. In the real world or in a game. That's what Changeling is about. Not that they are trying to reject the world we live in, but reject the idea that it has to be dull, boring and serious all the time because it's the &quot;grown up&quot; ideal that everyone has to be. Changeling basically makes it ok for people to be eccentric without being called crazy and put in the nut house or given medication to make them robotic zombies who don't do anything outside society's expectations. If you've ever seen the movie Equilibrium, that's a really good example of the kind of thing Changelings are dreading will happen and that's what they are fighting against. Adult and grounded behavior is all well and good, as long as you can remember how to have fun, be silly and laugh at yourself once in a while. All in moderation.<br /> <br /> And maybe this should be a separate discussion and not in this thread. I hope this answers your questions though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T11:13:56-07:00","id":240429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=239762#post239762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just how many people were writing for Changeling on projects that never got finished? Any idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>I worked on <b>Book of Glamour</b> with Daniel Ginn, Tadd McDivitt, and Christopher Howard.<br /> <br /> Christopher Howard and Carla Hollar was assigned to <b>Keys to the Kingdom</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Kithbook: Boggan </b>was also assigned to Christopher Howard, but I don't know if anything was actually written before the cancellation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":2494,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","user":"Rigistrade","date":". 08-25-2014, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T12:11:52-07:00","id":240480,"title":"","content":"I will just say that for the sake of C20, DO NOT get Phil Brucato any near the project. The author of Freak Legions and NWoD Changing Breeds will only give Vietnam flashbacks from sheer number of stuff in &quot;Dude, not funny&quot; territory. Both crunch and fluff will suffer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T12:51:14-07:00","id":240520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=240480#post240480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will just say that for the sake of C20, DO NOT get Phil Brucato any near the project. The author of Freak Legions and NWoD Changing Breeds will only give Vietnam flashbacks from sheer number of stuff in &quot;Dude, not funny&quot; territory. Both crunch and fluff will suffer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going to sadly slightly agree there (<i>See my user name for why</i>.<i> I used to check out and read Innocent Killers by Jane Goodall all the time during my high school years</i>). Phil worked on both Bastet and NWOD Changing Breeds and just...<br /> I can only imagine what would happen to Hyena Pooka.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T13:15:12-07:00","id":240603,"title":"","content":"He was also involved in Kithbook: Satyr, for what that\u2019s worth. And then there\u2019s Deliria. <br /> <br /> Overall, I\u2019d be quite content with letting the M20 line consume all of his time, and letting others come to the fore on Changeling. Nothing against him; even if he could do a fantastic job on Changeling, his time is better spent on Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T14:42:07-07:00","id":240758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=240480#post240480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will just say that for the sake of C20, DO NOT get Phil Brucato any near the project. The author of Freak Legions and NWoD Changing Breeds will only give Vietnam flashbacks from sheer number of stuff in &quot;Dude, not funny&quot; territory. Both crunch and fluff will suffer.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far I remember, both Freak Legion and Changing Breeds had a whole lot of other authors involved, not just Brucato. Also, he was the one behind Deliria.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T22:03:31-07:00","id":241074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=240758#post240758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far I remember, both Freak Legion and Changing Breeds had a whole lot of other authors involved, not just Brucato. Also, he was the one behind Deliria.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Freak Legion has little in the way of relevance, yes, but he captained the ship as the developer for nWoD Changing Breeds. There's also the matter of the copy-pasted Bubasti entry from the Bastet breedbook that shows up in the nWoD title, with perhaps a word or two changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T11:43:33-07:00","id":244228,"title":"","content":"First off hi everyone. Been on here for years and years but I really only lurk. So yay for 2nd post ever.<br /> <br /> Anyway back to topic. One of the things I would love to see that hasn't been mentioned multiple times is that science is not banal in and of its self look at all the science fiction genre. Even better if they could include ;most likely as a target add on; but rules or at least guidelines for making those things I mean there are 2 hard core crafting kiths Nockers and boggins as well as house Dugal. But nothing on how to make items except some vague indication of a craft roll. In the nocker kith book it mentions having to get chimerical ingredients from the dreaming but that's about it. <br /> <br /> It would also be intresting to have for lack of a better work updated setting. I read a post somewhere a while back about mage 20th and how in the now current society the average joe dosent know or for some even care how the comptuter works just so long as it does. So how that new mind set could mess with the technocrats.( If anyone knows what post I am referring to please give me a heads up so I can quote and give credit where it's due) I think it would be intresting to see that reflected some in CtD. A good example is my mom she has no clue how the computer works and when ever it has issues she blames it on computer pixies. Now I know the wod is not our world and a much darker reflection of it but it is an intresting thought. Like Nockers and more sciencevery minded boggins gaining access to the dreaming via the Web and so on and so forth. I'd also like to see a bit more concerning humans are not the only things that dream as well as produce glamour and effect the dreaming, just perhaps the most potent<br /> <br /> I, like quite a few people would like to see the glamour system smoothed out some. but I always thought it worked well and was scary versatile. But as I have never played mage I could be biased. <br /> <br /> I do agree that I would like to see more of the juxtaposition in the art a good example of one I've always liked is the splash page for the wilder section of the core rule book. The punky decked out in plaid satyr with the cig. As well as a more of a level/ equal quality to the art. Though I loved the varied styles there were some that were like &quot;wait is this the same book / does the artist even know what they were commissioned for&quot; feel to them if that makes sense. <br /> <br /> Please excuse any typos and auto-in-correts as I am writing from my phone as my computer when about as FUBAR as an angry nocker could make it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1287-nukuchan","name":"Nukuchan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T22:03:14-07:00","id":271394,"title":"","content":"There's so much that can be added to. Nunnehi and their freeholds (I've been running them a bit like a cross between freeholds and caerns). Magical steeds (I did a whole write-up on Changeling animals, because they're mentioned in Rage Across Appalachia only briefly). A good Realms overhaul. Actually showing people that Piskies are Commoners. I've long loved Changeling, and have written and tinkered with a lot for it because it sadly never got the revisions it needed. I'd love to see this happen.<br /> <br /> Giving the Nunnehi some Crafters, and perhaps the Mer and others, would also be nice, I think, as well as finally taking a look at some African and Central and South American Changelings; I never bought the whole &quot;The Amazon is a realm of Banality&quot; argument. As it is, I don't buy that PLACES are Banal. People are banal. Disbelief is banal. Places shouldn't be, I feel. There is a real chance here to expand and explore that I'd relish assisting in even, if possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","user":"Windthin","date":". 10-03-2014, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T03:17:34-07:00","id":271514,"title":"","content":"I think Changeling20 should get a &quot;Book of Gallain&quot; like the Changing Breeds for W20. With all the non-Kithain changelings fully explained.<br /> And I still dream with &quot;Keys to the Kingdom&quot; now it could be an entire world atlas for all the changeling realms and kingdoms in the mundy world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/n6g3njp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/kpa5GS5Mp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/93820aaad7.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/584-eliseo-ap-liam","name":"Eliseo ap Liam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T11:43:31-07:00","id":272423,"title":"","content":"Darling Rose suggested a historical setting and a historian character. Even wrote up a semi-stable timeline for that suggestion along with a theory why all of Changeling history always referred to the medieval setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T20:20:43-08:00","id":341492,"title":"","content":"Giving this a bump. As someone who is actively running a Changeling LARP, I am very interested in seeing this project take off. I even sent in a writing sample with the hope I could write for it. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T13:36:43-08:00","id":344079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obyrne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=78529#post78529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It varies. Kindred are nearly all awful for Changelings - most of them are unchanging and cold/calculating. They're basically the embodiment of Banality (which shreds Lings).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Changelings have groups in each of the games with which they could work well. Mage offers very unique interactions for Changlings - especially with the Cult of Ecstasy, Verbena, and OMG the Marauders... Vampires of the more creative side, such as Toreador, Tzimisce, and the Daughters of Cacophony, could work very well - especially for Dark Court. Werewolves should have no trouble integrating the servants of the Wyld into a positive framework. Wraith would be slightly more difficult - but the Keeners are an expression of Changeling values. I have no trouble with the Sluagh holding a seance for their personal kind of reverie. Then there is the Urmen - for those of you who remember the five seeds linking everything together as one - How much more Changeling can one get that that? I would like a little better tie in with the other games in a new Changeling - but it is not like the warp and weft are not prepared.<br /> <br /> The game to me always had an incredible dynamic to work on: How does one balance Subversion of Self for the needs of Society while keeping the Expression of Self for the needs of Self-Actualization. The balance point is the Changeling version of Golconda. While Changeling has the 'highlight of the party' image - that is a very dark and dangerous party. The problem with Creative Wisdom is that exposure to it is brief, blinding, universe changing, and ephemeral. The instant in which the entire possibility of the universe is exposed and immediately fades because it is too great to be comprehensible. The Dream is both inspiring and the narcotic which the junkie can never have again. For vampires Golconda is a desired convenience and relief from the world. For Changeling that balance is the sanity that makes expression in the world both possible and effective in the manner that endures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T23:18:39-08:00","id":344427,"title":"","content":"I've always found Banality based on splat increadibly silly. I mean OCD Malkavian is closer to the Dreaming than an Etherite who's hunted Tyranosaurs in the Hollow Earth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T18:41:39-08:00","id":429575,"title":"","content":"Things I'd love to see:<br /> <br /> Kithbook: Boggan<br /> Kithbook: Piskie (they ARE a normal Commoner Kith, after all, even if not in the core book)<br /> An in-depth look at Nunnehi Freeholds (and Freeholds in general)<br /> An in-depth look at Nunnehi, including Central and South America<br /> A look at Gallain and other Changelings in Africa and other places<br /> Another look at Fae animals (steeds and hounds are mentioned in the Appalachia book, but I think that so much MORE could be done with it)<br /> The Korred from the French book brought into the main stream<br /> A look at the Inanimae mentioned under House Varich<br /> A look at the Nymphs mentioned in some books<br /> A complete re-structuring of Actor and Nature to make more sense and be more usable.<br /> Another look at how chimera and treasures work.<br /> A re-design of the silly &quot;by the time you hit 30 you're so jaded you can't possibly believe in magic&quot; dynamic. Expanding the range of Grump and Wilder would really work better.<br /> A better look at Legacies and Courts. The book often states that Seelie isn't good and Unseelie isn't evil, but then does so much to undermine that, such as having pretty much exclusively negative, horrible Legacies available for the Unseelie and having Thallain, who have TWO Unseelie Legacies, just to show how extra-special evil they are. I think focusing more on &quot;Law and Order&quot; vs &quot;Freedom and Chaos&quot; would work far better. Seelie can be just as nasty as Unseelie, and Unseelie can be heroic (there are even a few heroic Unseelie mentioned in books!)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T18:44:28-08:00","id":429578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=79235#post79235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know anything about Changeling, being a vampire guy, but it's hard for me to square a supernatural existence with the concept of banality. I understand what you mean by vampires being unchanging, but the older a vampire gets the more powerful their disciplines, the more blood magic they learn, the more crazy occult shit they see...their world view and understanding of what's possible should be much more expansive than a mortal man's.<br /> <br /> I mean, the embrace all by itself should break down a lot of mental barriers. If vampires are real and I'm one of them, then anything is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea isn't so much that vampires are unmagical but forces of stasis. It's their static nature that somehow makes them more Banal... which of course doesn't necessarily make sense in the face of Changelings who also can have extended lives. So, yeah, Banality requires a good looking-at. Another thing I like to point out is that places are not Banal, people are. A place may feel worse because of the people in it, but a place itself, I feel, should never be Banal, as Banality is all about belief. However, it is true that many Vampires are forces of stasis, enforcing a status quo and actively undermining change and belief in magic via the Masquerade. Interesting ideas there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:11:05-08:00","id":430143,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I would love to see a reworking of the mechanics of Glamour and Banality such that they both had ups and downs, and the latter could be used as more than a poison pill to resist Cantrips. Banality would strengthen the mortal half and keep the Changeling &quot;sane&quot; in a mortal sense (and from the perspective of most Changelings, who do have to deal with the real world). Glamour keeps them from forgetting who and what they are. Echoes, rather than a flaw, should be something that they can exploit to gain and preserve Glamour and avoid or shed Banality, while Banality protects against their limitations.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see a serious look taken at how Glamour is gained in general, because I like the <i>concept</i> behind Ravaging and Reverie, but they were impractical for how long they took (especially Reverie) vs. how much Glamour they returned vs. how much Glamour it cost to do...anything. Pools were too small to regenerate so slowly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:12:27-08:00","id":430162,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping the Adhene get some love. I didn't discover C:tD until about the time Kingdom of Willows came out and I think the game went on permanent hiatus shortly thereafter, and I didn't read the Denizens book until much much later when old World of Darkness books starting showing up on DTRP. I lament never getting the opportunity to play a fir-bholg prince during the heyday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thread Reaper <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">\uff1c(\u00b4 \u055e)\u0a0a( \u055e )\uff1e\ufeff</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/377-xanandithras","name":"Xanandithras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar377_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-16T19:38:46-08:00","id":787785,"title":"","content":"Love many of these ideas and hope they're seen (hence the necro). However, I'd hate Concordia to be international for the simple reason it'd make the game even more US-centric. I also doubt very much that nobles from Europe, who've had kingdoms for millennia, would submit to the rule of a nation that only recently (in immortal terms) came about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T02:57:47-08:00","id":788636,"title":"","content":"So I've been moving away from physical roleplaying books altogether. Is there no way to get the new Freeholds pdf as an add on if we are at a pdf rather than a hardcopy reward tier for the 20th Anniversary core?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T04:45:36-08:00","id":788667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=787785#post787785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Love many of these ideas and hope they're seen (hence the necro). However, I'd hate Concordia to be international for the simple reason it'd make the game even more US-centric. I also doubt very much that nobles from Europe, who've had kingdoms for millennia, would submit to the rule of a nation that only recently (in immortal terms) came about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Two things. Kithain in North America Predate European contact. Secondly majority of Nobles left with the Shattering, what was left behind has been redistributed via all sorts of means over the last 800+ years. Add to that the Ressurgence was as much a thing in Europe as America, and things got twisted up again. Now i'd love to see European kingdoms outside Isle of the mighty but they sure as hell don't date back millennia and probably have no more aged legitimacy than any of the Kingdoms of concordia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T08:43:04-08:00","id":788789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=788667#post788667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Two things. Kithain in North America Predate European contact. Secondly majority of Nobles left with the Shattering, what was left behind has been redistributed via all sorts of means over the last 800+ years. Add to that the Ressurgence was as much a thing in Europe as America, and things got twisted up again. Now i'd love to see European kingdoms outside Isle of the mighty but they sure as hell don't date back millennia and probably have no more aged legitimacy than any of the Kingdoms of concordia.</div> </div> </div> </div>The commoners have been there for millennia, reincarnating and ruling themselves. Isle of the Mighty gives a history for the British Isles fae that literally goes back thousands of years. True, the sidhe are relative newcomers (returnees?), although there were Scathach and commoners in positions of power in the meantime.<br /> <br /> But Concordia itself (in its current form, united by High King David) is a relatively modern conception, and feels a very American one (it united one nation under one king). It seems more of a stretch to somehow have an entire world (or even the Western world) united under that one same ruler.<br /> <br /> Also, as a personal note, Changeling always felt like it had a far stronger US bias in the core book than any of the other games. I'd like to see less of that, rather than more.<br /> <br /> Another way to do it, which might be a stronger idea, would be if each nation had its own High King, and each High King met in some sort of international cabinet, sort of like the Camarilla Inner Council.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 12-18-2015, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T09:26:22-08:00","id":788812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=788789#post788789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The commoners have been there for millennia, reincarnating and ruling themselves. Isle of the Mighty gives a history for the British Isles fae that literally goes back thousands of years. True, the sidhe are relative newcomers (returnees?), although there were Scathach and commoners in positions of power in the meantime.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, commoners took the changeling way 800 years ago. If we are going to count fae history in general then North America has fae history dating back to the ice age thanks to the Nunnahei, The kingdoms of isle of the Mighty don't date back centuries. Like everything else they were rewritten by the Ressurgence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another way to do it, which might be a stronger idea, would be if each nation had its own High King, and each High King met in some sort of international cabinet, sort of like the Camarilla Inner Council. </div> </div> </div>Or no council. No symetry. A vague land mass ruled by Kithain calls itself whatever it wants and you deal with it as a such. Perhaps there's an alliance of Smaller kingdoms in reaction to the blatant power play that is Concordia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T10:50:56-08:00","id":788861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/77869-changeling-20th-anniversary?p=788812#post788812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, commoners took the changeling way 800 years ago. If we are going to count fae history in general then North America has fae history dating back to the ice age thanks to the Nunnahei, The kingdoms of isle of the Mighty don't date back centuries. Like everything else they were rewritten by the Ressurgence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or no council. No symetry. A vague land mass ruled by Kithain calls itself whatever it wants and you deal with it as a such. Perhaps there's an alliance of Smaller kingdoms in reaction to the blatant power play that is Concordia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the Nunnehi probably wouldn't consider themselves part of Concordia, though. Concordia always seemed (to me) to be the nation of European kiths in North America, and the Nunnehi have very little to do with that nation, with very few exceptions. They share a landmass, but they go their separate ways.<br /> <br /> I could see Concordia certainly claiming to rule the entire Western world, because the sidhe of any nation are pretty arrogant. <br /> <br /> I get your point about the Changeling Way meaning fae history is somewhat non-contiguous. DA:F also lacks Houses and much of the social structure of CTD, so that also suggests fae history has been rewritten at some point as fae bound themselves to the myths of mere mortals to survive Banality (similar to the retreat of bygones to escape Paradox). <br /> <br /> Either way, though, I still have trouble seeing an American empire of fae ruling the Western world. It just seems implausible, but that's probably my own European bias coming to the fore. :-P <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I would've loved a map of faerie Europe at the back of the book, so that it didn't repeat the same map as at the front and and gave some setting ideas for non-American kingdoms right off the bat. <br /> <br /> A wider scope in the core book would've been great, but part of the problem is that so much of the metaplot revolves around Concordia. <br /> <br /> Hopefully, the inclusion of all the Kithain and Gallain means the core book will now have that breadth in C20. We'll get French kiths, for example, to add to the mainly Celtic kiths we've already got, plus the Nunnehi and Menehune. I'd also like to see more non-European faerie types as kiths in future. Or at least some recognition of more localised variants on the main kiths (Glaistig as Scottish satyrs, trasgu potentially as Boggans or pooka, xana as sidhe or some kind of beautiful river hag).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T19:29:59-07:00","id":1507533,"title":"","content":"Back in the Forums. Sorry about the necroposting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}